	<xs:complexType name="ActionPlanInputsType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PlanInputsCoreType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="PlanningCandidate" type="uci:RequirementPlanningCandidateType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates specific Systems to consider and plan for along with System-specific planning constraints.  If omitted, all Tiers and all Systems at and below those that the planning process is applicable to shall be planned.  A System is a planning "candidate" because its plan may or may not change as a result of the command; zero to one Plans per *Plan type will potentially be created for each candidate.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProposedActionPlan" type="uci:ActionPlanConstraintType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an existing ActionPlan of the System superior to the sibling PlanningCandidates that provides a proposed "Action deck" to allocate amongst the candidates.  This element can be supplemented with additional Actions from the sibling ProposedAction element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProposedAction" type="uci:ActionAllocationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a proposed Action for the planning process.  An Action given here is added to any Actions provided in the sibling ProposedActionPlan to create the full set of Actions to be considered by the planning process.  An Action given here overrides the same Action in the sibling ProposedActionPlan.  An empty list here, combined with no sibling ProposedActionPlan is considered a command to deallocate previously allocated Actions.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AssociationConstraint" type="uci:RequirementAssociationConstraintType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an association between Requirements that is a constraint on how the Actions are allocated and planned.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="OutputPlanParts" type="uci:ActionPlanPartsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates Parts required in the output ActionPlan.  When populated, this element must match or be a subset of the Parts associated with the planning process (sibling PlanningProcessID) as advertised in PlanningFunction*messages.  This element is optional when all Parts of the process are required.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
