		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ActivityID" type="uci:ActivityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability which the Activity is an instance of.  Generally an Activity is an instance of a single Capability.  An Activity can be associated with multiple Capabilities when, for example, a Subsystem has distinct Capabilities for automated and manual.  In this case, if a manual command is issued while an automated Activity that achieves the desired result already exists, a single Activity represents both Capabilities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Interactive" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether or not the Activity can be edited/modified via a [Capability]Command...Activity message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityState" type="uci:ActivityStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current state of the Activity its state machine.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Basis" type="uci:ActivityBasisEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the basis of the Activity.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  If omitted, a basis of ACTUAL should be assumed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityRank" type="uci:ComparableRankingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the rank of the Activity amongst all other Activities of the Capability and/or Subsystem.  This isn't necessarily the same as the Rank associated with the sibling ActivitySource.  This element is meant to convey the Subsystem determined relative ranking of all Activities of a Capability category (ESM, EA, etc.).  For Subsystems with multiple Capability categories this element is meant to convey relative ranking across all Capability categories.  In addition to the rank of the ActivitySource, an Activity's rank can be influenced by Capability priority (see CapabilitySettings), RF_ControlCommands and other factors that influence the Subsystem's internal scheduling and resource allocation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityReason" type="uci:CannotComplyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates details regarding the reason for and/or a contributing factor to the sibling ActivityState element.  This element is only expected when the Activity is in a potentially undesirable state such as constrained, failed or completed with less than optimum results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Source" type="uci:ActivitySourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an originating "source" of the Activity; the command or other item which invoked this specific Activity of a Capability.  A single Activity can fully or partially satisfy Activity sources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedStartTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimated time when the Activity started or is expected to start.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedCompletionTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimated time when the Activity will complete.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPercentComplete" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current estimated percent complete of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityByType" uci:version="000.000.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the "activity" of the Entity. Derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUIs 1798/001, 1798/002, 1798/003, 1798/004 and 1798/005 for additional details. In MIL-STD-6016, activity indexes/values vary by environment and therefore this element is only meaningful when paired with the sibling ActivityCategory element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityAmplification" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates amplifying information for the activity of the Entity. See MIL-STD-6016 DFI 752 DUI 001 for additional details. Each environment has a corresponding set of activity amplifications.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityCategory" type="uci:EnvironmentEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the MIL-STD-6016 list/category of the sibling Activity element. Derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUI 275/004 for additional details. Each environment has a corresponding set of specific types.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CustomActivity" type="uci:ForeignKeyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a custom activity that is supplemental to the sibling Activity element. This element is expected only if a custom activity, which isn't included or fully described by MIL-STD-6016 can be identified. In that case, the sibling Activity Element indicates "no statement" or the closest match and this element completes the activity characterization.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivitySubCategory" type="uci:ActivitySubCategoryEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of track being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityChoiceType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="EffectID" type="uci:EffectID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Effect associated with the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActionID" type="uci:ActionID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Action associated with the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TaskID" type="uci:TaskID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Task associated with the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ResponseID" type="uci:ResponseID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Response associated with the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityCommand" type="uci:CapabilityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability command that is planned to occur.  This is an abstract polymorphic extension point/element; the CapabilityCommandBaseType used here is an abstract base type used in a Capability-specific type that describes the unique Capability command such as EA_Command.  This abstract element must be replaced by a Capability-specific command type to form a valid planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SupportingCapabilityCommand" type="uci:SupportCapabilityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Supporting Capability command that is planned to occur.  This is an abstract polymorphic extension point/element; the SupportCapabilityCommandBaseType used here is an abstract base type used in a Capability-specific type that describes the unique Capability command such as StoreManagementCommand.  This abstract element must be replaced by a Supporting Capability-specific command type to form a valid planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VehicleSettings" type="uci:VehicleCommandDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a planned system/vehicle setting that is generally independent of mission, tasking and kinematic planning from a UCI perspective.  These activities are related to operation of the system/vehicle itself as opposed to a mission Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommAction" type="uci:CommDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates planned/needed communications resources/activities. For example, this could indicate that an EO/IR capability is being used during a kinematic segment and therefore higher bandwidth is needed by the System in order support streaming video.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductTaskID" type="uci:TaskID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a Product management Task (ProductDisseminationTask, ProductProcessingTask, etc.) associated with the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityCommandBaseType" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ActivityID" type="uci:ActivityID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Activity which the sibling changes are commanded to.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeActivityRank" type="uci:ComparableRankingType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change the rank of the Activity.  This is not a means of modifying the rank of the original source of the Activity (Capability Command, Task, etc.).  It is a means of modifying the Subsystem assigned rank of the Activity reported in the associated Activity message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeActivityState" type="uci:CapabilityCommandStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change the state of the Activity.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DeleteActivity" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to delete the Activity.  It is equivalent to a sticky disable command.  A deleted Activity can't be re-enabled, including by an automated Capability that was the original source of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="UnassignActivity" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to break the Activity's current assignment to Subsystem resources, thereby making them available for other Activities per the Subsystem resource allocation and scheduling.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityExecutionStatusType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PlannedActivityID" type="uci:PlannedActivityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID for the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityExecutionStatus" type="uci:ActivityExecutionStatusEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the status of execution of the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TransitionHistory" type="uci:TransitionStatusType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an actual current/past transition of the Planned Activity.  See *ActivityPlan for planned transitions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualActivityID" type="uci:ActivityID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an actual [Capability]Activity associated with execution of the sibling PlannedActivityID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ActivityID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to *Capability Activities.</xs:documentation>
