	<xs:complexType name="AIMIDB_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FLIGHT_NO" type="uci:AIMIDB_FlightNumberStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Each flight shall be identified by a flight number in the range 01 to 09. Flight 01 shall be the first flight of the day, flight 02 the second, etc. In order to ensure uniqueness in the image id, if the aircraft mission extends across midnight UTC, the flight number shall be 0x (where x is in the range 0 to 9) on images acquired before midnight UTC and Ax on images acquired after midnight UTC; for extended missions Bx to Zx shall designate images acquired on subsequent days. The value 00 indicates the flight number is unavailable.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MISSION_NO" type="uci:AIMIDB_MISSION_NO_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Four-character descriptor of the mission (see NOTE), which has the form PPNN, where PP is the DIA Project Code (range is AA to ZZ) or U0 if the Project Code is unknown, and "NN" is an assigned two digit identifier, for example, the last digits of FLIGHT_NO. "UNKN" (without quotes) shall be used if no specific descriptor is known. NOTE: The length and pattern  are incorrect, should be 4 chars, but the trailing space can just be dropped when producing the NITF product.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AirDataType" uci:version="001.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="IndicatedBaroAltitude" type="uci:AltitudeBarometricType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicated height above Mean Sea Level as measured by local barometric pressure, in meters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BarometricAltitudeRate" type="xs:float" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Rate of change of local barometric pressure, in meter per second.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Kollsman" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the altimeter setting used for the Indicated Barometric Altitude in hectopascals.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TrueAirspeed" type="uci:SpeedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The true airspeed of the aircraft reported in meters per second.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Alpha" type="uci:AngleHalfType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The aerodynamic angle of attack of the vehicle.  This is the difference between the pitch of the DOMAIN velocity vector (climb angle - gamma) and the vehicle's pitch Euler angle.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Beta" type="uci:AngleHalfType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The aerodynamic sideslip of the vehicle.  This is the difference between the heading of the DOMAIN velocity vector and the vehicle's yaw Euler angle.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time when the velocity data was measured or last known to be correct.  The element can also indicate the time at which a future velocity of a System, Entity, etc. will be achieved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
