			<xs:element name="AirVolumeSensorReferenced" type="uci:AirVolumeSensorReferencedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a 3D sensor referenced volume that an air volume capability is directed against.  This will define the volume in terms of azimuth and elevation angles.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AirVolumeLocation" type="uci:ZoneType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a 3D area that an air volume capability is directed against.  This should define the latitude/longitude extents of the volume along with any guidance regarding the height of the volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AirVolumeCueType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="VolumeLocation" type="uci:AirTargetVolumeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded air volume center and extents.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CueVelocity" type="uci:Velocity2D_UncertaintyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If capability is CUED, this field provides an estimate of the velocity of the center of the cue for moving targets. This velocity is at the center of the current cue.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AirVolumeSensorReferencedType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="AzimuthScanWidth" type="uci:AnglePositiveType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded azimuth width.  It represents the angular width between the two 3 dB extents of the scan volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AzimuthScanCenter" type="uci:AngleType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded azimuth center. For BODY stabilized volumes it is referenced to the centerline of the platform.  For INERTIAL stabilized volumes it is referenced to true north; clockwise rotation is positive in both cases.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElevationScanWidth" type="uci:AngleHalfType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded elevation scan width.  It represents the angular width between the two 3 dB extents of the scan volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElevationScanCenter" type="uci:AngleHalfType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded elevation center.  For BODY stabilized volumes it is referenced to the centerline of the platform.  For CENTER_ALTITUDE stabilized volumes it is referenced to the center altitude range pair.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MaxRangeOfInterest" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the maximum range of interest.  This will potential affect dwell times, scan rates, reported Entities, etc.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinRangeOfInterest" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the minimum range of interest.  This will potential affect dwell times, scan rates, reported Entities, etc.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AzimuthScanStabilization" type="uci:LOS_ReferenceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Center of volume can be stabilized either relative to the centerline of the aircraft (BODY) or relative to true north (INERTIAL).  In either case the radar will position volume either aligned with the aircraft's current direction or a particular line of bearing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElevationScanStabilization" type="uci:ElevationScanStabilizationEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Center of volume can be stabilized either relative to the boresight of the antenna installation on the aircraft (BODY) or relative to a location defined by the Elevation Scan Center Altitude Range Pair (CENTER_ALTITUDE).  In either case the radar will position volume either aligned with the aircraft's current pitch.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElevationScanCenterAltitudeRangePair" type="uci:AltitudeRangePairType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>For a center altitude stabilized elevation volumes, this is the center point around which the volume is stabilized.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RollStabilized" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) the volume should be stabilized parallel to the horizon.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AIS_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MMSI_Number" type="uci:MMSI_NumberStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Maritime Mobile Service Identity (MMSI) number of the vehicle/vessel.  In AIS, MMSI numbers are part of the unique ID of a track and serve as a form of identification.  Therefore, AIS MMSI numbers are directly represented in UCI instead of being considered a "foreign" or external type of ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="IMO_Number" type="uci:IMO_NumberType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the International Maritime Organization (IMO) identifier number of the vehicle/vessel.  In AIS, IMO numbers are part of the unique ID of a track and serve as a form of identification.  Therefore, AIS IMO numbers are directly represented in UCI instead of being considered a "foreign" or external type of ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VesselName" type="uci:AlphanumericDashSpaceUnderscoreString20OnlyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the AIS vessel name.  In AIS, vessel name is part of the unique ID of a track and serves as a form of identification.  Therefore, AIS vessel name is directly represented in UCI instead of being considered a "foreign" or external type of ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CallSign" type="uci:AlphanumericDashSpaceUnderscoreString20Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the AIS radio call sign.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AllowableSensorsType" uci:version="002.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the required, allowed, or excluded sensors. See parent element for additional context.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SensorCountConstraint" type="uci:SensorCountConstraintType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides the minimum and maximum number of sensors used to accomplish the task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Required" type="uci:SensorConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the types of sensor systems and specific systems that only can be used to accomplish the Orbital Surveillance Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Allowed" type="uci:SensorConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the types of sensor systems and specific systems that can be used to accomplish the Orbital Surveillance Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Excluded" type="uci:SensorConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the types of sensor systems and specific systems that must not be used to accomplish the Orbital Surveillance Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinOperatingClassificationLevel" type="uci:SecurityInformationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the sensor has to be capable of operating at this classification level or higher.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NearRealTimeProduct" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the service can generate and disseminate a product that doesn't take an extensive amount of time (within a handful of minutes) between collection and product dissemination.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AlongOrbitalArcDeltaType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The AlongOrbitalDelta is based on the mean anomaly along the orbit of the primary target.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MeanAnomaly" type="uci:AngleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The MeanAnomaly is an optional angular measurement for how far along the orbit to search.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeDelta" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The TimeDelta specifies the distance from the primary target based upon the time of the orbit.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AltitudeConstraintsType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specify a range of valid altitudes by defining min, max, or both. At least 1 of the child elements should be defined.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Min" type="uci:AltitudeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The minimum altitude in meters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Max" type="uci:AltitudeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The maximum altitude in meters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AltitudeOffsetReferenceType" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements for more details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="AltitudeOffsetReference" type="uci:AltitudeReferenceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to altitude offset measurement source.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AltitudeOffset" type="uci:DistanceOffsetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Altitude offset as measured from reference type in units of meters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AltitudeRadialPairType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Altitude" type="uci:AltitudeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This defines the altitude which provides 1,000 feet of clearance over all obstacles but do not necessarily assure acceptable navigation signal coverage.  Note: even though this annotation references obstacle clearance in feet (taken from the FAA Instrument Procedures Handbook), the altitude specified here is in meters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Radial" type="uci:AngleType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This defines the starting angle for the associated altitude.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AltitudeRangePairType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Altitude" type="uci:AltitudeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This defines the altitude around which the volume is stabilized.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Range" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This defines the range at which the associated altitude is calculated to define a particular geospatial point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AltitudeRangeType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Min" type="uci:AltitudeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Minimum value of the altitude range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Max" type="uci:AltitudeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum value of the altitude range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AltitudeReferenceType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements for more details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="AltitudeReference" type="uci:AltitudeReferenceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to altitude measurement source.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Altitude" type="uci:AltitudeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Altitude as measured from reference type in units of meters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AltitudeReferenceUncertaintyType" uci:version="001.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements for more details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="AltitudeReference" type="uci:AltitudeReferenceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Reference to altitude measurement source.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Altitude" type="uci:AltitudeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Altitude as measured from reference type in units of meters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VarAltitude" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Variance of altitude measurement with units of meters squared.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AmplifyingInformationType" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates amplifying information on the operational status of a weapon or facility along with locally defined amplifying data.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="OperationalStatus" type="uci:ObservedOperationalStatusEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the operational status of a reported weapon or facility.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LocalDiscreteIdentifier" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates locally defined amplifying data concerning a reported entity or system with discrete meaning established by the operational commander.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_ActivityCommandType" uci:version="003.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureActivityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Attempt" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If specified, indicates the specific attempt of an activity to which this command applies.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeDependentActivity" type="uci:DependentActivityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Changes Activities that this Activity is dependent on.  If the dependent Activity's Resource Allocation is removed or never allocated, this Activity's Resource Allocation will be removed or not fulfilled.  This is used to tie Activities within or across subsystems.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ResourceSelection" type="uci:ResourceSelectionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a Shared Antenna and/or AntennaResources to be used for the resulting Activity. This allows Mission Processing to direct an specific antenna, antenna resource type, or antenna resource instance to be used by the resulting Activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TargetVolume" type="uci:AirTargetVolumeCommandType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="2">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the volume or specific Entity that defines the extents of the spatial region covered by the command. 
For VOLUME AMTI Capabilities, the entity is not an option. 
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, two instances of this element are allowed to support an air volume that defines the extents of the cue volume around the Entity.
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, a single instance is allowed if it is an Entity in which case the Entity location uncertainty defines the extents of the cue volume or a sensor volume with a cue velocity.
For TRACK AMTI Capabilities it is expected that the Entity is the only valid selection.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="BlankingVolume" type="uci:AirTargetVolumeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an air volume that should be "blanked"; the Capability should not generate outputs associated with the volume because it is a known source of clutter or other interference for the Capability. For example, a blanking volume could be created around a wind farm that interferes with AMTI.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:CapabilityCommandFrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency to be used for the Command. If omitted, frequency selection is left to the command recipient within constraints of RF_Profiles imposed by RF_ControlCommand, MDF, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionOptions" type="uci:RadarCollectionOptionsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates guidance regarding which aspect or aspects of collection to favor if the command cannot be optimally scheduled as requested.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionConstraints" type="uci:AMTI_CollectionConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a set of bounding requirements for the particular collection associated with this command. The subsystem should attempt to satisfy all specified constraints.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TrackingRange" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the range within which a track should be initiated and a corresponding Entity message reported for detected moving targets. Beyond this range tracks should not be initiated and Entity should not be reported for detected moving targets. This element can be used to control track loading for large and/or dense search volumes. If omitted tracking range selection is left to discretion of the command recipient.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Repetition" type="uci:RepetitionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the required repetition of the command. If omitted, the command should be performed once.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProductOutput" type="uci:ProductOutputCommandBasicType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a required output Product of the Command. Only Products consistent with AMTI and supported by the commanded AMTI Capability should be requested. If omitted, no output Product should be produced. See ProductTypeEnum for further details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_ActivityMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Subsystem which hosts the AMTI Capabilities whose Activities are given in this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="uci:AMTI_ActivityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dynamic operational characteristics of an Activity of an AMTI Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_ActivityMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:AMTI_ActivityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_ActivityType" uci:version="003.001.003.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureActivityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SubCapability" type="uci:AMTI_SubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific SubCapability associated with the Activity.  If omitted, all SubCapabilities of the associated Capability are applicable for the Activity.  This element is required whenever a subset of SubCapabilities of a Capability are used by the Activity. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TargetVolume" type="uci:AirTargetVolumeCommandType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="2">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the volume or specific Entity that defines the extents of the spatial region covered by the command. 
For VOLUME AMTI Capabilities, the entity is not an option. 
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, two instances of this element are allowed to support an air volume that defines the extents of the cue volume around the Entity.
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, a single instance is allowed if it is an Entity in which case the Entity location uncertainty defines the extents of the cue volume or a sensor volume with a cue velocity.
For TRACK AMTI Capabilities it is expected that the Entity is the only valid selection.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Repetition" type="uci:RepetitionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the repetition of the Activity.  If omitted, the Activity is not repetitive.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Metrics" type="uci:MTI_ActivityStatusDetailType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates performance metrics that provide the system insight regarding the progress of an activity, description of the results of an activity and related stats. This is a list to provide reporting for all revisits between activity messages.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PolicyApplied" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>When TRUE, indicates the Activity could not be scheduled as requested but the radar was able to apply the command's CollectionPolicy and then successfully schedule or complete the activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AllProductsAndMessagesProduced" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Flag indicating whether or not all products (e.g., ProductLocation) and messages (e.g., Entity) expected to be produced by this activity have been output.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Traceability" type="uci:TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>C2 sources work at different levels of detail and abstraction, progressing from what to do to how specifically to do it.  Inputs from abstract tasking sources and Tasks can be decomposed into discrete, actionable Tasks and/or Capability commands.  This element provides traceability to the external tasking or Task from which this Capability command was derived.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ElectronicProtectionOptionsEmployed" type="uci:ForeignKeyType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates which electronic protection IDs are in use for this activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MultistaticModeOptionsEmployed" type="uci:MultistaticModeOptionsEmployedType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates which emitter IDs are in use for this activity and whether Multistatic Mode is enabled or disabled.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CapabilityCommandType" uci:version="003.001.003.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureCapabilityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SubCapability" type="uci:AMTI_SubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific AMTI SubCapability being invoked by the command.  If omitted, all SubCapabilities of the sibling CapabilityID are to be invoked.  If specified, only those SubCapabilities specified are required in order to satisfy the command.  See enumeration annotations for further details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DependentActivity" type="uci:DependentActivityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Changes Activities that this Activity is dependent on.  If the dependent Activity's Resource Allocation is removed or never allocated, this Activity's Resource Allocation will be removed or not fulfilled.  This is used to tie Activities within or across subsystems.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ResourceSelection" type="uci:ResourceSelectionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a Shared Antenna and/or AntennaResources to be used for the resulting Activity. This allows direction of a specific antenna, antenna resource type, or antenna resource instance to be used by the resulting Activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MultistaticMode" type="uci:MultistaticModeType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the Multistatic Mode settings and associated data to be used for the command.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TargetVolume" type="uci:AirTargetVolumeCommandType" maxOccurs="2">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the volume or specific Entity that defines the extents of the spatial region covered by the command. 
For VOLUME AMTI Capabilities, the entity is not an option. 
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, two instances of this element are allowed to support an air volume that defines the extents of the cue volume around the Entity.
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, a single instance is allowed if it is an Entity in which case the Entity location uncertainty defines the extents of the cue volume or a sensor volume with a cue velocity.
For TRACK AMTI Capabilities it is expected that the Entity is the only valid selection.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="BlankingVolume" type="uci:AirTargetVolumeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an air volume that should be "blanked"; the Capability should not generate outputs associated with the volume because it is a known source of clutter or other interference for the Capability.  For example, a blanking volume could be created around a wind farm that interferes with AMTI.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:CapabilityCommandFrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency to be used for the Command.  If omitted, frequency selection is left to the command recipient within constraints of RF_Profiles imposed by RF_ControlCommand, MDF, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionOptions" type="uci:RadarCollectionOptionsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates guidance regarding which aspect or aspects of collection to favor if the command cannot be optimally scheduled as requested.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  Omitting this element is equivalent to FLEXIBLE, that is deferring to the Command recipient.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionConstraints" type="uci:AMTI_CollectionConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a set of bounding requirements for the particular collection associated with this command.  The subsystem should attempt to satisfy all specified constraints.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TrackingRange" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the range within which a track should be initiated and a corresponding Entity message reported for detected moving targets.  Beyond this range tracks should not be initiated and Entity should not be reported for detected moving targets.  This element can be used to control track loading for large and/or dense search volumes.  If omitted tracking range selection is left to discretion of the command recipient.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Repetition" type="uci:RepetitionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the required repetition of the command.  If omitted, the command should be performed once.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProductOutput" type="uci:ProductOutputCommandBasicType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a required output Product of the Command.  Only Products consistent with AMTI and supported by the commanded AMTI Capability should be requested.  If omitted, no output Product should be produced.  See ProductTypeEnum for further details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CapabilityMDT" uci:version="001.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an installed AMTI Capability, its configurable characteristics and its controllability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CapabilityMT" uci:version="001.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CapabilityOptionsType" uci:version="000.001.000.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="InterruptOtherActivities" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) the Capability supports the InterruptOtherActivities element in the AMTI_Command message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CollectionPolicy" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) the Capability supports the CollectionPolicy element in the AMTI_Command message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConcurrentOperationSupported" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the capability has the ability to run concurrently with at least one other capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticOptionsSupported" type="uci:MultistaticOptionsSupportedType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the multistatic options supported by the Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FalseAlarmLevelUpperLimit" type="xs:unsignedByte" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the FalseAlarmLevel capability is supported and also defines the upper limit allowed by the capability. Used to set the quantity of sensitivity levels. If omitted tracking range selection is the full range of the reference type. A common range is [0,15].</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElectronicProtectionOptionsSupported" type="uci:ElectronicProtectionOptionsSupportedType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the list of EP capabilities that the current HW / SW allows an external actor to control for this capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CapabilityStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityStatus" type="uci:CapabilityStatusType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the high level availability/state of a Capability instance.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="RF_Profile" type="uci:RF_ProfileType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a RF Emission Profile currently applied to the Capability.  If omitted, there are no current profiles and the Capability is operating per its defaults and other constraints.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DefaultEmcon" type="uci:EmconSettingType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Defines the default emission control level to be applied to targets detected by this capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EmissionBalanceState" type="uci:EmissionBalanceEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See enumeration annotations for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CurrentMessageOutput" type="uci:AMTI_MessageOutputsEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Specifies which messages are currently being output by the Capability.  See enumerated type annotations for details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ElectronicProtectionOptionsEnabled" type="uci:ElectronicProtectionOptionsEnabledType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates which electronic protection options are currently enabled and will be used by this Capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CapabilityStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CapabilityType" uci:version="001.001.003.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CommandableCapabilityDeclarationType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's first tier type in the AMTI taxonomy.  For AMTI, the first tier is an indication of the physical area covered.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SubCapabilityType" type="uci:AMTI_SubCapabilityEnum" maxOccurs="4">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability of the AMTI Capability; the second tier in the taxonomy of AMTI.  For AMTI, the second tier is waveform category.  See enumeration annotations for further details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition. The selection of AUTO_SUBCAPABILITY_SELECT still requires the evaluation of all sibling attributes by the Capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityOptions" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityOptionsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's support for select optional elements in its accepted control interface messages.  Support for these elements is expected to vary across Capability implementations but must be known in order to adapt and configure upstream Systems and Services which use the Capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SupportedFrequencies" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a frequency range used by the Capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageOutput" type="uci:AMTI_MessageOutputsEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a message that is an output of the Capability.  See enumerated type annotations for details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CollectionConstraintsType" uci:version="001.002.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CollectionConstraintsType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SurfaceMoverVelocityGate" type="uci:SpeedType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the velocity below which moving targets should be assumed to be surface moving targets despite being detected by AMTI, not initiated as AMTI tracks and not reported as Entities.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TargetRCS" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the radar cross section (RCS) of targets which are of interest for the Command.  This element can be used to guide dwell times, inform trackers, etc.  If omitted RCS selection is left to discretion of the command recipient.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FalseAlarmLevel" type="xs:unsignedByte" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the acceptable false alarm level for outputs from the Command.  This element can be used to adjust the sensitivity of the Capability in initiating tracks and reporting Entities.  Lower numbers indicate a more restrictive capability, i.e. fewer results. See FalseAlarmLevelUpperLimit for further details.  If omitted tracking range selection is left to the discretion of the command recipient. A common range is [0,15].</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Emcon" type="uci:EmconConstraintType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Used to control the RF emissions associated with this command.  If this field is not populated, the service determines all parameters.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TargetRadialVelocity" type="uci:SpeedRangeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates both closing and opening velocities. This is the Radial velocity along the LOS to the sensor for each valid range of radial velocity i.e., Volume searches may have multiple radial velocities that are of interest.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CommandMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Command" type="uci:AMTI_CommandType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an instance of an AMTI Capability command.  A Capability command message can have multiple command instances to allow a sequence of related commands in a single coherent message.  Each command instance reports status via a separate, independent Capability CommandStatus message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CommandMT" uci:version="003.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:AMTI_CommandMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CommandResponseType" uci:version="000.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an AMTI collection is desired in response to the specified events or conditions.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the desired AMTI_Command type.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TargetRCS" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the radar cross section (RCS) of targets which are of interest for the Command.  This element can be used to guide dwell times, inform trackers, etc.  If omitted RCS selection is left to discretion of the command recipient.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductOutput" type="uci:ProductOutputCommandBasicType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a required output Product of the Command.  Only Products consistent with AMTI and supported by the commanded AMTI Capability should be requested.  If omitted, no output Product should be produced.  See ProductTypeEnum for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CommandStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityCommandStatusBaseType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CommandStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:AMTI_CommandStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_CommandType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityCommandType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a new invocation of an AMTI Capability.  Generally, if accepted, the command will result in one or more new AMTI Activities being created and reported via the AMTI_Activity message.  The request/response interaction terminates as soon as the command is accepted or rejected; this element is not used to interact with an "active" command.  Updates and/or additional interaction with the resulting Activity (after the command is accepted) is accomplished via the sibling Activity element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="uci:AMTI_ActivityCommandType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to modify an existing AMTI Activity (which was previously reported via the AMTI_Activity message and was marked as "interactive").  The request/response interaction terminates as soon as the modification is accepted or rejected.  The modifications are reflected in subsequent AMTI_Activity messages.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_SettingsCommandMDT" uci:version="001.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilitySettingsCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ElectronicProtectionOptions" type="uci:ElectronicProtectionOptionsDefaultType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates which advertised EP options should be applied to all Activities associated with this Capability. This list will completely replace any previously commanded list of EP options.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EmissionBalanceState" type="uci:EmissionBalanceEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See enumeration annotations for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageOutput" type="uci:AMTI_MessageOutputsEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Specifies which messages are to be output by the Capability as the result of capability commands.  See enumerated type annotations for details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="UnassignAll" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to break all current assignments of Activities to resources.  As a result, the resources could be assigned to other Activities, re-assigned to the original Activity or a combination of the two.  Equivalent to simultaneously commanding each current Activity to be Unassigned via the AMTI_Command message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DefaultEmcon" type="uci:EmconSettingType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Defines the default emission control level to be applied to targets detected by this capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
