	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_TargetType" uci:version="002.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="AirVolumeSensorReferenced" type="uci:AirVolumeSensorReferencedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a 3D sensor referenced volume that an air volume capability is directed against.  This will define the volume in terms of azimuth and elevation angles.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AirVolumeLocation" type="uci:ZoneType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a 3D area that an A2A capability is directed against.  This should define the latitude/longitude extents of the volume along with any guidance regarding the height of the volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of an Entity that is the target of a cued AMTI search.  This element can be used as the full specification of the target volume for the cued search.  It can also be used in combination with the sibling AirVolume element to define extents of the cue volume around the Entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_TaskBaseType" uci:version="002.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:AMTI_CapabilityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's first tier type in the AMTI taxonomy.  For AMTI, the first tier is an indication of the physical area covered.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubCapabilityType" type="uci:AMTI_SubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability of the AMTI Capability; the second tier in the taxonomy of AMTI.  For AMTI, the second tier is waveform category.  See enumeration annotations for further details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CollectionPolicy" type="uci:CollectionPolicyEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates guidance regarding which aspect or aspects of collection to favor if the command cannot be optimally scheduled as requested.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  Omitting this element is equivalent to FLEXIBLE, that is deferring to the Command recipient.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CollectionConstraints" type="uci:AMTI_CollectionConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates constraints on the collection and/or processing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Output" type="uci:ProductOutputCommandBasicType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a desired output Product of the Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="AMTI_TaskType" uci:version="003.000.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:AMTI_TaskBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Target" type="uci:AMTI_TargetType" maxOccurs="2">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the volume or specific Entity that defines the extents of the spatial region covered by the command. 
For VOLUME AMTI Capabilities, the Entity is not an option.
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, two instances of this element are allowed to support an air volume that defines the extents of the cue volume around the Entity.
For CUED AMTI Capabilities, a single instance is allowed if it is an Entity in which case the Entity location uncertainty defines the extents of the cue volume.
For TRACK AMTI Capabilities it is expected that the Entity is the only valid selection.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
