	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetEstimationRequestMDT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:RequestBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CommAssetID" type="uci:CommAssetID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The ID of the System whose state should be estimated as part of this request.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="RequestType" type="uci:CommAssetEstimationMessageEnum" maxOccurs="2">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The type of estimation requested and resulting messages to produce as part of this request. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="RequestFrequencyType" type="uci:RepeatEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>A System Estimation Request can be used in 2 ways:

1.)  SINGLE - A request for a single estimation of system state.  The invoked service function is called once and returns one set of responses (one per requested message type).  The request should not persist beyond the single call, and can be deleted immediately upon successful completion.

2.)  PERIODIC / STOP - A request to periodically estimate system state and periodically publish the requested messages.  A request for periodic estimates should continue to execute until the request is updated with this value set to STOP.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ResultsInNativeMessage" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates whether the position estimate should be published via the "native" message or contained within the CommAssetEstimationRequestStatus message.  For example, if TRUE, a successful CommAssetEstimationRequest would result in CommAssetPositionReport messages being published.  If FALSE, the CommAssetPositionReport would be embedded in CommAssetEstimationRequestStatus.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TimeStep" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>For a PERIODIC estimation, the time step determines the rate at which the estimation should be published.

For a SINGLE estimation, the time step determines the number of estimations that will occur between the start and the end.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EstimationStart" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>In absence of this element, the estimator service should always use the state last reported by the asset.  It should also use the time associated with the last report as the basis of estimation.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EstimationEnd" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element can be used to specify the time to stop estimation.

In absence of this element, the estimator service should continue estimating the state until requested to stop.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetEstimationRequestMT" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message is used as an event to generate a position estimate assessment. This message should always have the ResultsInAssessmentMessage set to FALSE because position estimates are reported using PositionReport instead of Assessment.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:CommAssetEstimationRequestMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetEstimationRequestStatusMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:RequestStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="EstimationResult" type="uci:CommAssetEstimationResultType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The result of the communication asset estimation.  If a SINGLE response was requested there will be multiple results for each timestep.  This field will be populated if ResultsInNativeMessage=true and the RequestStatus is COMPLETED.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetEstimationRequestStatusMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:CommAssetEstimationRequestStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetEstimationResultType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CommAsset" type="uci:CommAssetMDT" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates details about a specific communication asset within a particular communication system in the CommAsset message format.  This is optional and populated only if the CommAssetEstimationRequest specified ResultsInNativeMessage=FALSE so the communication asset estimation result would be embedded in the CommAssetEstimationRequestStatus message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommAssetPositionReport" type="uci:CommAssetPositionReportMDT" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current position of a communication asset in the CommAssetPositionReport message format.  This is optional and populated only if the CommAssetEstimationRequest specified ResultsInNativeMessage=FALSE so the communication asset estimation result would be embedded in the CommAssetEstimationRequestStatus message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the timestamp of the estimation result.  This is optional and populated only if the CommAssetEstimationRequest specified ResultsInNativeMessage=FALSE so the communication asset estimation result would be embedded in the CommAssetEstimationRequestStatus message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetMDT" uci:version="002.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CommAssetID" type="uci:CommAssetID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the unique identifier for this particular communication asset.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommSystemID" type="uci:CommSystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique identifier for this particular communication system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Category" type="uci:CommAssetCategoryEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of asset this is.
 - STATIONARY assets do not move on their own.  It is possible for a stationary asset to relocate but doing so may change its identification.  The expectation is that the asset will not move while it is in use.
 - MOBILE assets may move or change their location while it is in use and must be accounted for when scheduling and/or evaluating communications coverage.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Antenna" type="uci:AntennaType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents a specific antenna that is available for use on this communication asset.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommAssetMT" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:CommAssetMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
