			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommPointingPlanAssessmentType" uci:version="003.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Base data structure containing both the inputs and outputs for a Comm Pointing Assessment.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Parameters" type="uci:CommPointingPlanRequestType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the parameters used in calculating the sibling results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Data" type="uci:CommPointingPlanDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the results of a comm pointing assessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommPointingPlanDataType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The results of an assessment that determines Comms coverage for a set of Mission Plans.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Window" type="uci:PointingPlanWindowType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The List of Time bounded Windows supported by this Pointing Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="CommPointingPlanRequestType" uci:version="003.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The inputs used in generating and/or requesting a Comm Pointing Assessment.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="RoutePlan" type="uci:RoutePlanReferencesType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a RoutePlan or parts of a RoutePlan to assess for communications support and pointing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssessmentConstraintLevel" type="uci:CommPointingAssessmentEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Refers to the level of possible resource windows to consider in the assessment, going from Unconstrained, to what's possibly Available, to only what's planned/requested, and at most restrictive only base the assessment on Approved Allocations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommScheduleAvailabilityConstraints" type="uci:CommCoverageUserDataType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element constrains the assessment to the use of all unscheduled, unpurchased, available comm.  When Assessment Constraint Level is set to COMM_SCHEDULE_AVAILABILITY, this element is populated concurrently with communication scheduling Requirements Constraints and communication schedule allocation Constraints.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommSchedulingRequirementConstraintsID" type="uci:CommSchedulingRequirementID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element constrains the assessment to the use of communication requirements that may or may not have been submitted in a CommSchedulingRequest.  This assessment type allows communication to be analyzed based on any pending communication purchases or prior to purchase.  When Assessment Constraint Level is set to COMM_SCHEDULE_REQUIREMENTS, this element may be populated concurrently with communicationSchedule Allocation Constraints.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
