				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The covariance between the inner product of the target pointing vector and the sensor Y-axis and the rate of change of the inner product of the target pointing vector and the sensor Y-axis. In the case of linear arrays, the Y-axis is the same as the orientation of the linear array. In the case of two-dimensional arrays, the Y-axis is the "Horizontal" axis. It has units of per second.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CosconeY_CosconeZ_Rate" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The covariance between the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Y-axis of the array face and the rate of change of the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Z-axis of the array face. CosconeY and CosconeZ represent the inner product of the target pointing vector and the "Horizontal" (Y) and "Down" (Z) axes respectively. This term is only used for two-dimensional arrays and has units of per second.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CosconeZ_CosconeY_Rate" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The covariance between the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Z-axis of the array face and the rate of change of the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Y-axis of the array face. CosconeY and CosconeZ represent the inner product of the target pointing vector and the "Horizontal" (Y) and "Down" (Z) axes respectively. This term is only used for two-dimensional arrays and has units of per second.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CosconeZ_CosconeZ_Rate" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The covariance between the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Z-axis of the array face and the rate of change of the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Z-axis of the array face. The Z-axis is the "Down" axis of the array, perpendicular to both the X-axis (boresight) and the Y-axis (horizontal). This term is only used for two-dimensional arrays and has units of per second.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CosconeY_RateCosconeZ_Rate" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The covariance between the rate of change of the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Y-axis of the array face and the rate of change of the inner product of the target pointing vector and the Z-axis of the array face. CosconeY and CosconeZ represent the inner product of the target pointing vector and the "Horizontal" (Y) and "Down" (Z) axes respectively. This term is only used for two-dimensional arrays and has units of per second squared.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
