	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_ID_Type" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to DMPIs.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:VersionedID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_LocationType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specifies the DMPI location information.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_Coordinates" type="uci:Point3D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the geographic location of the DMPI.  Generally, services are encouraged to send time data whenever it is known.  In this case the time data should indicate the time when mensuration of the target/DMPI was performed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LinearErrorProbable" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the altitude error of the DMPI. This element specifies the vertical component of the geospatial position accuracy due to measurement errors.  It is the linear error of the location with an uncertainty specified by sibling field Confidence, i.e. a percent (indicated by sibling field Confidence) of all vertical errors in the DMPI location will be less than or equal to this element.  The sibling CircularErrorProbable and Confidence fields should be provided when this field is provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CircularErrorProbable" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element specifies the horizontal component of the geospatial position accuracy due to measurement errors.  It is the radius of a circle centered on the location in which there is a specified probability (sibling field Confidence) that the target lies within.  The sibling LinearErrorProbable and Confidence fields should be provided when this field is provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Confidence" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element is the percent of confidence in the measurement errors associated with the geospatial accuracy of a location.  For example if the value is 90%, then 90% of all DMPI location horizontal errors will be less than or equal to sibling CircularErrorProbable and 90% of all DMPI location vertical errors will be less than or equal to sibling LinearErrorProbable.  The sibling CircularErrorProbable and LinearErrorProbable fields should be provided when this field is provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_MDT" uci:version="003.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataRecordBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="DMPI_ID" type="uci:DMPI_ID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a unique ID assigned to the DMPI.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Target" type="uci:DMPI_TargetType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the target location of the DMPI.  The target can be by physical location or by an Identity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Traceability" type="uci:DMPI_TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>These are IDs or other information that provides traceability of the DMPI to its sources.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Remarks" type="uci:RemarksType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates free text comments from a DMPI creator.  Both a short and longer detailed comment can be provided.  These comments are ad-hoc and unformatted but may include explanations of how and why the DMPIs were placed and/or weaponeered.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Weaponeering" type="uci:WeaponeeringType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the weaponeering solution for the DMPI.  The weaponeering solution is driven by many factors including the specific type of the target, available weapons, rules of engagement and other factors, some of which are captured in other UCI messages linked to the DMPI message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Source" type="uci:CreationSourceEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of the DMPI.  This is different than sibling Traceability which indicates external sources.  This field can be used to indicate an Operator created the DMPI.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Ranking" type="uci:ComparableRankingType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the ranking of DMPIs relative to targets as result of weaponeering/targeteering.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_MT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:DMPI_MDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_PatternChoiceType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="XbyY_Pattern" type="uci:DMPI_XbyY_PatternType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a rectangular X by Y DMPI pattern; a pattern of rows and columns with a regular grid spacing.  The columns are oriented parallel to the PatternOrientation.  The DMPI IDs listed correspond to the pattern beginning at the top of the leftmost column, proceeding right across the first row and then on to the leftmost column of the second row and so forth.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RadialPattern" type="uci:DMPI_RadialPatternType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A radial pattern is a wheel-and-spoke pattern.  The first spoke/radial originates at the PatternLocationCenter in the direction given by PatternOrientation.  The DMPI IDs listed correspond to the pattern beginning at the centermost DMPI on the first radial then proceeding clockwise to the centermost DMPI on the next radial and subsequent radials followed by the next outermost DMPI of the first radial and so on.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FreePatternDMPI_ID" type="uci:DMPI_ID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a free pattern used to group DMPIs that can't be defined as an X by Y or radial pattern.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_PatternID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to DMPI patterns.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_PatternMDT" uci:version="001.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataRecordBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="DMPI_PatternID" type="uci:DMPI_PatternID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a unique ID assigned to the DMPI pattern.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Pattern" type="uci:DMPI_PatternChoiceType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the collection of information to indicate a DMPI pattern is rectangular, radial or a free pattern.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_PatternMT" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:DMPI_PatternMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_PatternType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_ID" type="uci:DMPI_ID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a list of unique IDs of DMPIs.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PatternCenterLocation" type="uci:Point3D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the geometric center of the DMPI pattern.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PatternOrientation" type="uci:AngleType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orientation of the DMPI pattern relative to true north.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="IncludeDMPI_AtCenter" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) a DMPI, in addition to the DMPIs specified by the DMPI pattern, is included at the geometric center of the pattern.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CenterDMPI_ID" type="uci:DMPI_ID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the center DMPI.  When the IncludeDMPI_AtCenter element is TRUE, this element must be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_RadialPatternType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DMPI_PatternType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="NumberOfRadials" type="xs:unsignedInt">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of radials/spokes in the pattern.  The radials originate from the PatternCenterLocation and are equally spaced angularly.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="RadialSpacing" type="uci:DistanceType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates DMPI spacing along a radial.  The first DMPI is this distance from PatternCenterLocation as is the second DMPI on the radial from the first.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DMPIS_PerRadial" type="xs:unsignedInt">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of DMPIs on each radial/spoke.  The total number of DMPIs in the pattern is this number times the NumberOfRadials plus 1 if IncludeDMPI_AtCenter is true.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_StatusMDT" uci:version="002.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_ID" type="uci:DMPI_ID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of the DMPI corresponding to this status message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_State" type="uci:DMPI_StateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of a DMPI.  This could be a partial state per System, Task, or MissionPlan.  The DMPI state may be influenced by the sibling StoreStatus.  For example, if multiple weapons are being released, the DMPI State will be EXECUTING while the store states in StoreStatus are a mix of RELEASED and ALLOCATED.  Once all store states in StoreStatus are in a RELEASED state the DMPI state will be RELEASED.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_StrikeState" type="uci:StrikeStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the strike designation of a DMPI if supported.  If missing, such as in legacy systems, default is Strike.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the System to which the DMPI has been allocated.  For a given DMPI, the associated System can change when the allocation of the associated Task changes.  A multiple store DMPI can be associated with multiple Tasks allocated to multiple Systems with status reported via multiple DMPI_Status messages each indicating the same DMPI_ID.  Through its life cycle, a DMPI could be allocated to a System  with this element then associated with a kinematic and action plan of the System with sibling elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssociatedRoutePlan" type="uci:RoutePlanReferencesType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the RoutePlan which the DMPI_Status is associated with.  For a given DMPI, the associated RoutePlan can change when the allocation of the associated Task changes.  A multiple store DMPI can be associated with multiple Tasks allocated to multiple RoutePlans with status reported via multiple DMPI_Status messages each indicating the same DMPI_ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssociatedActivityPlan" type="uci:ActivityPlanReferenceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the *ActivityPlan which the DMPI_Status is associated with.  For a given DMPI, the associated *ActivityPlan can change when the allocation of the associated Task changes.  A multiple store DMPI can be associated with multiple Tasks allocated to multiple *ActivityPlans with status reported via multiple DMPI_Status messages each indicating the same DMPI_ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StoreStatus" type="uci:DMPI_StoreStatusType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI status in terms of its associated store or stores.  The number of instances of this element varies depending on the store quantity of the associated DMPI, how the associated Strike Task or Tasks are allocated, etc.  See the annotations for the DMPI_Status message for further insight.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TaskID" type="uci:TaskID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of the Task which the DMPI has been allocated to.  Required once the DMPI is associated with a Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_StatusMT" uci:version="002.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:DMPI_StatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_StoreStatusType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="StoreState" type="uci:DMPI_StoreStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI relevant state of a store associated with the DMPI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a store (Strike capability) instance which has been allocated to satisfy the DMPI store instance.  This element is expected for sibling StoreStates where a capability/store is assigned to the DMPI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Reason" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a free text explanation of the DMPI's/store's state.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeOfImpact" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimated time of impact of the assigned store (Strike Capability).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_TargetType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the target of the DMPI. The target can be specified by location or by identity. This allows DMPI targets to be specified based on target types.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="ByLocation" type="uci:DMPI_LocationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the geographic location and location error for the DMPI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ByIdentity" type="uci:IdentityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the target of the DMPI in the form of an Identity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_TraceabilityType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="BE_Number" type="uci:BasicEncyclopediaNumberType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Basic Encyclopedia Number of the target which the DMPI corresponds to.  This optional element is intended to support use cases where DMPIs precede the creation of Entities.  In use cases where Entities precede DMPIs, the EntityID element would be used instead of or in addition to this element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TraceObject" type="uci:GeoLocatedObjectType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of the Object which the DMPI corresponds to. This optional element is the general, preferred linkage from DMPIs to the target which the DMPI supports.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ATO_Traceability" type="uci:ATO_TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a reference to an external (non-UCI) DMPI source: the Air Tasking Order.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_ViolationChoiceType" uci:version="000.000.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="OpLineID" type="uci:OpLineID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The air corridor violated by a line between the release point and the indicated DMPI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OpZoneID" type="uci:OpZoneID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The NoFire OpZone violated by the minimum safe distance (blast radius) around the indicated DMPI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OpVolumeID" type="uci:OpVolumeID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The NoFire OpVolume violated by the minimum safe distance (blast radius) around the indicated DMPI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_ViolationType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ViolationType" type="uci:DMPI_ViolationChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of geospatial control element violated by the DMPI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_ID" type="uci:DMPI_ID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates which DMPI violate the given corridor or NoFire zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DMPI_XbyY_PatternType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DMPI_PatternType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="X_Spacing" type="uci:DistanceType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates pattern spacing in the X coordinate; spacing between columns.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="X_Number" type="xs:unsignedInt">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of X columns in the DMPI pattern.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Y_Spacing" type="uci:DistanceType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates pattern spacing in the Y coordinate; spacing between rows.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Y_Number" type="xs:unsignedInt">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of Y rows in the DMPI pattern.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DomeType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element describes the geometric parameters of a dome via a radius. The location of the dome is referenced by the point representing the center of a sphere of the same radius; in other words, the center of the circle which is the base of the dome (see sibling Kinematics element for position of this point).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Radius" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the radius of the dome.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorCommandChoiceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="DoorState" type="uci:DoorCommandEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Command the door to open or close.  In some systems this may not be required and the stores management system will automatically open the door when a release is commanded.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CloseOnHungStore" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This setting is used with systems that automatically open and close the bay door as part of a store release command.  When a release fails and there is a hung store, this setting dictates whether the door should be left open or forced closed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorCommandMDT" uci:version="002.001.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Command" type="uci:DoorCommandType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command instance.  Multiple command instances allow a sequence of related commands to be described in a single coherent message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorCommandMT" uci:version="002.002.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:DoorCommandMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorCommandStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SupportCapabilityCommandStatusBaseType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorCommandStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:DoorCommandStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorCommandType" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type represents a command to control a door that is relevant to mission operations.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SupportCapabilityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="DoorCommand" type="uci:DoorCommandChoiceType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates information to command the door to open or close and specify close on hung store condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorStatusMDT" uci:version="002.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type represents the status and settings for a door that is relevant to mission operations.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="DoorStatus" type="uci:DoorStatusType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This type represents the status and settings for each door that is relevant to mission operations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorStatusMT" uci:version="003.002.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:DoorStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoorStatusType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SupportCapabilityStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="DoorState" type="uci:DoorStateEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The door state is reported.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CloseOnHungStore" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If the door automatically opens and closes in association with the release of a store, this element reports if the door will try to close when a hung store / failed release is reported.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of a Capability whose use requires operation of the door.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Locked" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates if the door is locked.  A door can be locked in any open position and it can be locked in the closed position.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PercentOpen" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The percent the door is from closed to fully open.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DoubleMinMaxType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Generic type to use for xs:double type minimum and maximum allowable setting values.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Min" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Minimum allowable value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Max" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum allowable value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DownloadConstrainedSubPlanType" uci:version="002.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ConstrainedSubPlanRank" type="uci:ComparableRankingType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element provides precedence and priority ranking for each constrained subplan.  In the case that multiple subplans return true (all filters in more than one subplan are true), this is used to determine which subplan to apply.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AutoDownload" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This value enables/disables automatic download of products.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Filter" type="uci:ProductFilterType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Filters are used to determine if the constrained subplan applies.  All of the filter criteria within a constrained subplan must be satisfied to apply the subplan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DragCoefficientChoiceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>A choice of drag coefficient to use. It is a choice between a simple drag coefficient and VCM drag parameters.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="VCM_DragParameters" type="uci:VCM_DragParametersType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A set of drag parameters used for VCM propagation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DragCoefficientValue" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A dimensionless value based on the shape of the RSO that is used to help quantify the drag force on the RSO.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DropRestrictionType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Nature and/or source of a drop restriction.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="DropRestriction" type="uci:DropRestrictionEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of drop restriction on the Entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssociatedMessage" type="uci:AssociatedDropRestrictMessageType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the message that is requiring the drop restriction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DuplicateRequirementType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a Requirement that is equivalent to a Requirement or Requirements already planned by the subject System.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="RequirementID" type="uci:RequirementInstanceID_ChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of a Requirement given in the RequirementOptionsCommand that was determined to be equivalent to the Requirement or Requirements given by the sibling ExistingRequirementID element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ExistingRequirementID" type="uci:RequirementInstanceID_ChoiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of an existing Requirement that is already planned by the System and is equivalent to the Requirement indicated by the sibling RequirementID element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DurationRangeType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Minimum and Maximum time duration range values.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Min" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Minimum time duration value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Max" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum time duration value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DVR_ProcessingParametersType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This is a polymorphic extension which allows for the extension of the base ProcessingParametersPET. This represents the processing parameters needed for using a DVR-like service to create new Products from existing video Products or streams.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ProcessingParametersPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Operation" type="uci:DVR_OperationEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the DVR operation to perform to create the new Product.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="StartTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This field represents a time offset from the beginning of an existing video Product.  If the sibling Operation to be performed is "CLIP" then this is the starting point for the new video Product.  If the sibling Operation to be performed is "STILL" then this element represents the time offset of the video frame that should be should as the still image for the new Product.  For all other sibling Operations this field should not be used.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EndTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This field represents a time offset from the beginning of an existing video Product.  If the sibling Operation to be performed is "CLIP" then this is the ending point for the new video Product.  For all other sibling Operations this field should not be used.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="DwellID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ActivityChangeBeamCommandType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="BeamID" type="uci:BeamID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the EA Beam being changed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ChangeBeamState" type="uci:CapabilityCommandStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change the state of the Beam.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="UnassignBeam" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to break the Beam's current assignment to Subsystem resources/components, thereby making them available for other Beams per the Subsystem's resource allocation and scheduling.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DeleteBeam" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to delete a Beam.  A deleted Activity can't be re-enabled, including by an automated Capability that was the original source of the Activity.  It is equivalent to a sticky UnassignBeam command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ChangeFrequency" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to modify the Frequency Range of the EA_Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ActivityCommandType" uci:version="003.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureActivityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ChangeBeam" type="uci:EA_ActivityChangeBeamCommandType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to modify an existing Beam of an existing EA Activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeDependentActivity" type="uci:DependentActivityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Changes Activities that this Activity is dependent on.  If the dependent Activity's Resource Allocation is removed or never allocated, this Activity's Resource Allocation will be removed or not fulfilled.  This is used to tie Activities within or across subsystems.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeReceiveAntenna" type="uci:SelectAntennaType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Update the Antenna, Antenna Resource Type, or Antenna Resource Instance used for receive portion of this activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeTransmitAntenna" type="uci:SelectAntennaType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Update the Antenna, Antenna Resource Type, or Antenna Resource Instance used for transmit portion of this activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeTarget" type="uci:EA_ChangeLocationAndPowerType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Change steering of the jamming.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeProtectedEntityPredictedReturnPower" type="uci:ProtectedAssetReturnPowerType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The ProtectedAsset child element indicates which of the protected assets of the activity are the subject of the child attribute ChangeProtectedAssetPredictedReturnPower. (In order to add or remove protected entities, a new CapabilityCommandType must be utilized.).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:CapabilityCommandFrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency to be used for the Command.  If omitted, frequency selection is left to the command recipient within constraints of RF_Profiles imposed by RF_ControlCommand, MDF, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ActivityMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Subsystem which hosts the EA Capabilities whose Activities are given in this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="uci:EA_ActivityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dynamic operational characteristics of an Activity of an EA Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProtectedEntityAssessment" type="uci:VehicleThreatAssessmentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an assessment of a protected entity's benefit from the EA described in the sibling Activity element.  EA contributions from other sources, including from other Capabilities or Subsystems, should be included in the assessment whenever known.  The term "protected entity" comes from EA doctrine and roughly means a blue force system, generally an aircraft, that is being protected by an EA system.  In UCI terminology "protected entity" would be better stated as "protected System".</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ActivityMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_ActivityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ActivityType" uci:version="003.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureActivityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="EA_Details" type="uci:EA_DetailsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the details of the EA activity for both assigned and unassigned beams.  The beam structure is also used to provide characteristics of omnidirectional transmissions.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProtectedEntityID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a system to be protected by the electronic attack.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ConsentRequired" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) the Activity requires consent to transition from the ENABLED state to an ACTIVE state.  This element is required and shall be TRUE for Activities which require consent.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ConsentState" type="uci:ConsentEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of consent for the Activity.  This element is required for Activities which require Consent.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_BeamGroupType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TxBeam" type="uci:TxBeamType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates current jamming being performed by a specific Beam.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RxBeam" type="uci:RxBeamType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a receive beam in use by EA to perform tracking.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CapabilityCommandType" uci:version="003.000.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureCapabilityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ResourceAllocatorCommandExtension" type="uci:ResourceAllocatorCommandExtensionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates whether a command is for a resource manager or a subsystem. If the element is present, the EWRM receives the command and treats it as "directed" (CapabilityID selected by mission processing) or overridable, according to the enum. The subsystem will ignore the command until the resource manager sends a modified command without the ResourceAllocatorCommandExtension. If field is not included, the command is always interpreted to be for a subsystem (capability/activity).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Emission" type="uci:EA_EmissionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded EA emission.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Activation" type="uci:EA_ActivationEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the activation trigger for the EA.  Reactive EA doesn't become "active" until the associated emitter is detected.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:CapabilityCommandFrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency to be used for the Command.  If omitted, frequency selection is left to the command recipient within constraints of RF_Profiles imposed by RF_ControlCommand, MDF, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProtectedEntityPredictedReturnPower" type="uci:ProtectedAssetReturnPowerType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The ProtectedAsset child element indicates which of the protected assets of the activity are the subject of the child attribute ChangeProtectedAssetPredictedReturnPower. (In order to add or remove protected entities, a new CapabilityCommandType must be utilized.).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ResourceSelection" type="uci:ResourceSelectionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a Shared Antenna and/or AntennaResources to be used for the resulting Activity. This allows Mission Processing to direct an specific antenna, antenna resource type, or antenna resource instance to be used by the resulting Activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CapabilityMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:EA_CapabilityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an installed EA Capability, its configurable characteristics and its controllability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EA_Component" type="uci:EA_ComponentType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a Subsystem Component used to implement one or more EA Capabilities.  An EA Component's characteristics and performance directly influence those of the Capabilities.  A single Component can support multiple Capabilities.  Components may have settings/configuration independent of Capabilities.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="JammedTrackLimit" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The total number of tracks that can be jammed by the Subsystem.  Optional for Subsystems that can jam independent of tracks and/or are limited only by number of beams and commutations.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CapabilityMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_CapabilityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CapabilityOptionsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="InterruptOtherActivities" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) the Capability supports the InterruptOtherActivities element in the EA_Command message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CapabilityStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityStatus" type="uci:CapabilityStatusType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the high level availability/state of a Capability instance.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="RF_Profile" type="uci:RF_ProfileType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a RF Emission Profile currently applied to the Capability.  If omitted, there are no current profiles and the Capability is operating per its defaults and other constraints.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CapabilityStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_CapabilityStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CapabilityType" uci:version="002.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CommandableCapabilityDeclarationType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:CapabilityInitiationEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's first tier type in the EA taxonomy.  For EA, the first tier is an indication of the means of initiation of the Capability.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityOptions" type="uci:EA_CapabilityOptionsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's support for select optional elements in its accepted control interface messages.  Support for these elements is expected to vary across Capability implementations but must be known in order to adapt and configure upstream Systems and Services which use the Capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EA_Indicator" type="uci:EA_IndicatorEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a characteristic of the EA Capability.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  If a program-specific enumerated type is CLASSIFIED, then the documentation defining the enumerated type will be maintained by the classifying program, in accordance with that program's Security Classification Guide (SCG).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Technique" type="uci:EA_TechniqueType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an EA technique supported by the Capability.  Names and implementations of techniques vary widely across EA Subsystems.  This element is an abstraction that describes them from a heterogeneous command and control perspective.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AssociatedComponentID" type="uci:ComponentID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command and control relevant Subsystem Component associated with the Capability.  Only those Components that are independent of the sibling Technique element should be listed; Technique has its own association to Components.  Multiple Capabilities can use the same Component.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageOutput" type="uci:EA_MessageOutputsEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a message that is an output of the Capability.  See enumerated type annotations for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TechniqueGroupIdentifier" type="uci:EA_TechniqueGroupIdentifierType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The technique group is not described in UCI.  It is based on the organization of EA capability and is left to external implementation.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ChangeLocationAndPowerType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Pointing" type="uci:EA_TargetPointingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates where to point for EA beams.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Power" type="uci:EA_PowerType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates power level for EA beams.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CommandMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Command" type="uci:EA_CommandType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an instance of an EA Capability command.  A Capability command message can have multiple command instances to allow a sequence of related commands in a single coherent message.  Each command instance reports status via a separate, independent Capability CommandStatus message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CommandMT" uci:version="003.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_CommandMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CommandResponseType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ProtectedAsset" type="uci:AssetType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an asset to be protected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activation" type="uci:EA_ActivationEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the activation trigger for the EA.  Reactive EA doesn't become "active" until the associated emitter is detected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CommandStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityCommandStatusBaseType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CommandStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_CommandStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_CommandType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:EA_CapabilityCommandType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a new invocation of an EA Capability.  Generally, if accepted, the command will result in one or more new EA Activities being created and reported via the EA_Activity message.  The request/response interaction terminates as soon as the command is accepted or rejected; this element is not used to interact with an "active" command.  Updates and/or additional interaction with the resulting Activity (after the command is accepted) is accomplished via the sibling Activity element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="uci:EA_ActivityCommandType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to modify an existing EA Activity (which was previously reported via the EA_Activity message and was marked as "interactive").  The request/response interaction terminates as soon as the modification is accepted or rejected.  The modifications are reflected in subsequent EA_Activity messages.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ComponentType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ComponentID" type="uci:ComponentID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an EA Component to which an Emission can be assigned.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FieldOfRegard" type="uci:FieldOfRegardType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Azimuth and/or Elevation field of regard of the Component relative to its installation orientation/boresight.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyChangeTime" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Time between frequency changes for the Component.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DutyFactorLimit" type="uci:PercentType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum duty factor of the Component.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BeamLimit" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum number of beams for the Component.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommutationsLimit" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum number of commutations per beam.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Band" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the bandwidth of the Component.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InstantaneousBand" type="uci:FrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the maximum instantaneous bandwidth of the EA component,  This field will only be valid when individual EA "channels" are reported as components.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ConsentRequestMDT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Subsystem requiring Consent for the EA Activity to proceed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConsentRequest" type="uci:EA_ConsentRequestType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a consent request instance.  An EA_ConsentRequest can have multiple consent request instances to allow a sequence of related consent request to be described in a single coherent message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ConsentRequestMT" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_ConsentRequestMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ConsentRequestStatusMDT" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityConsentRequestStatusBaseType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ConsentRequestStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_ConsentRequestStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ConsentRequestType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:RequestBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ProposedEA" type="uci:EA_ProposedType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the details of the proposed EA.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_DetailsAssignedType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ComponentID" type="uci:ComponentID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of an EA component, such as an antenna, which the EA Activity has been assigned to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EA_BeamGroup" type="uci:EA_BeamGroupType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Pairs of Receive and Transmit Beams performing a "Jam". Must choose TxBeam or RxBeam or both.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_DetailsType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Assigned" type="uci:EA_DetailsAssignedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates current jamming being performed by a specific EA Component.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Unassigned" type="uci:EA_DetailsUnassignedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates jamming Activity that hasn't been assigned to a Component.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_DetailsUnassignedType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Emission" type="uci:EA_EmissionType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unassigned jamming emission.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activation" type="uci:EA_ActivationEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether this activity is preemptive or reactive.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ComponentID" type="uci:ComponentID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an EA Component the sibling Emission can be assigned to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_EmissionType" uci:version="003.002.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TechniqueIdentifier" type="uci:EA_TechniqueIdentifierType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the jamming technique.  See type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency of the jamming emission.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Target" type="uci:EA_TargetType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the target of the EA emission.  This element indicates the characteristics of the target which are the focus of the EA.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ChannelAttenuation" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Attenuation applied to the payload port.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_EmitterDataType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the target is being attacked according to Signal/emitter data from a corresponding Entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EmitterType" type="uci:EmitterIdentityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the target is being attacked according to Signal/emitter data associated with its emitter type.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SignalDescription" type="uci:SignalSummaryType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the target is being attacked according to specifically commanded Signal data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SignalID" type="uci:SignalID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the target is being attacked according to a previously detected Signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_EntityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Entity UUID associated with the EA activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TechniqueIdentifier" type="uci:EA_TechniqueIdentifierType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a proposed EA technique.  See type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the EA Capability associated with the proposed EA.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ComponentID" type="uci:ComponentID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the proposed Component which the EA will be assigned to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_PowerType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="PowerAtTarget" type="uci:DecibelType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Power at target In dBW. This will use the center point for calculation if an area or line is selected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ERP" type="uci:DecibelType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Effective Radiate Power in dBW. It is an IEEE standardized definition of directional radio frequency (RF) power transmitted from a theoretical half-wave dipole antenna.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="JtoS" type="uci:DecibelType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jam to Signal ratio In dB. The ratio of the signal strength of the jamming signal (J) to the signal strength of the target return signal (S).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ProposedType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="ActivityID" type="uci:ActivityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ActivityID of the EA_Activity which describes the proposed EA.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Entity" type="uci:EA_EntityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the EntityID and characteristics of the proposed EA activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_ResponseType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="RouteRequirements" type="uci:EA_TaskEscortType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element specifies a task to escort an asset.  The tasked vehicle shall provide protection for the escorted asset.  Additional protected assets can be specified in the ProtectedAssets element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProtectedAssets" type="uci:EA_TaskProtectedAssetsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element provides a list of friendly assets which should be protected in addition to those who are being escorted, if any.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Threats" type="uci:EA_TaskThreatsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threats that are the target of the electronic attack.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_SettingsCommandMDT" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilitySettingsCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="UnassignAll" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to break all current assignments of Activities to resources.  As a result, the resources could be assigned to other Activities, re-assigned to the original Activity or a combination of the two.  Equivalent to simultaneously commanding each current Activity to be Unassigned via the EA_Command message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_SettingsCommandMT" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_SettingsCommandMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_SettingsCommandStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilitySettingsCommandStatusBaseType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_SettingsCommandStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EA_SettingsCommandStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TargetPointingType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="LocationData" type="uci:TargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of or explicit values for geospatial characteristics of the EA target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AirVolume" type="uci:AirVolumeSensorReferencedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the pointing volume for the EA transmission.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TargetType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EmitterData" type="uci:EA_EmitterDataType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of the emitter/signal characteristics that are being used to determine how to electronically attack the emitter target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Pointing" type="uci:EA_TargetPointingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates where to point for EA beams.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Power" type="uci:EA_PowerType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates power level for EA beams.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LastSignalTimestamp" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time at which the target emitter is last known to have transmitted a signal, either by direct receipt by an ESM Capability of the EA Subsystem or via an indication from a messaging input to the EA Subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TaskEscortType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EscortedAsset" type="uci:ProtectedAssetType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the identity and priority of escorted assets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinDistanceOffset" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element indicates the minimum distance the tasked vehicle should fly relative to the escorted asset position.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MaxDistanceOffset" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element indicates the max distance the tasked vehicle should fly relative to the escorted asset position.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RelativeAngleOffset" type="uci:AnglePairType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Angle Relative to the heading of the escorted asset measured clockwise.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RendezvousPoint" type="uci:Point4D_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the location and time for a rendezvous.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TaskProtectedAssetsType" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ProtectAll" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If this element is "TRUE", all known friendly assets should be protected to the extent EA resources are available.  If this element is "FALSE", either:
1.)  A subset of protected assets shall be specified.  This is a requirement if the mission is to loiter and protect.  It is optional if an escort.
2.)  The mission is an escort and only the escorted vehicle or entity should be protected.  In this case, NO protected assets shall be specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SelfProtect" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If this element is set to TRUE, the jamming asset should utilize resources for self protection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProtectedAsset" type="uci:ProtectedAssetAndThreatType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the identity and priority of protected assets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TaskRouteRequirementsType" uci:version="002.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Path" type="uci:PathType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element specifies specific waypoints that the vehicle being tasked should fly.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Loiter" type="uci:LoiterType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the loiter location and pattern from which the tasked vehicle should provide protection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Escort" type="uci:EA_TaskEscortType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element specifies a task to escort an asset.  The tasked vehicle shall provide protection for the escorted asset.  Additional protected assets can be specified in the ProtectedAssets element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ZoneConstraints" type="uci:ZoneChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This specifies the geospatial location zone for the vehicle to execute the EA Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VolumeConstraints" type="uci:VolumeChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This specifies the geospatial location volume for the vehicle to execute the EA Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TaskSuppressionConstraintsType" uci:version="003.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EA_Target" type="uci:EA_TargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element contains the ID of the entity which should be jammed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Priority" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element contains the prioritization of the specified entity.  Priorities are relative to other entities specified in the task.  Absence of this element indicates that the tasked system should determine priorities based on entity type.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TechniqueIdentifier" type="uci:EA_TechniqueIdentifierType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the EA technique to be used for this target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TaskThreatsType" uci:version="003.000.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="SuppressAll" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If true this element implies that all known threats should be jammed to the extent resources are available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SuppressionConstraints" type="uci:EA_TaskSuppressionConstraintsType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines specific constraints on the entities or frequencies to suppress.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TaskType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="RouteRequirements" type="uci:EA_TaskRouteRequirementsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines requirements that must be executed for this electronic attack tasking. This element is optional because the flight path of that a vehicle uses for an Electronic Attack task does not have to be specified in the tasking. In many cases the vehicle will want to create its own route for survivability purposes.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProtectedAssets" type="uci:EA_TaskProtectedAssetsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element provides a list of friendly assets which should be protected in addition to those who are being escorted, if any.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Threats" type="uci:EA_TaskThreatsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threats that are the target of the electronic attack, from which the sibling ProtectedAssets will be protected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TechniqueGroupIdentifierType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an identifier corresponding to a group of EA techniques based on the organization of EA Capability.  The use of Nickname and MDF name is left to the external implementation to organize and identify.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Nickname" type="uci:VisibleString2_4Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The short name assigned to the EA  technique group by the external EA capability planning and designing organization.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MDF_Name" type="uci:VisibleString256Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The MDF file name associated with the technique group.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TechniqueIdentifierType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an ID corresponding to an EA technique.  The use of ForeignKeyType is an indication that EA techniques aren't universally defined and come from multiple systems/sources but they are expected to be unique within the context of their source.  For an EA technique in UCI, the EA_TechniqueIdentifierType.Key element indicates the technique ID and the EA_TechniqueIdentifierType.SystemName element indicates the system that assigned the ID and ensures it is unique.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ForeignKeyType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EA_TechniqueType" uci:version="002.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TechniqueIdentifier" type="uci:EA_TechniqueIdentifierType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the EA technique.  EA techniques are not taxonomically described in UCI.  It is left to external actors to organize, uniquely describe and identify them.  See type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activation" type="uci:EA_ActivationEnum" maxOccurs="2">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates how the technique is activated.  See annotated type enumerations for further details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Pointing" type="uci:EA_PointingEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates how the Technique is pointed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Band" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the bandwidth of the Technique.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ComponentID" type="uci:ComponentID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an EA Component the Technique can be assigned to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Emitter" type="uci:EmitterIdentityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an emitter type which the Technique might be effective against.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpecificEmitter" type="uci:SpecificEmitterIdentityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific emitter type ***instance*** which the Technique might be effective against.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EarthOrientationParametersDataChoiceType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Defines the type that allows a choice of Earth Orientation Parameters data type: EarthOrientatonParameters message or static values.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="EarthOrientationParametersID" type="uci:EarthOrientationParametersID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of the set of EarthOrientatonParameters to use.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StaticValues" type="uci:TimeAndPolarDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The static (non-changing) time and polar motion data to use.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EarthOrientationParametersID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Defines the Earth Orientation Parameters ID.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EarthOrientationParametersMDT" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EarthOrientationParametersID" type="uci:EarthOrientationParametersID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the Earth Orientation Parameters ID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CreationTime" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time at which the EOP was measured, modeled or forecast.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Epoch" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time range within which all of the sibling EOP data is applicable.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Parameters" type="uci:TimeAndPolarRecordType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Includes the Earth Orientation Parameters, one record for each Epoch contained within.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EarthOrientationParametersMT" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EarthOrientationParametersMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Contains data for the Earth Orientation Parameters.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ECEF_AccelerationAccelerationCovarianceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The 1-sigma acceleration-acceleration covariance terms in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system. The covariances are symmetric and therefore the covariance values expressed here are the minimum set.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="AxAx" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The X-X acceleration covariance with units of meters squared per second to the fourth power.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AxAy" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The X-Y acceleration covariance with units of meters squared per second to the fourth power.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AxAz" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The X-Z acceleration covariance with units of meters squared per second to the fourth power.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AyAy" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Y-Y acceleration covariance with units of meters squared per second to the fourth power.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AyAz" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Y-Z acceleration covariance with units of meters squared per second to the fourth power.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AzAz" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Z-Z acceleration covariance with units of meters squared per second to the fourth power.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ECEF_AccelerationType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The Acceleration vector in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system. See the WGS84C_3D world model for details and precise definitions.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="X_Acceleration" type="uci:AccelerationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the X-component of the Acceleration in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Y_Acceleration" type="uci:AccelerationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Y-component of the Acceleration in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Z_Acceleration" type="uci:AccelerationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Z-component of the Acceleration in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ECEF_KinematicsType" uci:version="002.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Provides kinematic information in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system. ECEF is a cartesian coordinate system with an origin located at the center of mass of the Earth, a Z-axis aligned with the rotational axis of the Earth (positive Z in the direction of the North pole), the X-Y plane passing through the equator (positive X in the direction of the Prime meridian, and positive Y in a direction perpendicular to both X and Z to form a right-handed coordinate system). See the WGS84C_3D world model for details and precise definitions.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TimeValid" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Date/Time stamp of the sibling data elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Position" type="uci:ECEF_PositionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the position in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Velocity" type="uci:ECEF_VelocityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the velocity in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Acceleration" type="uci:ECEF_AccelerationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the acceleration in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Orientation" type="uci:OrientationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Euler Angle Sequence describing the orientation of the vehicle in the order yaw, pitch, roll.  The angles are given in the Earth-Centered-Earth-Fixed (ECEF) coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
