					<xs:element name="EEI_ID" type="uci:EEI_ID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>EEI_ID was derived from ACTDF.  EEI_ID is a unique ID to identify an EEI.  It does not use the ACTDF EEI_ID format (EEI_[0-9]+) because UCI standardized on industry standard UUIDs.  If traceability to ACTDF is required, use ACTDF_Traceability or ForeignKeyMap.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EEI_Text" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The essential elements of information associated with a given EEI ID.  For intelligence, there are two types of EEIs, generic and specific.  If generic EEIs are requested, the imagery analysis will report all activity and structures in an area as defined by the commanders' objectives.  Specific EEIs are instructions the targeteer provides to report specific activity/ observation (e.g., general BDA or specific assessment of a critical target.  See the USAF Intelligence Targeting Guide (Pamphlet 14-210, Feb 1, 1998 chapter 2 for more information.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
