		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PlanInputsCoreType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="PlanningCandidate" type="uci:RequirementPlanningCandidateType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates specific Systems to consider and plan for along with System-specific planning constraints.  If omitted, all Tiers and all Systems at and below those that the planning process is applicable to shall be planned.  A System is a planning "candidate" because its plan may or may not change as a result of the command; zero to one Plans per *Plan type will potentially be created for each candidate.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProposedEffectPlan" type="uci:EffectPlanConstraintType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an existing EffectPlan of the System superior to the sibling PlanningCandidates that provides a proposed "Effect deck" to allocate amongst the candidates.  This element can be supplemented with additional Effects from the sibling ProposedEffect element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProposedEffect" type="uci:EffectAllocationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a proposed Effect for the planning process.  An Effect given here is added to any Effects provided in the sibling ProposedTaskPlan to create the full set of Effects to be considered by the planning process.  An Effect given here overrides the same Effect in the sibling ProposedEffectPlan.  An empty list here, combined with no sibling ProposedEffectPlan is considered a command to deallocate previously allocated Effects.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AssociationConstraint" type="uci:RequirementAssociationConstraintType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an association between Requirements that is a constraint on how the Effects are allocated and planned.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="OutputPlanType" type="uci:EffectPlanPartsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates Parts required in the output EffectPlan.  When populated, this element must match or be a subset of the Parts associated with the planning process (sibling PlanningProcessID) as advertised in PlanningFunction*messages.  This element is optional when all Parts of the process are required.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EffectPlanInvalidType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
