	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EntityManagementSetFusionEligibilityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Entity whose fusion eligibility is being changed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FusionEligibility" type="uci:EntityFusionEligibilityEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded eligibility of the Entity given by the sibling EntityID element for automated fusion operations by the Entity's source System/Service and/or fusion tier.  FULL indicates that this Entity, and therefore its contributor Entity or Entities, is fully eligible for future automated fusion operations.  SELECTIVE_EXCLUSION indicates that the Entity or Entities is eligible for future automated fusion operations excluding merging with the Entity or Entities given in the sibling CorrelatedEntity element.  SELECTIVE_INCLUSION indicates that the Entity or Entities are automatically merged with the Entity or Entities given in the sibling CorrelatedEntity element.  NONE indicates that this Entity is not eligible for future automated fusion operations regardless of the associated Entity.  This element does not restrict future operator initiated fusion operations via the EntityManagementRequest.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CorrelatedEntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of an Entity which is excluded or included for future automated fusion operations with the Entity given in the sibling EntityID element.  This element is required when the sibling FusionEligibility indicates SELECTIVE_EXCLUSION or SELECTIVE_INCLUSION and should be omitted otherwise.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EntityManagementSetIdentityType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Entity whose identification is being changed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Identity" type="uci:EntityIdentityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the new Identity to apply.  Omitting a form of Identity here that is in the associated Entity is an indication to leave it unchanged.  Including a form of Identity here replaces that form in the Entity completely and is subject to the rule that included instances should sum to 100%.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EntityManagementSetLink16MetadataType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
