	<xs:complexType name="EW_ConfigurationMDT" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EW_ConfigurationID" type="uci:EW_ConfigurationID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a unique ID assigned to the EW_Configuration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Subsystem whose status is given in the message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RF_Bands" type="uci:RF_BandType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This represents the RF Band or Bands which the subsystem will operate over.  RF bands represent the frequency range that a subsystem can operate over with specific combinations of tuners, antennas, and RF distribution components.
A subsystem typically can operate over several selectable bands, but has to reconfigure to switch bands.  Certain capabilities may be restricted to specific bands.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ChannelDescription" type="uci:ChannelDescriptionType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the RF channel or channels which are used by a subsystem.  The channels are typically defined by tuner characteristics and may be constrained by hardware, firmware, and/or software.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EW_ConfigurationMT" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:EW_ConfigurationMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EW_CoordinationDataLinkIdentifierType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This is a polymorphic extension which allows for the extension of the base DataLinkIdentifierPET. This represents data used to describe the manner in which the relevant message data may apply to an electronic warfare (EW) coordination exchange.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataLinkIdentifierPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="RequestNumber" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Provides an audit trail for responses to electronic warfare coordination requests, which are uniquely identified by a combination of RequestNumber, SourceSystemID, and (if specified) DestinationSystemID.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Response" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates whether this message was produced in response to an electronic warfare coordination request.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SourceSystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>ID of the System that originated the electronic warfare coordination request that is being referenced. Required if the sibling RequestNumber field is populated with a nonzero value.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DestinationSystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>ID of the System to which the referenced electronic warfare coordination request was addressed. If not specified while sibling RequestNumber specifies a nonzero value, the request was addressed to all relevant participants.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="NetworkLinkID" type="uci:NetworkLinkID_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The external network to which this data applies.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="EW_IndexNumberDataLinkIdentifierType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This is a polymorphic extension which allows for the extension of the base DataLinkIdentifierPET. This represents data used to uniquely identify sensor target reports from a particular originator.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataLinkIdentifierPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="IndexNumber" type="xs:unsignedInt">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>A value assigned by the originator to differentiate among sensor target reports.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>ID of the System whose IndexNumber is being reported.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="NetworkLinkID" type="uci:NetworkLinkID_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The external network to which this data applies.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
