					<xs:documentation>Maximum allowable value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FocalPlaneArrayNonUniformityCorrectionReferenceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The reference and offset values for the non-uniformity correction.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NUC_Reference" type="uci:FocalPlaneArrayNonUniformityCorrectionReferenceEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The reference for the non-uniformity correction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NUC_Offset" type="uci:FocalPlaneArrayNonUniformityCorrectionOffsetEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The offset for the non-uniformity correction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FocalPlaneArrayOperationNonUniformityCorrectionType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The correction values for the channel's NUC for a subsystem capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NUC_TablesSettings" type="uci:UnsignedIntegerMinMaxType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The allowable table numbers for the channel's correction values for NUC for this subsystem capability. This element associates to and is set when FPA Channel Operation NON_UNIFORMITY_CORRECTION is available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NUC_ReferenceOffsetSettings" type="uci:FocalPlaneArrayNonUniformityCorrectionReferenceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The allowable reference and offset for the channel's correction values for NUC for this subsystem capability. This element associates to and is set when FPA Channel Operation NON_UNIFORMITY_CORRECTION is available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FOR_Type" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the field of regard (FOR) limits for a passive optical sensor to what it can view from its mounting position on the platform typically due to physical barriers such as sensor window limitations.  Establishes conditions for defined FOR and provide lists of LOS points that allows defining a region relative to the reference position and provide an optional warning threshold when within range of boundaries.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FOR_Type" type="uci:FOR_Enum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates what FOR curve that this series of points and/or warning threshold pertains to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LOS" type="uci:LOS_VariableA_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Azimuth/Elevation position for a point or series of points to allow a FOR curve to be generated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WarningThreshold" type="uci:AnglePositiveType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a minimum angle value to allow a subsystem to figure out all curves based on this value and one additional curve.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForceModelType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Components of the force model for the satellite, independent of the satellite itself.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="GravityModel" type="uci:GravityModelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Gives the name of the spherical harmonic gravity model and the number of zonals (degree) and tesserals (order) to be used. May be omitted when the perturbation is not used for the subject RSO.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AtmosphericDragModel" type="uci:AtmosphericDragModelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Contains the parameters used to define the atmospheric drag model. Examples include the name of the atmospheric density model, space weather data, the ballistic coefficient and first-derivative, and engergy dissipation rate to be used in propagation. May be omitted when atmospheric perturbations are not used for the subject RSO.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SolarRadiationPressureModel" type="uci:SolarRadiationPressureModelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Surface area model and Solar Radiation Pressure coefficient to be used in propagation. May be omitted when Solar Radiation Pressure force model is not used for the subject RSO.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ThirdBodyGravityModel" type="uci:ThirdBodyGravityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The source of celestial body ephemerides as well as the graviational parameters used in propagation. May be omitted when third body perturbations are not used for the subject RSO.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EarthOrientationParametersDataChoice" type="uci:EarthOrientationParametersDataChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the set of Earth Orientation Parameters data to be used for the purpose of propagation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PhysicalModel" type="uci:PhysicalModelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The model used to describe physical characteristics of the RSO, such as mass and area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Maneuver" type="uci:OrbitalManeuverDetailsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A list of maneuvers to be included in the propagation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VCM_ForceModelOptions" type="uci:VCM_ForceModelOptionsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>VCM specific force model options.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyMapDRL" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ForeignKeyMap Data Record List</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataRecordListBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ManagedLists" type="uci:ForeignKeyMapML" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element contains the managed list of ForeignKeyMap data records.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyMapID_Type" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Contains the ForeignKeyMap Data Record List (DRL).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataRecordListID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyMapMDT" uci:version="001.001.000.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ForeignKeyMapDRL">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ForeignKeyMapID" type="uci:ForeignKeyMapID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the mapping.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyMapML" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Contains the managed lists within the ForeignKeyMap message.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ManagedListBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ForeignKeyPairListElement" type="uci:ForeignKeyPairDRLE" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element contains a list of the ForeignKeyMapPair data records.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyMapMT" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:ForeignKeyMapMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyPairDRLE" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Foreign Key Pair Data Record List Entry</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataRecordBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ForeignKeyPairID" type="uci:ForeignKeyPairID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a unique ID assigned to the ForeignKeyPair.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyPairID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to ForeignKeyPairs.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyPairMDT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ForeignKeyPairDRLE">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ForeignKey" type="uci:ForeignKeyType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element represents a key, ID, etc. that exists in another system, protocol, network, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="NativeID" type="uci:ID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element represents the ID from within the UCI protocol that the ForeignKey is related to.  Whereas most elements of type ID_Type infer a specific kind of UCI ID type, this element is intended to refer to any UCI ID type; there is not a "Native" ID type in the UCI schema.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyPairMT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:ForeignKeyPairMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ForeignKeyType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Key" type="uci:VisibleString256Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element contains the value of the ForeignKey.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SystemName" type="uci:VisibleString256Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element refers to the "system" where the ForeignKey is managed.  That system could be another message standard/ protocol, network, database, shared table, etc.  UCI leaves it to implementers to choose and coordinate use of the foreign "system".</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FOV_ActivityType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:FOV_Type">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="GroundFOV" type="uci:PolygonType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the "footprint" of the FOV when projected onto the ground.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FOV_Timestamp" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the timestamp when the sibling FOV elements were valid.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MaximumEffectiveRange" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the maximum range at which the Activity associated with the FOV is still effective.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FOV_ExtentType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Characterizes the FOV extent of the sensor.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="AzimuthExtent" type="uci:AnglePositiveType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Azimuth FOV extent of the sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElevationExtent" type="uci:AnglePositiveType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Elevation FOV extent of the sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FOV_Type" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="LOS" type="uci:LOS_InertialB_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the line of sight from the cone apex to center of the cone's base as referenced to the North-East-Down coordinate frame.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AzimuthWidth" type="uci:AnglePositiveType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates angular width of the cone in the global horizontal plane at the observation point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElevationWidth" type="uci:AnglePositiveType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the angular width of the cone in the global vertical plane at the observation point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FOV_VolumeType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the Field of View of the source.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:AzElRequiredReferenceType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="AzimuthExtent" type="uci:AnglePositiveType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Azimuth FOV extent centered at the sibling Azimuth element. e.g., a 0.5 radian extent for azimuth centered at 0.25 radian would go from 0 to 0.5 radian.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ElevationExtent" type="uci:AngleHalfPositiveType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Elevation FOV extent centered at the sibling Elevation element. e.g., a 0.5 radian extent for elevation centered at 0.25 radian would go from 0 to 0.5 radian.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FrequencyControlType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyRange" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific frequency range to be used for the life of this commanded capability. This Frequency does not override governing RF Profile IDs active for this Capability or the sibling RF Frequency Restriction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ControlOptions" type="uci:CoverageEffortEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates to the RF Payload whether the entire sibling frequency range should be covered with their RF_ResourceAllocationRequest or a best effort to cover as much of the frequency range as possible.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FrequencyDataBaseType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyAverage" type="uci:FrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the average measured frequency of the Signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyMin" type="uci:FrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the lowest measured frequency of the received Signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyMax" type="uci:FrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the maximum measured frequency of the received Signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyLast" type="uci:FrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the last measured frequency of the received Signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyDeviation" type="uci:DoubleNonNegativeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the standard deviation of the value of the measured frequency of the data type.  Estimate (weighted or unweighted) of standard deviation of operating RF. (Values greater than or equal to 0.0.).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyModulationVariation" type="uci:FrequencyModulationVariationEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the variation of the modulation of the Signal's frequency.  See enumerate annotations for further details.  Optional when identification of the modulation is not attempted.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FrequencyDataType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:FrequencyDataBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="AgilityPattern" type="uci:FrequencyAgilityPatternEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the agility pattern driving an agile Signal.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  Optional when identification of the agility pattern is not attempted.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AgilityValues" type="uci:FrequencySwitchingEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the nature of the frequency values driving the pattern used in a Signal with agile frequency modulation.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  Optional when identification of the agility values is not attempted.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AgilityPeriodicity" type="uci:FrequencyPatternPeriodicityEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the repeating nature of the agility pattern of an agile Signal.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  Optional when identification of the agility pattern periodicity is not attempted.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AgileEmitter" type="uci:EmptyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates whether the signal exhibits frequency agility.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SwitchingValues" type="uci:FrequencySwitchingPatternEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the nature of the frequency values used in a Signal with switched (non-agile) frequency modulation.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.  Optional when identification of the switching values is not attempted.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ModulationPatternPeriod" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the measured frequency modulation pattern period for the Signal; the time duration from the beginning of a pattern to the end of the pattern.  This element is expected only for sibling ModulationTypes that are patterned including STAGGER and AGILE.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FrequencyBins" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of frequency bins that were used to collect the Signal.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FrequencyMultiChannelType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NumChannels" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of channels in the signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Spacing" type="uci:FrequencyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency spacing between channels in the signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FrequencyParamsType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The Frequency parameters are in regards to the RF Frequencies to measure.  The min signal strength indicates the lowest threshold of collection. The RF Frequency resolution indicates the granularity of the collection. The frequency range indicates the specific RF band to collect. The optional product resolution time parameter is the minimum amount of time needed to get the desired level of resolution for the product.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyRange" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the minimum and maximum frequencies to collect.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinSignalStrength" type="uci:MilliwattPowerRatioType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the threshold level of the collection.  It is the power referenced to one milliwatt in units dBm.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RF_FrequencyResolution" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the desired resolution of the signal in the band of the expressed frequency.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductResolutionTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The optional product resolution time parameter is the minimum amount of time needed to get the desired level of resolution for the product.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FrequencyRangeType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Min" type="uci:FrequencyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the minimum or lower frequency in the frequency range. This can also indicate the frequency at the start of the pulse. If the frequency range is actually a discrete single frequency, this element and the sibling Max element should be equal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Max" type="uci:FrequencyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the maximum or upper frequency in the frequency range. This can also indicate the frequency at the end of the pulse.  If the frequency range is actually a discrete single frequency, this element and the sibling Min element should be equal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FrequencySetType" uci:version="001.000.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Modeled after SensorSpecificData in the ACTDF standard.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyRange" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates frequency or frequencies, expressed by either a single frequency, frequency range, or any multiple and combination of the two.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Modulation" type="uci:ModulationEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="62">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the signal modulation. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Encrypted" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies whether or not the signals are encrypted.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultiChannel" type="uci:FrequencyMultiChannelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element indicates a multiple channel signal.  If this optional field is omitted, the signal is single channel.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Content" type="uci:RF_SignalContentEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the signal content.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FuelCenterOfGravityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the center of gravity of a fuel system.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ActualCoG" type="uci:CenterOfGravityAeroType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the actual lateral and vertical center of gravity in meters and longitudinal center of gravity in percent mean aerodynamic chord.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DesiredCoG" type="uci:CenterOfGravityAeroType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the desired lateral and vertical center of gravity in meters and longitudinal center of gravity in percent mean aerodynamic chord.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LateralCenterOfGravityTrendEnum" type="uci:LateralCenterOfGravityTrendEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The position the center of gravity is moving towards along the lateral axis.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LongitudinalCenterOfGravityTrendEnum" type="uci:LongitudinalCenterOfGravityTrendEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The position the center of gravity is moving towards along the longitudinal axis.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VerticalCenterOfGravityTrendEnum" type="uci:VerticalCenterOfGravityTrendEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The position the center of gravity is moving towards along the vertical axis.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FuelSubsystemExtendedStatusType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Abstract extension for Fuel Subsystem Specific Status.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SubsystemExtendedStatusPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="FuelCenterOfGravity" type="uci:FuelCenterOfGravityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Center of gravity data for fuel subsystem at current and desired.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="RefuelingStatus" type="uci:RefuelingStatusType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Refueling data only needed when actively refueling.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FuelTankComponentExtendedStatusType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the remaining fuel in the tank by quantity or by percentage. Also give status on temperature of the fuel.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ComponentExtendedStatusPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="FuelQuantity" type="uci:MassType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the amount of fuel for the tank.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FuelPercent" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the percent of fuel remaining compared to the total capacity of the tank.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Temperature" type="uci:TemperatureType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the current temperature of the fuel tank.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PumpData" type="uci:PumpComponentExtendedStatusType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the pump by providing pressure, temperature, flow rate, flow direction, recirculating, line data, and/or valve data.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FuelUsageType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates fuel usage.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Fuel" type="uci:MassType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The measure of fuel used in kg.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Percent" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the percent of fuel used from a full system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FunctionalDamageConfidenceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DamagedFunctionType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Confidence" type="uci:DamageConfidenceEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates Overall confidence the damage described has occurred.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FunctionalDamageProbabilityType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DamagedFunctionType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Probability" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Probability that the damage above will occur.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FunctionID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type that refers to an aggregation of Subsystems.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsMDT" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>System to which the settings apply.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ServiceID" type="uci:ServiceID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Service to which the settings apply.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StalenessThresholds" type="uci:EntityStalenessThresholdsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines thresholds for determining the staleness of data.  Multiple instances of this element which vary temporally or geospatially are possible.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MergeAndDropSettings" type="uci:FusionSettingsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates settings that control how Entity fusion behaves in terms of merge, split, drop.  These settings apply to all "fusion eligible" Entities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InputSource" type="uci:FusionSourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a contributing source to fusion and details of how it is allowed to contribute.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsMT" uci:version="002.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:FusionSettingsMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsRequestMDT" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:RequestBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="RequestType" type="uci:FusionSettingsRequestType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Defines the type of request to perform for the Fusion Service configuration.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>One or more Systems to which the request applies. If omitted, the request applies to all Systems.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ServiceID" type="uci:ServiceID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>One or more Services to which the request applies. If omitted, the request applies to all Services (or all services within the system specified by the sibling SystemID element).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsRequestMT" uci:version="002.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:FusionSettingsRequestMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsRequestStatusMDT" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:RequestStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The system ID responding to the request.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ServiceID" type="uci:ServiceID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The service ID responding to the request.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsRequestStatusMT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:FusionSettingsRequestStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsRequestType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="SetStalenessThresholds" type="uci:EntityStalenessThresholdsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines thresholds for determining the staleness of data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SetMergeAndDropSettings" type="uci:FusionSettingsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates settings that control how Entity fusion behaves.  These settings apply to all "fusion eligible" Entities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SetInputSources" type="uci:FusionSourcesType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a request that configures the contributing sources to fusion and details of how they are allowed to contribute.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSettingsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SplitAllowed" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) fusion is allowed to split/unmerge contributors that were merged in as a result of a "merge" EntityManagementRequest.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RemergeAllowed" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) fusion is allowed to remerge to an Entity contributors that were previously unmerged from the same Entity as a result of a "split" EntityManagementRequest.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RespawnAllowed" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) fusion is allowed to create a new output Entity from a contributor that was previously the subject of a "drop" EntityManagementRequest.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSourcesType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Source" type="uci:FusionSourceType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a fusion source and its input settings.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FusionSourceType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SourceType" type="uci:EntitySourceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the fusion input source type which the sibling Enabled element applies to.  UNKNOWN source type indicates the setting applies globally across all source types.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SourceSystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific System which the sibling Enabled element applies to.  This further filters/constrains the sibling SourceType element to apply only for the System given by this element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Enabled" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether the fusion input source described by the sibling elements is (or is commanded to be) enabled (TRUE) or disabled (FALSE) as a fusion input.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AllowedUpdates" type="uci:FusionUpdatesEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of updates fusion can perform on fused data using data from the fusion source described by the sibling elements.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InitiateAllowed" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether fusion is allowed to initiate a new fusion Entity based solely on data from the fusion source described by the sibling elements (TRUE) or not allowed (FALSE).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FuzeTriggerType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="FuzeDistance" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Weapon fuze distance setting applies to proximity and hydrostatic fuze modes.  Hydrostatic values will be negative to denote subsurface.  Proximity values will be positive to denote height of burst above ground or distance to the target depending on the fuze's sensing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FuzeDelayTime" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Weapon fuze delay time setting; applies to impact and time fuze modes.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="FuzeType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Weapon fuze mode and setting. See operational handbooks and TTP manuals for allowable fuze modes and settings.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FuzeTrigger" type="uci:FuzeTriggerType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates information for fuze height of burst and fuze delay time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FuzeMode" type="uci:WeaponFuzeModeEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Fuze modes defined here are derived from operational handbooks and TTP manuals.  Impact is a type of fuze designed to function upon impact or after delay. The time delay (if any) is measured from the instant
of impact. The proximity fuze is a miniature Doppler radar set. The lag time between transmission and reception is precomputed and translated into selectable burst height values in altitude above the target. In a time fuze, the delay is initiated at bomb release from the aircraft and not at the instant of impact. The hydrostatic type of fuze is employed in depth bombs for underwater demolition work.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FuzePosition" type="uci:WeaponFuzePositionEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>For weapons with multiple fuzes, indicates which fuze the sibling elements apply to.  Optional for weapons with a single fuze.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Mnemonic" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The name of the fuze.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FuzeSeparationArmTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This indicates the time at which the fuze will arm after separating from the aircraft.  Prior to that time, the fuze will not detonate, even if a fuze trigger is hit.  This prevents fragmenting the vehicle if the weapon blows back into the aircraft or if it is flying very low.  Once the fuze separation arm time elapses, the fuze is armed and the weapon is hot, it will detonate when the fuze trigger hits.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
