	<xs:complexType name="IR_ImageParamsType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The Infra-red Image parameters describe the desired images to collect.  The spectral frequency indicates the size of the wavelength to collect. The temperature resolution is amount of temperature variance to measure. The optional Ir Image setting indicates the range of the IR frequency to measure.  The optional product resolution time parameter is the minimum amount of time needed to get the desired level of resolution for the product.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SpectralFrequencyResolution" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The spectral frequency resolution is the desired resolution of the size of the light wavelengths to collect.

Note: The spectral frequency resolution is traditionally measured in angstroms (10-10 m). The DistanceType is in meters: Visible light wavelengths are in the range of 4000-7000 Angstroms (4.0*10-7 - 7.0*10-7 m). Normal values for this parameter would be between 0.0000004 and 0.0000007.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TemperatureResolution" type="uci:TemperatureType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the desired resolution on the temperature of the collection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="IR_ImageSetting" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is an optional parameter of the minimum and maximum of the infrared spectrum to collect if it indicated.  Without this parameter the entire IR spectrum is collected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductResolutionTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The optional product resolution time parameter is the minimum amount of time needed to get the desired level of resolution for the product.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
