	<xs:complexType name="MA_ActionCommandType" uci:version="003.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:MA_ActionCapabilityCommandType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a new invocation of an Action Capability. Generally, if accepted, the command will result in one or more new Action Activities being created and reported via the ActionActivity message. The request/response interaction terminates as soon as the command is accepted or rejected; this element is not used to interact with an "active" command. Updates and/or additional interaction with the resulting Activity (after the command is accepted) is accomplished via the sibling Activity element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="uci:MA_ActivityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to modify an existing Action Activity (which was previously reported via the ActionActivity message and was marked as "interactive"). The request/response interaction terminates as soon as the modification is accepted or rejected. The modifications are reflected in subsequent ActionActivity messages.</xs:documentation>
