					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeActivityRank" type="uci:ComparableRankingType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change the rank of the Activity.  This is not a means of modifying the rank of the original source of the Activity (Capability Command, Task, etc.).  It is a means of modifying the Subsystem assigned rank of the Activity reported in the associated Activity message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeActivityState" type="uci:CapabilityCommandStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change the state of the Activity.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DeleteActivity" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to delete the Activity.  It is equivalent to a sticky disable command.  A deleted Activity can't be re-enabled, including by an automated Capability that was the original source of the Activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="UnassignActivity" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to break the Activity's current assignment to Subsystem resources, thereby making them available for other Activities per the Subsystem resource allocation and scheduling.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeEngagement" type="uci:MA_EngagementParametersType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change the engagement parameters corresponding to an ongoing tactic or activity in general. Note: an update to the number of missiles per contact applies to all targets assigned in the tactic. For changing individual targets' recieved missiles, see fields in the sibling ChangeActionConstraints</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ChangeActionConstraints" type="uci:MA_ActionConstraintType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change action constraints for the ongoing interactive Action. This could be used to update, remove, and/or change shot allocations for the targets or information about targets in an ongoing tactic or activity in general. Modifications are target centric. The implementing system or service can determine how best to allocate targeting changes. Number of shots changes can be indicated by checking the TargetObjectConstraints' Behavior</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
