	<xs:complexType name="MA_DDS_DataLinkNativeInfoType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This is a polymorphic extension which allows for the extension of the base DataLinkNativeInfo type for DDS connections.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataLinkNativeInfoPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Domain" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Specifies the DDS Domain ID to publish on. If not set the default Domain ID setup in the gateway will be used.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TopicName" type="uci:VisibleString256Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The unique topic name to use. If not set, the topic name will equal the message name (minus the MT) or the topic specified in the wrapper message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TopicPublishSubscribe" type="uci:MA_TopicPublishSubscribeEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If set, DDS will set up the connection for publishing, subscribing, or both on the topic and it will override the associated IER setting. If not set, the associated IER is used with EGRESS=publish, INGRESS=Subscribe, and BOTH=Pub_and_Sub.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TopicQosReliability" type="uci:MA_MessageReliabilityEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If set to Best Effort or Reliable, the DDS publisher/subscriber will use the Quality of Service (QoS) Reliability setting as specified for the associated topics. If set to NONE or not set, either the associated DeliveryProtocol is used or the ICD specified method is used to determine the QoS Reliability Setting.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TopicQosKeepLast" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If TRUE, upon reconnect the last message published will be sent out to a subscriber. This will configure the DDS publisher with the Keep Last QoS setting. This should only be done for status and some data type messages and it should not be used for commands, requests, or requirement messages that could cause issues with the receiving system. This provides a nice way for status messages to be delivered specifically for messages that are non-periodic.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TopicQosPriority" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If Empty, the IER Priority is used. In DDS, the higher the value, the higher the priority. Therefore the IER Priority would need to be inverted or mapped.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TopicPartition" type="uci:VisibleString256Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This field can be used to create partitions on a topic.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="DirectMessagingAllowed" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If TRUE, allows for sending Specific Destination messages to/from SystemIDs using the Systems UUID as the topic name. If FALSE, the whole wrapper message will be sent on a topic of the wrapper messages name and an IER would filter messages as needed.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
