		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CommandID" type="uci:EffectPlanCommandID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The ID of the Effect Plan Command. Used to reference the command when providing status.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ParentPlanCommandID" type="uci:EffectPlanCommandID_ChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the *PlanCommand which this EffectPlanCommand originated from. For example, an EffectPlan sent to a System might have as a parent the EffectPlanCommand sent from the operator/commander one level above to the Effect planner at that level.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommandState" type="uci:CommandStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The state of the command message data. Indicates if a command message is a NEW command, an UPDATE to an existing command, or a CANCEL of an existing command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Inputs" type="uci:EffectPlanInputsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates data and references to other messages and their data to be used to create the EffectPlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ForPlanningUseOnly" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>When TRUE, indicates the *Plan is to be used only for intermediate planning purposes. It will eventually be replaced/superseded by another *Plan or be discarded/abandoned. *Plans with this flag should only be used when explicitly referenced by other messages. These *Plans should never: trigger functionality, be subject to approvals, be activated, etc.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
