			<xs:element name="Subject" type="uci:MA_ExecutionPriorityTypeChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the specific task or action associated with the list item.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Rank" type="uci:ComparableRankingType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Used to compare different items (Tasks and Actions). This is accomplished by first comparing two ComparableRankingTypes' priority values. In the event of the items having equal priority values the precedence values are then compared. For example, Task A has a (priority, precedence) value pair of (4, 10), Task B has a (priority, precedence) value pair of (4, 23), Task C has a (priority, precedence) value pair of (7, 2): the ranking order would be first Task A, then Task B, then Task C. Since Task A and Task B have the same relative priority value, Task A will be ranked before Task B because Task A has a higher relative precedence value. Task C will be ranked after Tasks A and B because it has a lower relative priority value than Tasks A and B.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
