					<xs:documentation>Direction of turn when rounding the first loiter point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LegSpecification" type="uci:MA_HoldLegSpecificationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the length of the hold based on the inbound leg.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TurnSpecification" type="uci:MA_HoldTurnSpecificationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the turns of the hold.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Duration" type="uci:MA_OrbitDurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the duration of the hold.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EntryType" type="uci:MA_HoldEntryTypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specified method for entering the hold.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MA_HostileActIntentType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="HostileRegion" type="uci:MA_RegionChoiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The ID(s) of an OpZone/OpVolume or specified zone(s) for which entrance by an Entity can be considered a Hostile Act/Intent if the entity is not a Friend/Neutral and has a Positive Enemy Indicator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="HostileOpZoneOpVolumeCategory" type="uci:MA_OpZoneCategoryEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This can be used to identify the Types of OpZones or OpVolumes for which entrance by an Entity can be considered a Hostile Act/Intent if the entity is not a Friend/Neutral and has a Positive Enemy Indicator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="HostileThreatPostureType" type="uci:ThreatPostureEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Select all that apply to categorize what is considered Hostile Act/Intent of an Entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="HostileThreatActivity" type="uci:ActivityByType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the "activity" of the Entity that is considered a Hostile Act/Intent. "Activity" is derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUIs 1798/001, 1798/002, 1798/003, 1798/004 and 1798/005 for additional details. "ActivityCategory" is Derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUI 275/004 for additional details. Each environment has a corresponding set of specific types.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MA_HSA_CSA_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message shall be used to provide the ability to command a new flight vector to the Platform.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Altitude" type="uci:AltitudeReferenceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Altitude hold value to be achieved and reference to altitude measurement source.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Speed" type="uci:PathSegmentSpeedType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines speed type (reference frame) for all speed related fields in this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Direction" type="uci:MA_DirectionChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines heading or course type and reference to hold.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MA_IdMatrixCriteriaType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>These markers are used to identify an Entity as a Friend, Neutral, or Enemy and which enables or confirms the Entity's Standard Identity type to be set to FRIEND, NEUTRAL, SUSPECT or HOSTILE.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FriendIDs" type="uci:AssetType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is a list of known friend IDs. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FriendElectromagneticIndicators" type="uci:MA_ElectromagneticIndicationChoiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>These markers are used to identify an Entity as a Friend. If any of them are met this enables or confirms the Entity's Standard Identity type to be set to FRIEND.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FriendElectromagneticIndicatorsConfidence" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the threshold percentage that above this number is enough confidence to confirm the Electromagnetic Indicator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NeutralIDs" type="uci:AssetType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is a list of known Neutral IDs.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NeutralElectromagneticIndicators" type="uci:MA_ElectromagneticIndicationChoiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>These markers are used to identify an Entity as a Neutral. If any of them are met this enables or confirms the Entity's Standard Identity type to be set to NEUTRAL.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NeutralElectromagneticIndicatorsConfidence" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the threshold percentage that above this number is enough confidence to confirm the Electromagnetic Indicator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FriendNeutralProceduralIndicators" type="uci:MA_ConstraintPriorityTypeChoiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>An Entity in these OpLine, OpZone, OpVolume types are a procedural indicator that it is likely a Friend or Neutral. This cannot be used alone to indicate Friend or Neutral.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PositiveEnemyIndication" type="uci:MA_PositiveEnemyIndicationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>These markers are used to identify an Entity as an Enemy or enables confirmation that the Entity's Standard Identity type can be set to SUSPECT. Need at least one Enemy Electromagnetic Indicator (EEI) or one Visual Identification (VID) to have a positive Enemy Indication.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="HostileActIntentCriteria" type="uci:MA_HostileActIntentType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>These markers are used to identify that an Enemy has qualified for a Hostile Act (HA) or Hostile Intent (HI). The Entity must also have at least one Positive Enemy Indicator and one Hostile Act/Intent which enables or confirms the Entity's Standard Identity type to be set to HOSTILE. </xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
