	<xs:complexType name="MA_LeadershipMetricsMDT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PackagePartnerMetrics" type="uci:MA_PartnerMetricsType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the leadership fitness metrics for the partners in the package.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PackageLeaderElectionMethod" type="xs:int">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies which election method/algorithm the package will utilize for electing a Package Leader. Implementors are expected to set a default election method. If blank, the default election method will be used.

Integer values and corresponding elections methods are as follows: 

0 - Bully Election Method. Supports Dynamic Fitness Scores and cases where Leadership Fitness Scores need to be shared as part of an election process.
1 - Static Fitness Score Election Method. Supports nomination of a leader assuming leadership fitness scores remain static once they have been defined by MP/C2.
2 - Maximum Consensus Election Method. Supports utilizing consensus algorithms to reach team consensus on the leader while preserving communication bandwidth.
3 - Raft Leader Election Method. Supports leader election using the Raft consensus algorithm, which ensures a distributed and fault-tolerant approach to electing a leader.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
