	<xs:complexType name="MA_NURBS_ControlPointType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specifies a single point and weighting factor in a Non-Uniform Rational Basis Spline (NURBS) trajectory description.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ControlPoint" type="uci:Point2D_RelativeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the value of a single control point for the trajectory curve. To reduce the chance of discontinuities in the curve description, the frame of reference for each point is an Azimuthal Equidistant Projection (AEP) offset from a center reference point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Weight" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the weight factor used for this control point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MA_NURBS_PointType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specifies a Non-Uniform Rational Basis Spline (NURBS) representation of the platform trajectory to this endpoint. The following constraints should be observed when specifying the trajectory: A) A third-order curve should be sufficient for accurate description and higher orders add complexity without significant benefit, B) The curve description should be terminated at both endpoints and C) the curve should be continuous to first and second order across the path segments for the active route.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CenterReference" type="uci:WayPointPointChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the reference point from which the control points for the trajectory curve are defined. The frame of reference for the control points is specified as Azimuthal Equidistant Projection (AEP) to prevent discontinuities that a LLA (latitude, longitude, altitude) frame of reference may experience at the antipodes.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ControlPoints" type="uci:MA_NURBS_ControlPointType" minOccurs="4" maxOccurs="10">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Contains the collection of control points that with the knot vector describe the desired trajectory for this endpoint. Minimum size value is defined to ensure this endpoint is continuous with the rest of the route path. Maximum size value is defined for a third-order curve.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="KnotVector" type="uci:DoubleNonNegativeType" minOccurs="4" maxOccurs="14">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Contains the collection of knots that with the control points describe the desired trajectory for this endpoint. The number of knots is directly related to the number of control points and the order of the curve. The minimum size value is defined to ensure this endpoint is continuous with the rest of the route path. The maximum size value is defined for a third-order curve.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CurveTraversingParameters" type="uci:MA_CurveTraversingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Choice of Speed or Duration constraints to apply to curve following</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Curvature" type="uci:DoublePositiveType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the curvature value for the desired trajectory. This is an indication of the smoothness of the trajectory.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InitialControlPointIndex" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Index into the ControlPoints array that indicates the initial control point for this path segment trajectory description. To ensure a continuous route path, this value should be identical to the endpoint of the previous segment in this path.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FinalControlPointIndex" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Index into the ControlPoints array that indicates the final control point for this path segment trajectory description. To ensure a continuous route path, this value should be identical to the endpoint of this path segment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MA_ObjectShotCountChoiceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
