		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ManeuverConstraintsChoiceType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates choices for sensor collection maneuver constraints.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="BasicManeuverConstraints" type="uci:BasicManeuverConstraintsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>BasicManeuverConstraints are used for situations when looking for a maneuver, but there is nothing to drive expectations on maneuver size or direction.  Max delta-V is required to bound search space and Min to bound the sensor and processing resolution for maneuver detection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PredictedManeuverConstraints" type="uci:OrbitalManeuverDetailsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>PredictedManeuverConstraints is used when there is information on the nominal parameters of an expected maneuver (such as a vector of delta-V values, maneuver duration, and maneuver start time). Since the maneuver has not happened, these are nominal and the actual maneuver may vary in start time, duration, and velocity parameters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ManeuverDetectionType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Input parameters for an orbital surveillance maneuver detection task type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ManeuverConstraints" type="uci:ManeuverConstraintsChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maneuver constraints in support of sensor collects for maneuver detection of either a basic maneuver (where the maneuver size or direction cannot be predicted) or a predicted maneuver.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ExpectedManeuverWindow" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>ExpectedManeuverWindow is used to define the window over which the maneuver might occur.  Note that this is required in addition to the PredictedManeuverConstraints' StartEpoch and Duration, since those values are for the nominal maneuver and the ExpectedManeuverWindow covers the potential for variation from the predicted nominal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VelocityMetricResolution" type="uci:SpeedType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>VelocityMetricResolution relates to the desired ability for tasked sensors to detect differences in velocity from a pre-maneuver orbit.  This might be used for real-time detection of maneuvers (in contrast to detection through orbit-fitting).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ManeuverMultiStandardType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the maneuver in terms of the domain specific choice.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="OrbitManeuver" type="uci:OrbitManeuverType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The kinematics for this sequence of the orbit plan associated with a maneuver.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RouteManeuver" type="uci:RouteType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The route type associated with a maneuver.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ManeuverSummaryType" uci:version="002.001.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>A summary record of the planned, actual and final outcome of the maneuver.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ExpectedManeuver" type="uci:OrbitalManeuverDetailsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides information on what was planned for the maneuver.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualManeuver" type="uci:OrbitalManeuverDetailsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides the actual details of this maneuver.  This may be different from the expected due to, for example, environmental influences.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NominalManeuverProbability" type="uci:UnitIntervalDoubleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Calculated value that the maneuver was nominal, with 1 being maximum likelihood that maneuver was nominal and 0 indicating a non-nominal maneuver.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PostManeuverKinematics" type="uci:OrbitKinematicsParametersType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides kinematics information of the spacecraft's new orbit as a result of the maneuver.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MDF_CommandSubCategoryType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubCategoryID" type="uci:MDF_SubCategoryID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID associated with the MDF subcategory.  The child DescriptiveLabel should indicate a human readable description of the subcategory that distinguishes it from others in the same MDF.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FileID" type="uci:MDF_SubCategoryFileID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the active or commanded file associated with the MDF subcategory.  For a given subcategory, only one file can be active or commanded at a time.  The child DescriptiveLabel should indicate a human readable description of the file that distinguishes it from others in the same subcategory.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MDF_CommandType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded Mission Data File (MDF).  An MDF is a collection of data, organized into files, that is used to tailor, configure or otherwise affect the behavior of a Capability.  MDFs can vary from mission to mission or even by phases of a single mission.  They are generally developed in pre-mission planning and are unique for each Subsystem model.  Their content is not standardized by UCI, but the mechanism for advertising their availability and activating them is.  Their content is abstracted by the UCI concept of Capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MDF_ID" type="uci:MDF_ID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID associated with the MDF.  The child DescriptiveLabel should indicate a human readable description of the MDF that distinguishes it from others associated with the same Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubCategory" type="uci:MDF_CommandSubCategoryType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a subcategory of files that make up the MDF.  When an MDF is "active", at most one file from each subcategory can be active.  The subcategory concept allows a variety of MDF structures across Capability types and manufacturers.  For an ESM Capability, example subcategories could be "scan files" and "emitter ID files".  For an EA Capability, an example is "jam files".  This element is optional to support Capabilities or Subsystems whose MDF isn't decomposed into individually selectable categories and files.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MDF_FileType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FileID" type="uci:MDF_SubCategoryFileID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a file associated with the MDF subcategory.  For a given subcategory, only one file can be active or commanded at a time.  The child DescriptiveLabel should indicate a human readable description of the file that distinguishes it from others in the same subcategory.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FileStatus" type="uci:MDF_StatusEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the state/status of the MDF File.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MDF_ID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
