			<xs:element name="InterrogatorIdentifier" type="uci:InterrogatorIdentifierType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Interrogator ID (legacy address type): used for transponder lockout interactions</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SurveillanceIdentifier" type="uci:SurveillanceIdentifierType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Surveillance Identifier (modern address type): lockout interactions</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ModeS_OptionsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ModeS_InterrogatorAddress" type="uci:ModeS_InterrogatorAddressType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Mode S Interrogator Address.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ShortP4Enable" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Additional Pulse transmitted with Mode 3/A and Mode C Interrogations to prevent responses from Mode S Capable transponders. That information is obtained through Roll Calls for Mode S transponders.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ModeS_Type" type="uci:IFF_ModeS_SupportEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Mode S Types.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpecificBDS_Registers" type="uci:SpecificBDS_RegistersType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specific BDS Registers.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AllCallEnable" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>With All Calls enabled, the interrogator will actively transmit All Call interrogations to acquire targets new to the surveillance volume. When disabled, the interrogator will rely on ADS-B squitter to initiate Mode S tracks and track solely with Roll Calls.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LockoutEnable" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>When enabled, targets that have been acquired and are being interrogated using Roll Calls will no longer reply to All Calls from this interrogator's II or SI Code. Lockout expires on the transponder after 18 seconds.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LockoutOverrideEnable" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>In the event that two nearby platforms have interrogators with the same II or SI Code, lockout initiated on a target by one platform can prevent detection of that target from the other platform since Roll Calls from the first platform command the transponder not to reply. When enabled, this control will command the transponder to respond to All Calls regardless of the Lockout Command received in Roll Calls.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MixedModeLockoutEnable" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Some older tranponders only recognize Interrogator Addresses with II Codes, which use 4 of the 7 bits used to define SI Codes in the RF transmission. When  this control is enabled, the interrogator will be allowed to lockout the non-SI transponders using the apparent II Code. When disabled, the interrogator cannot lock out those older transponders. Note that Lockout is commanded in Roll Call Interrogations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MaxPOR" type="uci:MaxPOR_Enum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the maximum Probability of Reply for Mode S All Call interrogations. In the event that two nearby aircraft both respond to each All Call interrogations from an interrogator, responses can be garbled preventing the interrogator from detecting replies from one or both transponders. When set to values of "1 in 2" or lower ("1 in 4", "1 in 8", etc.), each transponder will apply the specified probability to whether they respond to a specific interrogation, and over the course of several interrogations, there will be replies from one transponder without the other enabling the interrogator to identify each transponder's Aircraft Address. The interrogator can then continue into Roll Call interrogations where each transponder is uniquely interrogated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ModifyRF_ThreadInstanceType" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="RF_ThreadInstanceIndex" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifier of the RF_ThreadInstance associated with the resource allocation. ResourceAllocator generates the index in a an incrementing fashion 1, 2, 3... at resource allocation time, assuring that identifiers are unique across resource allocations. RF_ThreadInstanceIndices may be re-used after an allocation has been de-allocated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActiveBeamInstanceIndex" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>When a centralized Beam Manager provides the steering, the ActiveBeamInstanceIndex indicates which of the defined steer points is to be used. ResourceAllocator generates BeamInstanceIndices at allocation time, and the BeamManager sets Active BII to one of the allocated BIIs when steering updates occur.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ResourceAccessPriority" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>New Resource Access Priority to be assigned to the RF Thread Instance Index. This is a positive ordinal integer value used to define arbitration priority for accesses to Shared Antenna Resources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BeamInstance" type="uci:SetupBeamConfigurationInstanceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This must match the resource definition in the resource allocation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RF_Gain" type="uci:RF_GainType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="2">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Gain of the RF path associated with the sibling System Thread. Multiplicity of 2 is to allow the transmit path to be different than the receive path gain.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ModRateDataType" uci:version="000.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:DataRateDataType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ModType" type="uci:ModulationEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the Modulation type of the signal.  See enumerated type annotations for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ModulationOnPulseDataBaseType" uci:version="000.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MOP" type="uci:ModulationEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a form of modulation detected in the Signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FMOP" type="uci:FMOP_Enum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency modulation on pulse measurement status/results for the Signal.  If omitted, no attempt to measure FMOP has been made for the Signal.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PMOP" type="uci:PMOP_Enum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the phase modulation on pulse measurement status/results for the Signal.  If omitted, no attempt to measure PMOP has been made for the Signal.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ModulationOnPulseDataType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ModulationOnPulseDataBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="FMOP_Span" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the measured time duration over which the frequency is modulated for a full pulse width.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FMOP_Range" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the measured FMOP excursion. This may be the full frequency excursion exhibited by the Signal or a fraction thereof depending upon the timing of specific measurements.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PMOP_BitDuration" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the time for a single bit in a phase shift keyed pulse.  The element is only expected when the sibling PMOP element indicates phase shift keying.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PMOP_Sequence" type="uci:PMOP_SequenceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates details regarding the phase modulation sequence.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ModulationParameterType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a custom modulation parameter that is not covered by other elements in the Signal data structure.  This will typically be used to fully cover the fields defined in other interoperability standards such as the JICD.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ModulationParameterIndex" type="uci:VisibleString64Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the index element of the index/value pair, and can be the name of the field as used in other standards.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ModulationParameterValue" type="uci:VisibleString64Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the data element of the index/value pair.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MSTGTA_RevA_Type" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TGT_NUM" type="uci:NITF_TargetNumberType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Preplanned Target Number for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_NUM: initialized at 00001; =00000 if segment is n/a; =99999 if manually tasked. Optional since might be populated downstream from UCI source.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_Identifier" type="uci:VisibleString12Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Designator of Target for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_ID from first 12 chars of ACTDF Target Name. Default is all spaces.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_BE" type="uci:VisibleString15Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Basic Encyclopedia ID / OSUFFIX of target for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_BE from ACTDF BE Number = 10-char BE # proper + optional 5-char O-Suffix.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_PRI" type="uci:NITF_TargetPriorityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Preplanned Target Priority for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_PRI from ACTDF Task Priority: 1 = top priority, 999 = lowest priority.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_REQ" type="uci:VisibleString12Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Target Requester: Identification of authority requesting targets image for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_REQ from ACTDF Originator field.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_LTIOV" type="uci:MSTGTA_TGT_LTIOV_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Target's Latest Time Information of Value for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_LTIOV from ACTDF Collection Time Window.Latest. This element contains the date and time, referenced to UTC, at which the information contained in the file loses all value and should be discarded. The date and time is in the format CCYYMMDDhhmm in which CCYY is the year, MM is the month (01–12), DD is the day of the month (01 to 31), hh is the hour (00 to 23), mm is the minute (00 to 59).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_TYPE" type="uci:SingleDigitStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Preplanned Target Type for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_TYPE from ACTDF:
0 = point
1 = strip
2 = area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_COLL" type="uci:SingleDigitStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Preplanned Collection Technique for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_COLL from Ground Station operator. This is a mandatory field for this TRE. Values are:
0 = vertical
1 = forward oblique
2 = right oblique
3 = left oblique
4 = best possible.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_CAT" type="uci:NITF_TargetCategoryCodeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Target Functional Category Code from DIAM-65-3-1 for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_CAT from ACTDF. The five-character numeric code with values between 10000 to 99999 classifies the function performed by a facility.  The data code is based on an initial breakdown of targets into nine major groups, identified by the first digit:
1 Raw Materials
2 Basic Processing
3 Basic Equipment Production
4 Basic Services, Research, Utilities
5 End Products (civilian)
6 End Products (military)
7 Places, Population, Government
8 Air and Missile Facilities
9 Military Troop Facilities
Each successive numeric character, reading from left to right, extends or delineates the definition further.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_UTC" type="uci:TGT_UTCStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Planned Time to arrive at Target for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_UTC from various ACTDF Start Times. Format is hhmmssZ: hh = Hours, mm = Minutes, ss = Seconds, Z = UTC time zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_ELEV" type="uci:ElevationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Target Elevation, -01000ft to +30000ft MSL or -305m to +9144m. Planned elevation of point target. For strip and area targets, this corresponds to the average elevation of the target area. Measured in feet or meters, as specified by TGT_ELEV_UNIT. For the NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_ELEV field; from ACTDF, as HAE coordinates. Use NGA's GEOTRANS or similar to translate from HAE to MSL.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_ELEV_UNIT" type="uci:MeterUnitLetterStringType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Unit of Target Elevation for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_ELEV_UNIT. Note: While NITF allows units in feet and meters, UCI and ACTDF allow meters only.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_LOC" type="uci:MSTGTA_TGT_LOC_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See simple type documentation. Target Location for NITF TRE MSTGTA TGT_LOC from ACTDF Look-at coordinates. Planned latitude/longitude of corresponding portion of target. Location may be expressed in either degrees-minutes-seconds or in decimal degrees. The format ddmmss.ssX represents degrees (00 to 89), minutes (00 to 59), seconds (00 to 59), and hundredths of seconds (00 to 99) of latitude, with X = N for north or S for south, and dddmmss.ssY represents degrees (000 to 179), minutes (00 to 59), seconds (00 to 59), and hundredths of seconds (00 to 99) of longitude, with Y = E for east or W for west. The format ±dd.dddddd indicates degrees of latitude (north is positive), and ±ddd.dddddd represents degrees of longitude (east is positive).  NOTE: Patterns below equate to ddmmss.ssXdddmmss.ssY and  ±dd.dddddd±ddd.dddddd.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MSTGTA_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TGT_NUM" type="uci:NumericSpaceString6OnlyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A number assigned to each preplanned target, initialized at 00001.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_PRI" type="uci:NumericSpaceString4OnlyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The priority of the preplanned target. 1 = top priority, 999 = lowest priority.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_LTIOV" type="uci:NumericSpaceString13OnlyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The mission target Latest Time Information of Value. This element contains the date and time, referenced to UTC, at which the information contained in the file loses all value and should be discarded.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_COLL" type="uci:NumericSpaceString2OnlyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The preplanned collection technique:
0 = vertical
1 = forward oblique
2 = right oblique
3 = left oblique
4 = best possible.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_CAT" type="uci:MSTGTA_TGT_CAT_String_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Target Functional Category Code from DIAM-65-3-1.  The five-character numeric code classifies the function performed by a facility.  The data code is based on an initial breakdown of targets into nine major groups, identified by the first digit:
1 Raw Materials
2 Basic Processing
3 Basic Equipment Production
4 Basic Services, Research, Utilities
5 End Products (civilian)
6 End Products (military)
7 Places, Population, Government
8 Air and Missile Facilities
9 Military Troop Facilities
Each successive numeric character, reading from left to right, extends or delineates the definition further.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TGT_UTC" type="uci:MSTGTA_TGT_UTC_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The planned time to arrive at the target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MTI_ActivityStatusBaseType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Set of metrics used to describe the progress of an activity (sensor collection). This base type is intended to be reused across multiple domains.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NumberOfTimesSearched" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Integer value of the number of times a volume has been completely searched for this activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeLastSearched" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the actual completion time for the last complete search of the volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Attempts" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>For the duration of this activity, this is the number of times a volume has attempted to be searched completely, sanitized or the number of times the radar has attempted to acquire the cue.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualRevisitPeriod" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>For a volume search, this is the average calculated amount of time between revisits of any part of the volume, for a track update activity this is the average revisit rate achieved against the target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PercentageInFOR" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If the radar is field of regard limited, this is the percentage of the volume that is currently in the radar FOR.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualStartTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the first time at which this activity utilized front end resources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualStopTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the last time at which this activity utilized front end resources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PercentSearched" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This represents the current percentage of the volume that has been successfully searched during the current attempt (as represented in the Attempts field).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EntitiesReported" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is an indication of the number of current entities have are being reported as a result of this activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CueAcquired" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indication that the radar has successfully acquired the target that was identified as the cue.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConcurrentActivity" type="uci:ConcurrentCollectionDetailsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the activity IDs and time windows of activities which ran concurrent with this activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PercentOccluded" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the percentage of the target collection area was occluded as by masking.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PercentRadarTimeline" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the percentage of radar timeline which is taken up by this MTI activity. The Revisit Rate and Time to Service both affect this metric. For instance an Activity might execute frequently and require a long Time To Service, meaning it would take up much radar timeline.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PercentageInFOV" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the percentage of the volume that is currently in the radar FOV. The field of view is defined as the area where the radar can immediately see. The field of regard is defined as the area the radar can see after mechanical movement or rotation. Generally, the FOV is a subset of the FOR.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RelativeDirectionOfTarget" type="uci:RelativeDirectionEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether target is on left or right side of the platform.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MTI_ActivityStatusDetailType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Collection metrics used for describing the progress of an activity (sensor collection) being performed by a MTI sensor.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MTI_ActivityStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="EstimatedERP" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Maximum estimated Effective Radiated Power (ERP) at the face of the array used for this activity attempt. If this attempt requires multiple beam positions, then this is the maximum estimate across all positions.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProductsProduced" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Count of how many products have been produced as a result of this activity.  This does not include messages (e.g. Entity) produced.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="HitsReported" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This is an indication of the number of hits that are currently being reported in a 4607 or raw MTI data product format.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EstimatedPerformance" type="uci:EstimatedPerformanceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="5">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Estimated performance of the activity. The multiplicity is limited to N-1 options where UNKNOWN is an environment type that has no value, thus removed from list of available options.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TargetAreaScanned" type="uci:AreaChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This array of points should be used to define the actual area that can be covered if only a portion of the requested area can be scanned currently (possible result of the application of a policy).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TimeToService" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the amount of time that is needed for a single visit/service of the Target area. This is different from Revisit Period, since other Activities are not taken into account when calculating this metric.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AverageTimeToService" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the amount of time that is needed for a single visit/service of the Target area. This is the arithmetic mean of Service times over the last N visits, where N is an arbitrary number of visits greater than 1.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MTI_OpZoneFilterAreaType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element represents a filtered area for raw Moving Target Indicator (MTI) measurements.  This type extends the base OpZoneFilterAreaPET to provide generic MTI parameters. Specialized MTI will have an extended type for additional parameters.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:OpZoneFilterAreaPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MinimumTargetCountInDwell" type="xs:int" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the minimum number of targets geographically constrained to this area.  If the filter area is defined as an inclusion zone then both MinimumTargetCountPerDwell and
MaximumTargetCountPerDwell can both be set.  Targets that remain after geographic filtering are applied to this parameter.  If the number of targets is less than the parameter MinimumTargetCountPerDwells they are excluded. If the filter area is defined as an exclusion zone then only one of MinimumTargetCountPerDwell and MaximumTargetCountPerDwell can be set. Targets that remain after geographic filtering are applied to this parameter.  If the number of targets is less than or equal to the MinimumTargetCountPerDwell then the targets are excluded.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MaximumTargetCountInDwell" type="xs:int" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the maximum number of targets geographically constrained to this area.  If the filter area is defined as an inclusion zone then both MinimumTargetCountPerDwell and
MaximumTargetCountPerDwell can both be set.  Targets that remain after geographic filtering are applied to this parameter.  If the number of targets is greater than the parameter MaximumTargetCountPerDwells they are excluded.  If the filter area is defined as an exclusion zone then only one of MinimumTargetCountPerDwell and MaximumTargetCountPerDwell can be set. Targets that remain after geographic filtering are applied to this parameter.  If the number of targets is greater than or equal to the MaximumTargetCountPerDwell then the targets are excluded.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MinimumSNR" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the minimum Signal to Noise (SNR) value (DB).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MaximumSNR" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the maximum Signal to Noise (SNR) value (DB).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MinimumRCS" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the minimum Radar Cross Section (RCS) value (DB).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MaximumRCS" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the maximum Radar Cross Section (RCS) value (DB).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MinimumRadialVelocity" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the minimum target radial velocity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MaximumRadialVelocity" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the maximum target radial velocity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Job" type="xs:int" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the specific Job Identifier.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MTI_PredictedActivityDetailType" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ActivityState" type="uci:ActivityStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current state of the Activity state machine. See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityReason" type="uci:CannotComplyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates details regarding the reason for and/or a contributing factor to the sibling ActivityState element. This element is only expected when the Activity is in a potentially undesirable state such as constrained, failed or completed with less than optimum results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPercentageOccluded" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If the radar is line-of-sight limited, this is the percentage of the target that is currently in the radar FOR and not visible due to terrain occlusion.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RevisitIndex" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Integer value of which revisit of a specific target these metrics estimate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedRevisitPeriod" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is an estimate of what revisit rate will likely be achieved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPercentageInFOR" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If the radar is field of regard limited, this is the percentage of the target that is currently in the radar FOR.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedStartTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the estimate of the time at which this revisit will first gain access to the front end timeline to perform the requested collection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedStopTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the estimate of the time at which this revisit will complete the collection and no longer require access to the front end.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedERP" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum estimated Effective Radiated Power (ERP) at the face of the array used for this activity attempt. If this attempt requires multiple beam positions, then this is the maximum estimate across all positions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPerformance" type="uci:EstimatedPerformanceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="5">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Estimated performance of the activity. The multiplicity is limited to N-1 options where UNKNOWN is an environment type that has no value, thus removed from list of available options.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConcurrentExecutionAssumed" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Flag to communicate whether or not the model assumed that concurrent execution was assumed in the model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedSweepTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimate of the time for the sweep to be performed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedTargetAreaScanned" type="uci:AreaChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If the whole GRCA cannot be scanned, this is an estimate of the bounds of what was scanned.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MTI_STANAG_4607_OpZoneFilterAreaType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element represents a filtered area for raw STANAG 4607 measurements. This type extends MTI_OpZoneFilterAreaType to provide Moving Target Indicator (MTI) parameters specific to STANAG 4607.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MTI_OpZoneFilterAreaType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="TargetClassification" type="uci:STANAG_4607_TargetClassificationEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="32">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the target classification. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="STANAG_4607_Mission" type="uci:STANAG_4607_MissionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Filter on the STANAG 4607 mission characteristics.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PlatformType" type="uci:STANAG_4607_PlatformTypeEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="41">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Field M3 from the STANAG 4607 Mission Packet. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MTI_TargetClassType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="MTI_TargetClass" type="uci:MTI_TargetClassEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the class of the Moving Target Indicator (MTI) cross-section. Specific quantitative cross section values associated with these target classes are defined outside of this schema.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ForeignClass" type="uci:ForeignKeyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the foreign class of the target for which the estimate applies.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultiObjectType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Input parameters for an orbital surveillance multi-object task type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CSO_Clearing" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Flag indicating if this Task is for closely spaced object clearing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinSeparation" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>For multi-object scenarios, including a deployment, the minimum distance between objects that needs to be resolved to address the need.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BreakupCharacterization" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Flag indicating to collect data to characterize the spread of objects after a breakup.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultiObjectVerification" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Flag indicating to verify the existence of multiple objects and that the object count matches the number specified in the combination of primary and secondary targets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CSO_GeometricCharacterization" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Flag to look for objects in the vicinity of the primary (if no secondaries specified) and provide information on relative geometries between any secondaries and the primary.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultiObjectMetric" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Flag to indicate requirement to provide distinct position (and velocity, as possible) measurements on each object (with separate identifiers for each object) when multiple objects are in close proximity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticEmitterDataID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the emitter data corresponding to this message.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticEmitterDataMDT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticEmitterDataID" type="uci:MultistaticEmitterDataID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the corresponding emitter data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticEmitter" type="uci:MultistaticEmitterType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the characteristics of the emitter(s) used as a source for passive detection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticEmitterDataMT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:MultistaticEmitterDataMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticEmitterID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the specified emitter.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticEmitterType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the characteristics of the emitter(s) used as a source for passive detection.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticEmitterID" type="uci:MultistaticEmitterID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the specified emitter.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Waveform" type="uci:EmitterWaveformDataType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of or explicit values for emitter characteristics of the emitter used as a source for passive detection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Location" type="uci:EmitterTargetLocationDataType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Source emitter location. Used if Waveform does not contain location.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticModeOptionsEmployedType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the Multistatic Mode settings.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticModeStatus" type="uci:MultistaticModeStatusEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates when the capability is operating in bistatic or multistatic radar mode (ENABLED) and when not to (DISABLED).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticEmitterDataID" type="uci:MultistaticEmitterDataID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the emitter data corresponding to this activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticModeType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the Multistatic Mode settings and associated data to be used for the command.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticModeActivation" type="uci:MultistaticModeActivationEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates when to operate in bistatic or multistatic radar mode (ENABLE) and when not to (DISABLE).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticEmitterDataID" type="uci:MultistaticEmitterDataID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the emitter data corresponding to this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MultistaticOptionsSupportedType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the multistatic options supported by the Capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticEmitterDataRequired" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether emitter data is required (TRUE) or not required (FALSE) to perform multistatic operations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultistaticOnly" type="uci:EmptyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>When present, indicates the Capability will only have the ability to perform multistatic operations. When not present, indicates the Capability has the ability to perform both multistatic and monostatic operations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MunitionInFlightType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TimeToActive" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Delta time in nano seconds until munition seeker activation. Assume seeker is active if time is zero or negative.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeToAutonomous" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Delta time in nano seconds until the munition is fully autonomous and able to guide without data link or external target designation. Assume munition is autonomous if time is zero or negative.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeToImpact" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Delta time in nano seconds until the munition impacts the target based on its current target estimate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MustFlyLocationType" uci:version="002.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the must-fly location is an Entity,  This is typically an overflight location with the desired altitude determined by the service design.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OpPointID" type="uci:OpPointID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the must-fly location is an OpPoint.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OpLineID" type="uci:OpLineID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the must-fly location is an OpLine.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OpZoneID" type="uci:OpZoneID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the must-fly location is an OpZone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OpVolumeID" type="uci:OpVolumeID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the must-fly location is an OpVolume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Point" type="uci:Point3D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the must-fly location is a geospatial point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ZoneTarget" type="uci:ZoneExternalType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Use of the Zone Target implies that a vehicle must enter the zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LineTarget" type="uci:LineTargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Use of the Line Target implies that a vehicle must fly through a corridor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VolumeTarget" type="uci:OpVolumeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Use of the Volume Target implies that a vehicle must enter the volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="MustFlyType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
