			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PathSegmentID" type="uci:SegmentID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element indicates the PathSegmentID of the next PathSegment in the Path.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="NITF_PackingPlanPET" abstract="true" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The base Polymorphic Extension Type (PET) used by NITF packing plan types.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="NITF_PackingPlanRevA_Type" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This is a revised NITF_PackingPlan rectifying the problems identified in NITF_PackingPlanType. It is a tailored reproduction of data definitions included in NITF 2.1 as described in MIL-STD-2500C, MIL-STD-2500B Notice 2, and companion appendices STDI-0002 Compendium Nov 2000 and IPON v1.0_01 August 2007. These data must flow from Task or Command source to recipient so that the recipient can populate the resulting Products with this data to enable PED and other functions. Under most circumstances, UCI doesn't reproduce other standards "in-band", in UCI messages.  An exception is made in this case because to do otherwise would disrupt C2 and PED.
NOTES:
1) Annotations for these fields specify where the source data can be obtained from an ACTDF message. But note that tasking can come in other forms such as target deck spreadsheets, email, chat, operator GUIs, etc.
2) The NITF Basic Character Set - Alphanumeric (BCS-A) is all ASCII characters between SPACE and TILDE show as patterns herein as "[ -~]",
2) The NITF Extended Character Set - Alphanumeric (ECS-A), is a subset of the Extended Character Set (ECS). Valid ECS-A character codes range from 0x20 to 0x7E, and 0xA0 to 0xFF but Line Feed (0x0A), Form Feed (0x0C) and Carriage Return (0x0D) are not valid ECS-A characters. This range is expressed herein in patterns as "[ -~ -ÿ]". Because of inconsistencies between standards, it is strongly advised that character codes ranging from 0xA0 to 0xFF should never be used. Therefore, the use of ECS-A characters should be restricted to its BCS-A Subset.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:NITF_PackingPlanPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="FileHeader" type="uci:FileHeaderRevA_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used in the file header of NITF imagery products. This structure was defined to support MIL-STD-2500B for NITF v2.1. Additional classification information is provided in the task/command message.  NOTE: All fields of the NITF File Header may occur no more than once. Only the FileSecurityClassification field is mandatory, but File Classification must be present if FSCLAS is T, S, C, or R, and hence any of the remaining security markings are present.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ImageSubheader" type="uci:ImageSubheaderRevA_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>NITF Image Subheader fields: Information to be used in the image subheader of NITF imagery products. This structure was defined to support MIL-STD-2500B for NITF v2.1.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ACFTB" type="uci:ACFTB_RevA_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>NITF TRE Aircraft Information Revision B - Information to be used for populating the Aircraft Information Revision B (ACFTB) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MSTGTA" type="uci:MSTGTA_RevA_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>NITF TRE Mission Target Information - MSTGTA provides information from the collection plan associated with the image, and should identify specific targets contained within the image (however, due to collection geometry, a referenced target may not actually correspond to the area contained in the image). Use of MSTGT is optional. The format and description of the user-defined fields of MSTGTA are given in table 8-16. As many as 256 instances of this data extension may occur in each NITF image segment.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="NITF_PackingPlanType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type is a tailored reproduction of data definitions included in NITF as described in MIL-STD-2500C and companion Appendices.  This data must flow from Task or Command source to recipient so that the recipient can populate the resulting Products with this data to enable PED and other functions.  Under most circumstances, UCI doesn't reproduce other standards "in-band", in UCI messages.  An exception is made in this case because to do otherwise would disrupt C2 and PED.  NOTE: This version of the NITF_PackingPlanType suffers from the following problems: Most elements are one space longer than allowed by NITF; some elements' lengths are off by more, short or long; many TREs and elements are extraneous (set by platform, not needed in UCI Task message), while other required tasking authority fields are missing; and many fields are free text that could be restricted by regular expressions to meet NITF standards. The new variants of the PackingPlanPET resolve these problems for MIL-STD-2500A, B, C.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:NITF_PackingPlanPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="FileHeader" type="uci:FileHeaderType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used in the file header of NITF imagery products.  This structure was defined to support MIL-STD-2500C for NITF v2.1.  Additional classification information is provided in the task/command message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ImageSubheader" type="uci:ImageSubheaderType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used in the image subheader of NITF imagery products.  This structure was defined to support MIL-STD-2500C for NITF v2.1.  Security information is expected to match the information provided in the File Header.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ACFTB" type="uci:ACFTB_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used for populating the Aircraft Information Revision B (ACFTB) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AIMIDB" type="uci:AIMIDB_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used for populating the Additional Image Identification Revision B (AIMDB) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EXPLTB" type="uci:EXPLTB_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used for populating the Exploitation Related Information Revision B (EXPLTB) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MPDSRA" type="uci:EmptyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used for populating the Exploitation Related Information Revision B (EXPLTB) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PATCHB" type="uci:PATCHB_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used for populating the Exploitation Related Information Revision B (EXPLTB) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MSTGTA" type="uci:MSTGTA_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used for populating the Mission Target Revision A (MSTGTA) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SECTGA" type="uci:SECTGA_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="250">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Information to be used for populating the Secondary Target Revision A (SECTGA) tagged record extension (TRE) as defined by the Compendium of Controlled Extensions (CE). Size of list is based on the number of allowed SECTGA extensions that can exist in a single NITF file.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="NormalizationTableType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Used for associating an actual metric with its normalized value.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ActualMetricValue" type="xs:float">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Actual performance value (i.e. 100nm for range). X-axis of interpolation table.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NormalizedMetricValue" type="uci:UnitIntervalFloatType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Normalized values for the sibling Actual metric value normalized to a 0 to 1 range. Y-axis of interpolation table.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="NotificationBaseType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates parameters for both Entity and System notification messages. This includes the notification's ID, the notification's current state, the timestamp, the source of the notification, the severity of the notification, the asset that the notification applies to (if applicable), and a notification narrative for a human operator.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NotificationID" type="uci:NotificationID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NotificationState" type="uci:NotificationStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current state within an enumerated state machine that characterizes the life cycle of a notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Timestamp" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The time at which the Notification was originally triggered (ex: event time).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Source" type="uci:NotificationSourceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the originating source of the Notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Severity" type="uci:NotificationSeverityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the overall severity of the notification.  Informational notifications are meant to provide informational context of events.  Indicates the existence of a hazardous condition requiring immediate action to prevent loss of life, equipment damage, or abortion of the mission. Critical notifications indicate the need for immediate attention.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AppliesTo" type="uci:SubjectType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an Asset that the Notification applies to and/or is affected by.  Optional when the Notification characterizes the Subject without regard for Assets it might affect.  Omission of this element doesn't necessarily mean the Notification isn't applicable to an Asset.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NotificationNarrative" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Human readable message for display to an operator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="NotificationID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to a notification.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="NotificationSourceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Identifies the System, as well as the Service, Subsystem, or Capability that originated this notification.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the system that originated the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ServiceID" type="uci:ServiceID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the specific service within the system that originated the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the specific subsystem within the system that originated the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the specific capability within the system that originated the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OperatorID" type="uci:OperatorID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>UUID of the operator associated with this notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OB_CorrelationInputType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the input that was correlated to the SOB with the results described in the sibling elements.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an Entity which was an input for xOB correlation.  Generally only one is given.  Multiple instances are possible if the Entity is a fused and its contributors are also considered in xOB correlation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a System which was an input for xOB correlation.  Generally only one is given.  Multiple instances are possible if the System is a fused and its contributors are also considered in xOB correlation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SignalID" type="uci:SignalID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Signal which was an input for EOB correlation.  Generally only one is given.  Multiple instances are possible if the Signal is associated with an Entity or SignalReport which were considered collectively in EOB correlation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SourceType" type="uci:EntitySourceEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="28">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of System and/or Service which created the sibling correlation input or inputs.  See enumerated type annotations for further details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Exercise" type="uci:MessageModeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the sibling input message or messages had an exercise indication. See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OB_SensorID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to order of battle sensors.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OB_SensorIdentityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Mobility" type="uci:MobilityEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the mobility type of the Sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Environment" type="uci:EnvironmentEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the operational environment of the sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OB_SensorType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SensorID" type="uci:OB_SensorID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The unique ID for an OB sensor record.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Identity" type="uci:OB_SensorIdentityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the identity characteristics of the sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FieldOfRegard" type="uci:FieldOfRegardType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the field of regard for the OB sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FieldOfView" type="uci:SensorFieldOfViewType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the field of view for the OB sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VisualMagnitudeLimits" type="uci:VisualMagnitudeLimitsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the limiting visual magnitude limits.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PrimaryApertureDiameter" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the size of the primary aperture.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Resolution" type="uci:AnglePositiveType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the pixel resolution of the sensor in units of radians/pixel.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Kinematics" type="uci:KinematicsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the geospatial kinematics (fixed or mobile) of the sensor associated with the EOB record.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OrbitalKinematics" type="uci:EntityEphemerisBasisChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orbital kinematics of the sensor associated with the EOB record.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ObjectCorrelationType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Describes the correlation of objects.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CorrelationIndicator" type="uci:CorrelationIndicatorEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether the correlation was performed by an object with C2 responsibility.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OldReferenceIdentifier" type="uci:IdentityKindInstanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the previous identification information for the object correlated with the currently identified object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ObjectInstanceDamageEstimateType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="DamagedObject" type="uci:DamagedObjectType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the damaged object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FunctionalDamage" type="uci:FunctionalDamageProbabilityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Details on that damage estimated for the Object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="HumanDamage" type="uci:DamagedHumanType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>List of any human damage associated with the object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DamageCause" type="uci:DamageCauseEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The estimated source of the damage.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DamageNarrative" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>General free text to handle specific details of the damage that cannot be covered in the other elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_ID" type="uci:DMPI_ID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates which DMPI will damage the object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ObjectKinematicsChoiceType" uci:version="003.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="InertialState" type="uci:InertialStateType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the inertial state of the object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OrbitKinematics" type="uci:OrbitKinematicsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates one of the four types of kinematics options to describe the object's motion.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ObjectTypeDamageEstimateType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ObjectType" type="uci:DamageObjectClassType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates information for identifying the object as a platform, entity, or human.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DamageType" type="uci:DamageType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of damage being summarized.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProbabilityZone" type="uci:DamageProbabilityZoneType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a geo-spatial zone and a range of probability that the damage given in the sibling DamageType element will occur.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DamageCause" type="uci:DamageCauseEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The estimated source of the damage.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DamageNarrative" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>General free text to handle specific details of the damage that cannot be covered in the other elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ObservationCountsByHourType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the hour of day (00-23) and the number of observations during that hour.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Hour00Count" type="xs:unsignedInt">
