	<xs:complexType name="OperatorNotificationMDT" uci:version="003.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="OperatorNotificationID" type="uci:OperatorNotificationID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Unique ID of this operator notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OperatorNotificationTemplateID" type="uci:ID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ID of a notification template for populating the content of the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OperatorNotificationTemplateParameters" type="uci:VisibleString32Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>List of parameters used as substitution arguments when applying notification templates. If a notification template syntax defined a substitution token (e.g. $#) in the Title, the template parameters would be used to replace those tokens. For example, given a template Title of "System $1 violated zone $2" an OperatorNotification that applies that template would replace the $1 token with the first template parameter and the $2 with the second template parameter.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Title" type="uci:VisibleString256Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Brief description of an operator notification. This human readable field will be provided to the operator as a summary of the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Details" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Detailed human readable message for display to an operator.  This is not to be interpreted by a machine. This information may be provided to an operator when they seek a more detailed description of a notification than what the title provides.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Category" type="uci:NotificationCategoryEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Categorizes this notification for purposes of organization and filtering.  It is expected that the service function providing the notification can be represented by this category.  For instance, if a mission planning service is reporting a notification regarding a task, it should report PLANNING as the category, not TASKING.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Severity" type="uci:NotificationSeverityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the overall severity of this notification.  Informational notifications are meant to provide informational context of events within the system.  Indicates the existence of a hazardous condition requiring immediate action to prevent loss of life, equipment damage, or abortion of the mission. Critical notifications indicate the need for immediate operator attention.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Location" type="uci:Point2D_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the geolocation of the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Source" type="uci:NotificationSourceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Source identifiers of the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Actions" type="uci:OperatorNotificationActionType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Actions the originator of the notification will execute or may execute based on operator action commands.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Count" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Occurrence count of this notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OccurrenceTimestamp" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Timestamp of when the notification event occurred. If the event has been repeated, this will contain the time of the most recent occurrence.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Priority" type="xs:unsignedByte" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Optional priority of the notification. This may be used for ordering alerts on the HMI. Higher priority values take precedence over lower ones. A common range is [0,100] with priority 100 notification being the highest priority available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AuralAlert" type="uci:AuralAlertType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Audible definition assigned to the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Destinations" type="uci:OperatorRoleType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Destinations for this notification. This field defines which Operator consoles are responsible for displaying or processing the alert. The Operator consoles can be specified as an Operator console role or by a non-Operator role. If this element is absent, the notification should be handled by all Operator consoles.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssociatedMessage" type="uci:AssociatedMessageType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a message that is associated with or the cause of the operator notification.  This element should be omitted if an input message was not the cause of the notification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
