						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpPointMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OpPointMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpPointPositionType" uci:version="001.002.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Position" type="uci:KinematicsFixedPositionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a geospatial position of a point with an optional estimate of uncertainty.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Velocity" type="uci:Velocity2D_UncertaintyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a velocity of a point with an optional estimate of uncertainty.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="HAE_Adjustment" type="uci:DistanceOffsetType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Difference in meters between the MSL and HAE altitudes of an object. MSL + HAE_Adjustment = HAE, per MIL-STD-6016.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpPointReferenceType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="StoredObject" type="uci:GeoLocatedStoredObjectType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The state of an object when an emergency is reported. This data is stored  to keep data about an object with an emergency after the object is dropped in the event that the lifetime of the emergency extends past the lifetime of the object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StoredObjectRef" type="uci:GeoLocatedObjectType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The state of an object when an emergency is reported. This data is referenced when the lifetime of the object will persist for the duration of the emergency being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DataLinkObject" type="uci:DataLinkIdentifierPET">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Object used when not known in UCI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpRoutingID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to op routing messages.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpRoutingMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="OpRoutingID" type="uci:OpRoutingID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The unique identifier of the set of routing constraints during operation associated with this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DefaultBlueSeparation" type="uci:SeparationParametersType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates default minimum geospatial separation to be maintained when planning or analyzing routes or manually navigating.  The separation is between the planned/navigated route and other routes or conflicting items.  This is the default separation.  It can be overridden in specific cases by the sibling element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DefaultRedSeparation" type="uci:SeparationParametersType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates default minimum geospatial separation to be maintained when planning or analyzing routes or manually navigating.  The separation is between the planned/navigated route and other routes or conflicting items.  This is the default separation.  It can be overridden in specific cases by the sibling element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpecificBlueSeparation" type="uci:SpecificBlueSeparationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines parameters to use when deconflicting blue player routes or generating routes to ensure proper separation from other blue players. These parameters apply at the vehicle type level. For example, these parameters would be used to define how close a mission planned vehicle could get to another fighter jet.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpecificRedSeparation" type="uci:SpecificRedSeparationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines parameters to use when deconflicting blue player routes or generating routes to ensure proper separation from other red players. These parameters apply at the vehicle type level. For example, these parameters would be used to define how close a mission planned vehicle could get to another fighter jet.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OpDescription" type="uci:OpDescriptionType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the name and description of the set of associated routing constraints.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>One or more Systems to which the routing constraints apply. If omitted, the constraints apply to all Systems.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ApplicableZone" type="uci:ZoneType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the geospatial zone in which the routing constraints apply.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Schedule" type="uci:ScheduleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time schedule during which the routing constraints apply.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MissionTraceability" type="uci:MissionTraceabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allows the creator of this zone to specify what the source or motivation for this zone originated from.  This could be ATO, ACO, etc.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpRoutingMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OpRoutingMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpsClockDayType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The consolidated operational schedule AKA Ops Clock: the seven days of the week with the corresponding 24 hour of counts of observations.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="DayOfWeek" type="uci:WeekdayEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The day of the week that this operational schedule is for/was observed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ObservationCountsByHour" type="uci:ObservationCountsByHourType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The day of the week that this operational schedule is for/was observed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpticalCollectionConstraintsType" uci:version="001.000.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type is used to specify a set of constraints that constrain when a PO or AO sensor can start collecting the requested image data.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CollectionConstraintsType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SunElevAngles" type="uci:AngleHalfPairType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The angle from the target plane at intersection of the optical line of sight with the earth's surface at the time of the first image line.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SunAzimuthAngles" type="uci:AnglePairType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The angle from True North clockwise (as viewed from space) at the time of the first image line.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SweepSpeed" type="uci:SpeedType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The rate at which the sensor look-point moves across the terrain.  This is only applicable to area or line targets.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="GimbalOrientation" type="uci:GimbalOrientationPairType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The orientation of the gimbal with respect to its reference frame.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpticalImageParamsType" uci:version="000.002.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The optical image parameters consist of the overall desired image resolution.

The optional ProductResolution provides guidance on the color depth and horizontal and vertical pixel counts.

The optional product resolution time parameter is the minimum amount of time needed to get the desired level of resolution for the product.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ImageResolution" type="uci:ResolutionMetersPerPixelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the meters per pixel of the image.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductResolution" type="uci:ProductResolutionType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This indicates the imagery product resolution in horizontal and vertical pixels and color depth on the service.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductResolutionTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The optional product resolution time parameter is the minimum amount of time needed to get the desired level of resolution for the product.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpVolumeID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to an OpVolume.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpVolumeKinematicsType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the reference point kinematics for an OpVolume expressed in one of several kinematics frames/standards.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PointChoice" type="uci:PointChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies a location either as a geospatial location or a location relative to a separately defined reference frame.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Velocity" type="uci:Velocity2D_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a velocity of a zone/region.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpVolumeMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:OpBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="OpVolumeID" type="uci:OpVolumeID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element represents the unique identifier of the OpVolume associated with this message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Category" type="uci:OpZoneCategoryEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element indicates the type of volume.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CategoryUniqueData" type="uci:OpZoneCategoryType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Contains parameters unique to certain OpZoneCategoryEnum values.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Volume" type="uci:OpVolumeType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element represents the  characteristics of the operational volume.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SituationalAwareness" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Volume used only for situational awareness.  Not used for planning purposes.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpVolumeMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OpVolumeMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element represents the details regarding the operational volume.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpVolumeType" uci:version="003.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>An operational volume comprises a three dimensional region of space.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="GeometricVolume" type="uci:GeometricVolumeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element describes a 3-dimensional geometric volume (e.g. sphere, cone, etc.) using kinematics to describe the zone's position in space.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GeocentricVolume" type="uci:GeocentricVolumeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Describes a 3-dimensional WGS-84 ellipsoid. For example, geocentric volumes can be used to include space objects in keep-in zones or to exclude space objects in keep-out zones.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OrbitRegime" type="uci:OrbitRegimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an orbital regime which are mostly altitude-based in which the space object will reside including optional indication of the class of orbits as secondary descriptions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OrbitAltitude" type="uci:OrbitAltitudeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an orbit altitude range that describes a region in space.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Qualitative" type="uci:OrbitQualitativeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element includes other qualitative types of regions in space such as space weather related zones.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpZoneCategoryType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Container for parameters that are unique to a specific enumeration in OpZoneCategoryEnum.  For example, KeepIn enumeration can have amplifying information such as entry and exit restrictions of the zone.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="ConstrainedEntryExit" type="uci:ConstrainedEntryExitType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines boundaries which applicable Systems can only enter and exit through defined edges.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FilterArea" type="uci:OpZoneFilterAreaPET" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the OpZone can be a zone filter type.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Jamming" type="uci:OpZoneJammingType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the OpZone is a jamming control zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="KeepIn" type="uci:IngressEgressType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines boundaries to which applicable Systems must stay inside.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MissileLaunchPoint" type="uci:OpZoneMissileDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Data defining a missile type, related track, and source of launch position.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NoFire" type="uci:OpZoneNoFireType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines areas where strike impact is restricted.  Does not restrict the launch of weapons.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NoFly" type="uci:OpZoneNoFlyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines area where flight is restricted.  Equivalent to MIL-STD-6016 restricted zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VehicleConfiguration" type="uci:VehicleCommandDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines vehicle configuration parameters that should change based on the planned location of a vehicle.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WeaponRestriction" type="uci:OpZoneWeaponRestrictionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Set of restricted weapons that cannot be used against a target type and or in a zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WeatherConditions" type="uci:OpZoneWeatherType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines area of weather conditions with potential of mission impact.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpZoneFilterAreaPET" abstract="true" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element represents the content of a filtered area.  Current extensions include MTI_OpZoneFilterAreaType, TrackingOpZoneFilterAreaType.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="FilterType" type="uci:OpZoneFilterEnum" default="INCLUSION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Determination of how the data is filtered in a geographic area.  If the enumeration is set to INCLUSION the contents are to be included for processing or other utilization.  If the enumeration is set to EXCLUSION the contents are to be ignored or excluded from processing or other utilization.  If the enumeration is set to BOTH then the contents could have both included and excluded data for processing or utilization as determined by the extending filter.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Ranking" type="uci:ComparableRankingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The ranking is used for overlapping exclusion and inclusion filter areas.  The zone with the highest precedence/priority combination is selected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpZoneID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to op zones.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpZoneJammingType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an OpZone is a jamming control zone.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Allowed" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) jamming is allowed within the OpZone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RestrictedFrequencyBand" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific frequency range where jamming is restricted.  This element is only applicable when the sibling Allowed element indicates jamming is allowed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OpZoneMDT" uci:version="003.000.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:OpBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="OpZoneID" type="uci:OpZoneID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element represents the unique identifier of the zone associated with this message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Category" type="uci:OpZoneCategoryEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element indicates the type of zone.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CategoryUniqueData" type="uci:OpZoneCategoryType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
