						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Traceability" type="uci:TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>C2 sources work at different levels of detail and abstraction, progressing from what to do to how specifically to do it.  Inputs from abstract tasking sources and Tasks can be decomposed into discrete, actionable Tasks and/or Capability commands.  This element provides traceability to the external tasking or Task from which this Capability command was derived.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityMDT" uci:version="002.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates that a subsystem is capable of performing an Orbital Surveillance Sensor activity in the domain generally characterized by altitudes greater than 100 km above Earth's surface and less than interplanetary ranges. Orbital Surveillance Sensor involves the use of sensors of various different phenomenologies to search for and/or collect information on a target, multiple targets or region of space in support of an Information Objective.  The focus of an Orbital Surveillance Sensor activity (identified under the specification of Target) can be location based, object based, or zone based and targets can be in equilibrium orbits (affected only by natural forces) or under powered flight.

Examples of information objectives achieved through sensor collects include achieving or maintaining a certain level of orbit accuracy, verifying that there are no unknown objects in a specific region of space or with certain orbital parameters, determining the structural elements of a target down to a specified resolution, determining the current operational configuration of a target, or something as specific as providing a baseline characterization of a target in a specific phenomenology to be used for future change-detection.

This message advertises a subsystem's mostly static characteristics for a mission-ready Orbital Surveillance Sensor Capability to other systems, which enables proper commanding of the capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an installed Orbital Surveillance Sensor Capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityMT" uci:version="002.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message indicates that a subsystem is capable of performing an Orbital Surveillance Sensor activity in the domain generally characterized by altitudes greater than 100 km above Earth's surface and less than interplanetary ranges. Orbital Surveillance Sensor involves the use of a single sensor to search for and/or collect information on a target, multiple targets or region of space to help meet a specific Information Objective.  The focus of an Orbital Surveillance Sensor activity (identified under the specification of Target) can be location based, object based, or zone based and targets can be in equilibrium orbits (affected only by natural forces) or under powered flight.

Examples of information objectives achieved through sensor collects include achieving or maintaining a certain level of orbit accuracy, verifying that there are no unknown objects in a specific region of space or with certain orbital parameters, determining the structural elements of a target down to a specified resolution, determining the current operational configuration of a target, or something as specific as providing a baseline characterization of a target in a specific phenomenology to be used for future change-detection.

This message advertises a subsystem's mostly static characteristics for a mission-ready Orbital Surveillance Sensor Capability to other systems, which enables proper commanding of the capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityStatusMDT" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Reports the current status of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor capabilities available to the system. This includes information regarding whether or not each capability is currently available based on hardware status, commanded operational states etc.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityStatus" type="uci:CapabilityStatusType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the high level availability/state of a Capability instance.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This message reports the current status of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor capabilities available to the system.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityType" uci:version="002.001.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Describes the Orbital Surveillance Sensor capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CommandableCapabilityDeclarationType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's first tier type in the Orbital Surveillance Sensor taxonomy.  For Orbital Surveillance Sensor, the first tier is the trajectory nature of the target.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SubCapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorSubCapabilityType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor Capability, the second tier in the taxonomy of Orbital Surveillance Sensor.  For Orbital Surveillance Sensor, the second tier is the high level functional collection and processing capabilities of a sensor and associated unit for a specified tracking altitude range.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CharacterizationOptions" type="uci:CharacterizationTypeEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="10">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a type of characterization phenomenology that is supported by this capability. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SensorConstraints" type="uci:SensorConstraintsBaseType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This field specifies which type of sensor constraints are supported by this capability. If multiple instances are given, each should be of a different constraint type as indicated by the child element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageOutput" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorMessageOutputsEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="7">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a message that is an output of the Capability. See enumerated type annotations for details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorMinimumCollectionRequirementsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specifies span of time for individual collection based on duration or rotational periods of target.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="TargetRotationalPeriods" type="xs:int">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Collection duration (in number of rotations).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Time" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Collection duration (in seconds).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorMinimumSizeType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the expected size of the smallest target for the task (or threshold for search) in either physical area  or apparent size appropriate to the phenomenology (e.g., radar cross section).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="RadarCrossSection" type="uci:PercentileRCSType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See Base Description.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VisualMagnitude" type="uci:VisualMagnitudeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>See Base Description.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Area" type="uci:AreaType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Area measured in m^2.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Intensity" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Intensity measured in watts per steradian.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorReportingCategoriesType" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the SDA special reporting requirements, to include the product, priority, need by date, and/or entity for which the product or products are to be reported.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SDA_SpecialInstructions" type="uci:SDA_SpecialInstructionsConstraintType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates additional instructions associated with tasking for sensor collections. When "All" is chosen, all of the special instructions must be accomplished to satisfy the Task.  When "Any" is chosen, that Task can be satisfied by performing only one of the special instructions provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RelativePriority" type="uci:ComparableRankingType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The priority of this reporting requirement relative to others.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductNeededBy" type="uci:ProductNeededByType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time by which the products are needed by the source which created the Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ReportTo" type="uci:ReportToType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the persons/services/Systems/Units for which the product is to be reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorSensitivityConstraintType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the expected size or apparent phenomenology-based size of the smallest target of interest for the task OR signal strength for targets emitting radio frequency information.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MinimumSize" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorMinimumSizeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Expected size of the smallest target for the task (or threshold for search) in either physical area  or apparent size appropriate to the phenomenology (e.g., radar cross section).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinimumSignalStrength" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the signal strength for targets emitting radio frequency information.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorSubCapabilityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the functional abilities of a sensor, to include the collections and processing abilities, at a given tracking altitude.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TrackingAltitude" type="uci:SensorTrackingAltitudesEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the maximum altitude that a sensor can track in a given operational mode. This enables distinction between average orbital altitudes, such as for a highly eccentric object, and the altitude at tracking time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FunctionalCapability" type="uci:SensorFunctionalityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the high level functional and processing capabilities of a sensor and related unit.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorTargetType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the target of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor Task.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="PointList" type="uci:SensorPointListType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor Task is defined by a sensor point list.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElementSetCloud" type="uci:ElementSetCloudType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor Task is defined by an element set cloud. This method is used currently to set up searches when limited information on a recently found object leads to non-trivial uncertainty in the estimate of the orbital parameters (target has a high likelihood of not being in the acquisition basket of a sensor receiving an orbital state estimate in a hand-off).  A tested approach for defining a search to be used by a sensor tasked for follow-up is to create a set of candidate orbital states that span the uncertainty in such a way that a sensor that attempts to acquire on each element set during a defined time window will have a high likelihood of acquiring the object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ObjectBased" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceObjectsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor Task is a specified object or objects or relative to a specified object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LocationBased" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceLocationTargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor Task is defined by orbit kinematic data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SensorCentricVolume" type="uci:SourceCoverageType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Sensor is defined by a volume specified with the sensor at the origin.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorTaskBaseType" uci:version="002.000.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The base type for an Orbital Surveillance Sensor Task.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorCapabilityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's first tier type in the Orbital Surveillance Sensor taxonomy.  For Orbital Surveillance Sensor, the first tier is the trajectory nature of the target.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CollectionRequirements" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceCollectionRequirementsType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides Capability-specific instructions and information to the sensor to enable appropriate sensor set-up and data collection to meet the orbital surveillance collection need.  Examples include minimum and maximum number of metric observations per collection interval for a metric collection task, requirement for an imagery collection and desired imagery resolution for a characterization task, and minimum separation distance for a multi-object task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConfirmObjectAcquisition" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If TRUE, report whether the tasked object was acquired or not. In space domain awareness (SDA) domain, this is referred to as "PosNeg".</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InformationObjective" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="20">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This provides additional context for the sensor units to inform the decisions on which sensors are appropriate and how best to set up collections.  This context can help to compensate for shortfalls in the fidelity of the sensor models. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ReportingRequirements" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorReportingCategoriesType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the SDA special reporting requirements, to include the product, priority, need by date, and/or entity for which the product or products are to be reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SetUpStartTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Time estimated by the collection planner required for the sensor to transition from completion of the previous task to initiate collection for the current task.  This may include sensor-slewing/attitude-change, mode change, or sensor position change.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PostCollectionWrapUp" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Time estimated by the collection planner required for the sensor to transition from completion of collection for a task until sensor has completed the task.  One example is the time to read out the data from an optical sensor focal plane.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SensitivityConstraints" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorSensitivityConstraintType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides information on the expected size or apparent phenomenology-based size of the smallest target of interest for the task OR signal strength for targets emitting radio frequency information.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSensorTaskType" uci:version="003.000.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an Orbital Surveillance Sensor Task type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorTaskBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Target" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSensorTargetType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The target for which this task applies.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSpecificDataType" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific data types for the Orbital Surveillance Capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's first tier type in the Orbital Surveillance taxonomy.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubCapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="20">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's second tier type in the Orbital Surveillance taxonomy. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceSubCapabilityDetailsChoiceType" uci:version="002.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability of the Orbital Surveillance Capability, the second tier in the taxonomy of Orbital Surveillance.  For Orbital Surveillance, the second tier is the desired outcome of the collection.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Search" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSearchType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a task to search an a region of space or for a specific object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OrbitAccuracy" type="uci:OrbitAccuracyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a task to achieve/maintain specified orbit accuracy.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Characterization" type="uci:CharacterizationObjectiveType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Task to characterize an object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MultiObject" type="uci:MultiObjectType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a task involving multiple objects.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ManeuverDetection" type="uci:ManeuverDetectionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a task to detect maneuvers (may require more than one sensor) and near real-time processing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DeploymentDetection" type="uci:DeploymentDetectionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a task that monitors primary target to detect deployment of secondary object or objects.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceTargetType" uci:version="003.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the target of the Orbital Surveillance Task as either object based, location based, or zone based.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="ObjectBased" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceObjectsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Task is a specified object or objects or relative to a specified object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LocationBased" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceLocationTargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Task is defined by orbit kinematic data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ZoneBased" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceZoneTargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Task is defined by a geocentric zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceTaskBaseType" uci:version="003.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The base type for an Orbital Surveillance Task.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceCapabilityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability's first tier type in the Orbital Surveillance taxonomy.  For Orbital Surveillance, the first tier is the focus of the collection, either based on one or more objects or for a defined volume.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubCapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSubCapabilityDetailsChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability of the Orbital Surveillance Capability, the second tier in the taxonomy of Orbital Surveillance.  For Orbital Surveillance, the second tier is the desired outcome of the collection.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InformationObjective" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceSubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This provides additional context for the collection planner and (as appropriate) the sensor units to inform the decisions on which sensors are appropriate and how best to set up collections.  This context can help to compensate for shortfalls in the fidelity of the sensor models.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinSize" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This optional field indicates the smallest sized objects to look for in the sensor Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConfirmObjectAcquisition" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If TRUE, report whether the tasked object was acquired or not. In space domain awareness (SDA) domain, this is referred to as "PosNeg".</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductNeededBy" type="uci:ProductNeededByType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time by which the products are needed by the source which created the Orbital Surveillance Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SensorConstraints" type="uci:AllowableSensorsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the required, allowed, or excluded sensors that the planner is allowed to consider tasking for collection to acquire the desired data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SDA_SpecialInstructions" type="uci:SDA_SpecialInstructionsConstraintType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates additional instructions associated with tasking for sensor collections. When "All" is chosen, all of the special instructions must be accomplished to satisfy the Task.  When "Any" is chosen, that Task can be satisfied by performing only one of the special instructions provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceTaskType" uci:version="003.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an Orbital Surveillance Task type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceTaskBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Target" type="uci:OrbitalSurveillanceTargetType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The target for which this task applies.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalSurveillanceZoneTargetType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the target of an Orbital Surveillance Task is defined by a zone/volume.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="GeocentricZone" type="uci:GeocentricVolumeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the target of the Orbital Surveillance Task is defined by geocentric zone.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalToleranceValuesType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type provides store values related to OPA tolerances.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="OrbitPlane" type="uci:AngleQuarterType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The tolerance value for the difference in the orbital plane.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Range" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The tolerance value for the range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DeltaV" type="uci:SpeedType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The tolerance value for the delta v. Measured in meters per second.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Longitude" type="uci:AngleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The tolerance value for the longitude degree.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StationLimitLongitude" type="uci:AngleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The tolerance value for the optimal longitude degree for station-keeping.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalUndockingEventType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type specifies details for an Undocking Operational Proximity Analysis Event.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="UndockTime" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The time at which two objects undock.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalVCM_ParametersType" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the parameters for requesting an orbital VCM. This information includes the creation time of the VCM results, the propagation model used, and the parameters for controlling the propagation process.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CreationTime" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time at which the VCM was created.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VCM_Propagator" type="uci:VCM_PropagatorType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A set of force models and numerical integrator settings used to propagate a resident space object (RSO) in time using parameters from an *OrbitalVCM message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalVCM_RequestParametersType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the parameters for requesting an orbital VCM. This information includes the time window of the VCM results and the interval between VCM results.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="RequestWindow" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Time window within which VCM analysis/results are being requested.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StepSize" type="xs:duration" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the requested interval between VCM results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalVCM_Type" uci:version="002.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the vector and covariance data of the VCM.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="StateVector" type="uci:OrbitalKinematicsStandardFrameChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates kinematics vector in the Earth-Centered Inertial (ECI) J2000 (ECI-J2K) Reference System.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CovarianceData" type="uci:VCM_DataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The covariance data provides a measure of the strength of the correlation between two or more elements of the orbit or tracked object state (position/velocity/other quantities), each of which have some underlying degree of statistical variation. The correlation coefficient between any two elements of the state can be derived from the variances and covariances of the two elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RevolutionNumber" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the revolution number (Revs) at the Epoch.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitalVolumeType" uci:version="002.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Describes a spherical volume centered on an orbital position.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Position" type="uci:OrbitalKinematicsChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the center of a spherical volume with sibling Radius.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Radius" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the radius of a spherical volume around the sibling Position element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitBreakupEventDetailsType" uci:version="003.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type provides the details of an on-orbit event which results in physical damage, whether in whole or in part, of an object or multiple objects.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="OrbitalConjunctionID" type="uci:OrbitalConjunctionID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a previously identified orbital conjunction that is the basis for this debris estimate request.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Collision" type="uci:OrbitCollisionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates details of an identified orbital collision that is the basis for this orbital debris estimate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SingleObjectBreakup" type="uci:OrbitObjectBreakupType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Characterizes a space based object breaking into pieces as a result of an internal explosion due to unvented fuel, overheated batteries or other causes.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeActivityMDT" uci:version="003.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Subsystem which hosts the Orbit Change Capability whose Activities are given in this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="uci:OrbitChangeActivityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dynamic operational characteristics of an Activity of a System's Orbit Change Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeActivityMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OrbitChangeActivityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeActivityType" uci:version="003.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Provides a summary of the dynamic operational characteristics of an Activity of a System's Orbit Change Capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ActivityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ManeuverSummary" type="uci:ManeuverSummaryType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Provides a summary detail of the specific maneuver that produced the new orbit.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="OrbitChangeSummary" type="uci:OrbitKinematicsChangeSummaryType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Provides an overall summary of the intended orbit.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeCapabilityMDT" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:OrbitChangeCapabilityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Provides a list of the specific Orbit Change Capabilities as defined by the OrbitChangeCapabilityEnum.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeCapabilityMT" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OrbitChangeCapabilityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeCapabilityStatusMDT" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilityStatusBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityStatus" type="uci:CapabilityStatusType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the high level availability/state of a Capability instance.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeCapabilityStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:OrbitChangeCapabilityStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeCapabilityType" uci:version="002.001.002.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a system's orbit change capability, its configurable characteristics and its controllability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CommandableCapabilityDeclarationType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitChangeCapabilityEnum" maxOccurs="9">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of Orbit Change capability. See enumeration annotations for further details. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SupportedChange" type="uci:OrbitChangeMagnitudeType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the magnitude of change supported by the Capability.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeChoiceType" uci:version="002.001.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a number of specific maneuvers to reach a new orbit.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="SpecificOrbit" type="uci:COE_OrbitType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific new orbit, described in classic orbital elements (COE), to change to.  The maneuver to reach the new orbit isn't specified; the orbit specified here is the steady-state post maneuver orbit.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpecificPosition" type="uci:OrbitalVolumeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific orbital position to move to, expressed as a spherical volume.  The maneuver to reach the volume and the resulting orbit after reaching the volume aren't specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Rendezvous" type="uci:RSO_ApproachType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific resident space object (RSO) to rendezvous with.  Rendezvous doesn't imply proximity operations, docking, etc.  The maneuver to achieve rendezvous and the resulting orbit after achieving it aren't specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProximityOperations" type="uci:ProximityOperationsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific resident space object (RSO) to initiate proximity operations around.  Specific objectives, specific desired maneuvers, etc. after entering proximity operations aren't specified.  The maneuver/rendezvous necessary to initiate proximity operations isn't specified.

Proximity operations means that two "neighboring" vehicles maneuver to affect their relative states.  It requires a precise match of orbital velocities and position vectors allowing them to remain at a constant distance through orbital station-keeping.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Longitude" type="uci:AngleType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orbital line of longitude to change to.  This choice is only applicable for geo-stationary and some geo-synchronous orbits.    The maneuver to reach the longitude and the resulting orbit after reaching it aren't specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SemimajorAxis" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orbital semi-major axis to change to.   For a circular orbit, this is equivalent to orbital altitude.   The maneuver to reach the new semi-major axis and the resulting orbit after reaching it aren't specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Inclination" type="uci:AngleHalfPositiveType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orbital inclination or tilt  to change to.  The maneuver to reach the inclination and the resulting orbit after reaching it aren't specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Eccentricity" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orbital shape or eccentricity to change to.    The maneuver to reach the eccentricity and the resulting orbit after reaching it aren't specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RaceTrack" type="uci:RaceTrackOrbitType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific new orbit, described in racetrack parameters, to change to. This choice is only applicable for geo-stationary and some geo-synchronous orbits. The manuerver to reach the racetrack orbit isn't specified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeMagnitudeType" uci:version="001.002.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the types of supported changes to accomplish an orbit change.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SemimajorAxisChange" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the greatest supported change in semi-major axis.  This is equivalent to orbital altitude for circular orbits.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InclinationChange" type="uci:AngleHalfPositiveType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the greatest supported change in orbital eccentricity.  Inclination is the angle of the orbital plane with respect to the equator of the object at the epoch of the vector used for the prediction, measured in radians.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LongitudeChange" type="uci:AngleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the greatest supported change in longitude, most commonly known as a change in orbital slot. Retains definition of longitude, but understood to be at GEO orbit at 42,164 km from the center of the Earth. This element is applicable to geostationary and certain geosynchronous orbits.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DestinationOrbit" type="uci:OrbitRegimeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="11">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a supported destination orbit. List size is based on the number of enum values ("Select All That Apply") in OrbitRegimeEnum type. If multiple instances are given, each should be of a different OrbitRegimeEnum type as indicated by the child element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EccentricityChange" type="uci:DoubleNonNegativeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the greatest supported change in orbital eccentricity.  Eccentricity is a quantity describing the shape of the satellite's orbit. In mathematics the eccentricity of a conic section is a measure of how much the shape deviates from being circular. A value of zero represents a perfect circle. As the eccentricity varies from zero to 1 the ellipse becomes more "stretched" An eccentricity of 1 is a parabolic rather than elliptical, and values greater than 1 are hyperbolas.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeTaskBaseType" uci:version="000.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Defines a common base task type that supports orbit changes.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityType" type="uci:OrbitChangeCapabilityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of capability to be used.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="OrbitChangeTaskType" uci:version="003.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Defines a task type that supports orbit changes.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:OrbitChangeTaskBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ChangeType" type="uci:OrbitChangeChoiceType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of Orbit Change desired. See annotations for the sibling CapabilityType element and those of the child choices for full details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
