	<xs:complexType name="PlannedActivityBaseType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PlannedActivityID" type="uci:PlannedActivityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Planned Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityType" type="uci:ActivityChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of planned Activity and the details to command and execute it.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Locked" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This flag is used to determine whether this Planned Activity can be modified/removed in subsequent planning steps and/or replans.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityTransition" type="uci:ActivityTransitionEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the planned state transition for the Planned Activity.  Transitions for a single Planned Activity can happen on different segments of an associated kinematic Plan and/or be far separated in time.  For example, a Task-based Planned Activity could start on one kinematic segment and end on a later one with many segments in between.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ResultTime" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The time or time window when the result of the sibling ActivityTransition is planned to occur.  This element is intended for transitions where time of execution start and time of results aren't simultaneous; for example Strike Tasks or OrbitChange Tasks.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedActivityExecutionStatusType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ActivityExecutionStatusType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="PlanID" type="uci:ActivityPlanID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The ID of the ActivityPlan this status pertains to.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedActivityID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to planned Activities.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedActivityTriggerType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PlannedActivityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ActivityTrigger" type="uci:ActivityTriggerType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the trigger for the planned Activity.  If omitted, "capture" of the endpoint of the associated kinematic sequence/segment/path is the trigger, if applicable.  Capture of an endpoint means kinematic behaviors are transitioning to the next planned sequence/segment/path.  Due to dynamic kinematic adjustments for weather, threat avoidance, etc. the System might not pass through/over the endpoint and might in fact be far from it at the moment of capture.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EndPointTrigger" type="xs:boolean" default="true">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>TRUE indicates the Activity should occur at the endpoint of the associated kinematic sequence/segment/path even if the Trigger doesn't occur before the EndPoint is captured.  FALSE indicates that the Activity should occur only if the Trigger occurs prior to capture of the EndPoint; if the Trigger does not occur before the EndPoint is captured then the Activity will never occur.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedActivityType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PlannedActivityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="TransitionTime" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The time or time window when the sibling ActivityTransition is planned to occur.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedCommActionExtendedType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PlannedCommActionType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedCommActionType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ConfigurationID" type="uci:CommConfigurationID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the ID for a specific configuration for a communication or gateway configuration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConfigurationState" type="uci:CommConfigurationStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether an instance of a Configuration is new or an update to an existing configuration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlannedSubsystemCommand" type="uci:PlannedSubsystemCommandType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Perform a command on the subsystem as a whole.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlannedCommCapability" type="uci:PlannedCommCapabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to deactivate the current Mission Data File and activate the MDF given by this element.  If the referenced MDF is already active, then this element indicates a command to activate a new file within one or more subcategories of the current MDF. An MDF is the primary source of configurations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedCommCapabilityType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Action" type="uci:NetworkLinkActionTypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether this is a new link to be created, or an existing one that needs to be modified or deleted.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability instance which the communication effectivity has been allocated to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Subsystem ID. If specified this indicates that the capability may be present on multiple subsystems and these settings must be applied to a specific communication subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Ranking" type="uci:CapabilityCommandRankingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the command's rank relative to other commands and rank-related overrides and tailoring.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Classification" type="uci:SecurityInformationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element provides the classification label that the Subsystem should place on messages and other data resulting from the Command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConnectionRequest" type="uci:CommConnectionCommandEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the desired state of the primary network connection for the link being commanded.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivateProfileID" type="uci:CommProfileID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Profile to which this link should be associated to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NetworkLinkID" type="uci:NetworkLinkID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a unique identifier for the configuration of an individual network connection.  Provides for the correlation of network link to a new activity or to an existing activity that will be updated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommonSettings" type="uci:CommControlType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allows the Communication Planner to deviate from the MDF. These configurations will be applied on top of the MDF therefore deviating from it.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CryptoKey" type="uci:CryptoLocationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allows the Communication Planner to apply the key at a specified slot. Such as selecting the appropriate VINSON Key.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CryptoZeroize" type="uci:CryptoLocationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allows the Communication Planner to Zeroize crypto slots.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CryptoRollover" type="uci:CryptoRolloverCommandType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allows the Communication Planner to perform a crypto rollover to slots.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LinkPortAssignments" type="uci:CommLinkPortMapType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the ports to assign to the connection to form the link.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VerboseStatus" type="uci:VerboseStatusType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides means to control the generation of verbose Activity messages that provide full field reporting.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WaveformSpecificSettings" type="uci:CommWaveformCapabilityCommandPET" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allows the Communication Planner to deviate from the MDF in a waveform specific manner applying configurations which are not common.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LinkConnectionRequest" type="uci:LinkConnectionRequestType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to change the connection status of the individual data links managed by the waveform. Generally, a link's connection status must be CONNECTED for the waveform to transmit payload data over the communication medium or for the waveform to receive transmissions from the communication medium.  Note that this parameter is not available until after a CommActivity is created and may not be available until the waveform has joined the network.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedControlInterfacesCommandType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PlanType" type="uci:InterfacePlanTypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific *Plan type that the interface is associated with.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ControlInterface" type="uci:PlannedControlInterfaceStateType" maxOccurs="4">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific messages/interface for the *Plan type indicated by the sibling element.  If multiple instances of this element are given, each should be of a different message/interface type as enumerated by the child PlanInterface element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedControlInterfaceStateType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ControlInterface" type="uci:ControlInterfaceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific messages/interface for the *Plan type indicated by the sibling element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivationState" type="uci:InterfaceStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current/commanded availability/activation state of the sibling ControlInterface.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedControlInterfacesType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates supported Mission Control related messages/interfaces along with their current state of activation.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PlanType" type="uci:InterfacePlanTypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific *Plan type that the interface is associated with.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ControlInterface" type="uci:PlannedControlInterfaceStateType" maxOccurs="4">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific messages/interface for the *Plan type indicated by the sibling element.  If multiple instances of this element are given, each should be of a different message/interface type as enumerated by the child ControlInterface element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlanSimultaneity" type="uci:PlanSimultaneityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates how many of the *Plan indicated by the sibling PlanType can be activated and executed simultaneously by the System.  For example, a System that supports multiple simultaneous active/executing RouteActivityPlans for different Capability types would indicate MULTIPLE_PARALLEL.  A System supporting activation of a current and future sequential RoutePlans would indicate MULTIPLE_SERIAL.  A System supporting only one RoutePlan active at a time would indicate SINGLE.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedGatewayConfigurationType" uci:version="003.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Ties the unique gateway - Link - Capability/Activity to Message and Product Ingress-Egress configuration details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="GatewayServiceID" type="uci:ServiceID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If specified, indicates the Service instance to Gateway the data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConfigurationID" type="uci:CommConfigurationID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the ID for a specific configuration for a communication or gateway configuration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConfigurationState" type="uci:CommConfigurationStateEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether an instance of a Configuration is new or an update to an existing configuration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivateMDF" type="uci:MDF_CommandType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to deactivate the current Mission Data File and activate the MDF given by this element.  If the referenced MDF is already active, then this element indicates a command to activate a new file within one or more subcategories of the current MDF. An MDF is the primary source of configurations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivateProfileID" type="uci:CommProfileID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Gateways Profile to which this link should be associated to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GatewayCapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The ID Gateway Capabilities which this is applicable to. If empty, means all.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GatewayActivityID" type="uci:ActivityID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The ID of the Activity (Instances) of the Gateway Capability which this is applicable to. If empty, means all.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GatewayLinkDestination" type="uci:GatewayLinkDestinationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the necessary IDs which facilitate gatewaying the data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MessageConfiguration" type="uci:MessageConfigurationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If specified, indicates the message topics, filters, and gateways.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductDisseminationIngressSystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The remote System ID for which product data shall be ingressed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProductDisseminationEgressDestinationID" type="uci:ProductDisseminationDestinationID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Product Dissemination Destinations which data should be sent to. This is the method to specify Product Egress within the standard Product Dissemination Workflow.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GatewaySpecificSettings" type="uci:GatewayConfigurationPET" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates Data Gateway Command information specific to a type of Data Gateway.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedReleaseConditionsType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Position" type="uci:Point3D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Notional System position at time of release.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Velocity" type="uci:Velocity2D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Representation of the vehicle's velocity as directional components in True Air Speed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Orientation" type="uci:OrientationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Euler Angle Sequence describing the orientation of the vehicle in the order yaw, pitch, roll.  The angles are given in a locally level, North-East-Down coordinate system centered on the vehicle.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WindVelocity" type="uci:Velocity2D_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element represents wind speed at the release point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssociatedRoutePlan" type="uci:RoutePlanReferenceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the RoutePlan associated with the sibling release conditions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlannedSubsystemCommandType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Subsystem ID to which this command applies.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivateMDF" type="uci:MDF_CommandType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command to deactivate the current Mission Data File and activate the MDF given by this element.  If the referenced MDF is already active, then this element indicates a command to activate a new file within one or more subcategories of the current MDF. An MDF is the primary source of configurations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningAllowedEscalationType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="AutonomousPlanningActionID" type="uci:AutonomousPlanningActionID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Assigns a unique ID to an allowed planning action.  This ID can be reference in *Plans, alerts, etc. that result when the planning action is triggered.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ByResultSetting" type="uci:MissionPlanningAutonomySettingByResultType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element allows control of the escalation of the autonomous replanning.  If the autonomous function indicated by the sibling AllowedType leads to a "by result" trigger described here, then additional autonomous planning is allowed as described here.  For example, if Tasks are dropped as a result of initial autonomous replanning then this element can be used to enable/disable a secondary "escalated" planning iteration that includes global Task allocation.  If omitted, the sibling AllowedType is allowed regardless of result.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AllowedType" type="uci:PlanningAllowedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the mission planning type that is allowed to be autonomously triggered.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningAllowedType" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:AutonomousPlanCommandType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="PlanAheadDuration" type="uci:DurationType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Required duration in the future when the Plan should start.  Existing *Plan will continue during this time.  This duration should account for everything that must happen from replan initiation to new plan activation.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningApplicabilitySystemType" uci:version="003.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ApplicabilityType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ConstrainingPlanIncorporation" type="uci:ConstrainedPlanIncorporationEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates how the planning process incorporates content from constraining *Plans into the new *Plans.  See enumeration annotations for further details.  This element is optional when the planning process doesn't support constraining *Plans.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningByCaseTriggerType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityAdded" type="uci:CapabilityTaxonomyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a new Capability or SubCapability which becomes available or a previously failed Capability which has been restored.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityFailure" type="uci:CapabilityTaxonomyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a failure of a Capability and/or SubCapability needed to perform a Requirement.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CommsLost" type="uci:CommsLostTriggerDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to lost comms.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_OverDesignation" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a situation where the designated DMPIs exceed those initially reserved for the Task, if this creates a shortage for other assigned Tasks.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DMPI_UnderDesignation" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a situation where the designated DMPIs are less than those initially reserved for the task, and if weapons not designated can be used to perform previous unallocated tasks.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EnduranceLow" type="uci:EnduranceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a low remaining endurance condition such as low fuel or battery power. This trigger can further be specialized by the definition of the Endurance thresholds to define the trigger.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OffRoute" type="uci:ThresholdOffRouteTriggerDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a vehicle that has deviated from the planned route to such a degree that a replan is required.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProximityConflict" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to the proximity of two items (Systems, Entities or other items) that exceeded a minimum geospatial separation limit as specified in OpRouting messages.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ReleasePointOutsideLAR" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to the location of a DMPI, updated LAR calculations or other changes that have resulted in the planned release point for a weapon falling outside the weapon LAR.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RouteConflict" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a route that exceeded a minimum geospatial separation limit with another item or items.  The separation is between a planned/navigated route and other routes or conflicting items as specified in OpRouting messages.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RouteVulnerability" type="uci:PlanVulnerabilityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to vulnerability due to exposure along the route with and without suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SystemStateChange" type="uci:SystemStateFilterType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a system state transition, as indicated by the SystemStatus message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RequirementAdded" type="uci:RequirementTriggerType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger indicates a new Requirement.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RequirementDependencyFailed" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger indicates a Requirement that cannot be planned/performed because a Requirement it is dependent on cannot be planned/performed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RequirementDropped" type="uci:RequirementTriggerType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a Requirement execution state transition to DROPPED, as indicated by execution status message for the Requirement (EffectStatus, TaskStatus, etc.).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RequirementFailed" type="uci:RequirementFailedTriggerType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a Requirement execution state transition to FAILED, as indicated by execution status message for the Requirement (EffectStatus, TaskStatus, etc.).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RequirementChange" type="uci:RequirementTriggerType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a change to a Requirement that impacts an existing plan.  For example, a change of the position of the target of the Requirement.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RequirementTiming" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger a Requirement that is not expected to meet its timing constraints.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ZoneViolation" type="uci:ZoneViolationTriggerDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to an OpZone conflicts with the current plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OrbitConflict" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to the position along a future planned/predicted/propagated orbit for a spacecraft exceeding a minimum geospatial separation limit with another item or items.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OffPlannedOrbit" type="uci:ThresholdOffOrbitTriggerDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a spacecraft that has deviated from its planned orbit to such a degree that a replan is required.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpacecraftEnduranceLow" type="uci:SatelliteEnduranceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to a low remaining endurance condition such as low fuel or battery power. This trigger can further be specialized by setting trigger thresholds in descendant elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpacecraftProximityConflict" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger refers to the proximity of two spacecraft (Systems, Entities or other space items) that exceeded a minimum geospatial separation limit.  Monitoring for this trigger should be based on current position of live items, not planned/predicted/propagated positions of Systems; see sibling OrbitConflict element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ResponseID" type="uci:ResponseID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This trigger indicates planning triggered by a Response and/or ResponsePlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningByResultTriggerType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="ReplanRequired" type="uci:PlanTypeEnum" maxOccurs="11">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a replan of one *Plan resulting in the need to replan an existing Plan of the type given by this element. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VulnerabilityChanged" type="uci:PlanVulnerabilityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This result refers to a replan which results in vulnerability changes that exceed the threshold or thresholds given in descendant elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RequirementUnallocated" type="uci:RequirementTriggerType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This result refers to a case where Requirements have been unallocated as a result of triggered replanning.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningCandidateBaseType" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The SystemID of the System to plan for.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConstrainingPlans" type="uci:ConstrainingPlansType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates existing plans of the System associated with the sibling SystemID that constrain the *Plan or *PlanCommand.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OtherSystemConstrainingPlans" type="uci:OtherSystemConstrainingPlansType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates existing plans of another System that constrain the *Plan or *PlanCommand.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningDiscoveryBaseType" uci:version="003.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PlanningProcessID" type="uci:PlanningProcessID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a planning process invocable through a *PlanCommand message/interface.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ValidationSupported" type="uci:SupportedFunctionEnum" maxOccurs="2">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether this process supports validation via the *PlanValidationCommand messages. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ApplicableTo" type="uci:PlanningApplicabilitySystemType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a type or instance, of System or Capabilities, that the planning process is applicable to; a System the process can create the specified *Plan type or types for.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Supports" type="uci:ApplicabilityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a type or instance of System, Capabilities or existing *Plans which the planning process can develop support for in the new *Plan.  For example, the sibling ApplicableTo element could indicate the planning process can plan electronic attack routes.  This element can then indicate the type or instance of Systems, Capabilities or *Plan types that can be supported by the electronic attack route/plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlanningTriggers" type="uci:MissionPlanningByCaseTriggerEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="24">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the set of triggers that the System is able to monitor to autonomously initiate the planning process. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningFunctionID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to PlanningFunctions.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningFunctionMDT" uci:version="003.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PlanningFunctionID" type="uci:PlanningFunctionID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a unique ID, assigned to this PlanningFunction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the System whose planning functions are being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlanningInterfaces" type="uci:PlanningInterfacesType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="10">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates planning interfaces supported by the System.  A supported interface isn't necessarily enabled currently; see the PlanningStatus message for current status/configuration of control interfaces advertised here.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlanningInterfaceDetails" type="uci:PlanningInterfaceDetailsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element is used to describe the details of planning interfaces/messages, specifically *PlanCommand interfaces of a System.  It provides discoverability of distinct planning process instances along with the functional scope and output *Plan type or types.  A planning interface/process described here can only be invoked when the sibling Interfaces element indicates it is enabled.

Planning processes are dynamically discoverable because Systems tend to have widely varying planning functionality.  Decomposing planning into discrete processes allows planning functionality to be distributed across a service oriented system of systems.  Making planning processes discoverable encourages planning-related services at multiple levels in a C2 hierarchy to adapt to and simultaneously support Systems with different planning functionality and processes.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PlanActivationAutonomyDetails" type="uci:SupportedPlanActivationAutonomyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates capabilities of the System to perform plan activation autonomously.  Plan activations can be performed either at the MissionPlan or SubPlan level.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ScoringInterfaceDetails" type="uci:PlanScoringProcessType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element is used to describe the details of scoring interfaces/messages summarized in the sibling Interfaces element. It provides discoverability of distinct scoring process instances along with the functional scope. A scoring interface/process described here can only be invoked when the sibling Interfaces ActivationState element indicates it is enabled.

Plan Scoring processes are dynamically discoverable because Systems tend to have varying scoring algorithms.  Decomposing plan scoring into discrete processes allows scoring functionality to be distributed across a service oriented system of systems.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PlanningFunctionMT" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See the annotation in the associated message for an overall description of the message and this type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:PlanningFunctionMDT">
