	<xs:complexType name="PlanningGuidelineType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Origin" type="uci:PlanningPointType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Denotes the origin for planning.  If omitted, the origin should be determined by context.  For example, during dynamic planning during live operations the current position of the System could be used.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Destination" type="uci:PlanningPointPriorityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Denotes the destination for planning.  If there are multiple then it is up to the planner to choose.  Multiple destinations can give planning algorithms the option to choose the safest/best end point (such as alternate Egress points).  If omitted, the destination should be determined by context.  For example, the planner could obtain all egress OpPoints associated with the subject System and Mission and determine the best egress destination.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SpeedOptimization" type="uci:SpeedOptimizationEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the System will vary its speed autonomously according to the specified optimization algorithm.  If omitted, it is N/A.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ClimbOptimization" type="uci:ClimbOptimizationEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the system will climb or descend at an autonomously chosen rate according to the specified optimization algorithm.  If omitted, it is N/A.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
