	<xs:complexType name="PO_ProductOutputCommandImageryType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ProductOutputCommandBasicType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ProductOutputID" type="uci:PO_ProductGeneratorOutputID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This ID is associated with the Capability message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="JPEG_Settings" type="uci:JPEG_SettingsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element specifies settings for JPEG files generated by the Command. This element should be omitted when the sibling ProductFormat doesn't indicate JPEG, settings are left to the discretion of the Command recipient and/or default settings are acceptable.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="NITF_PackingPlan" type="uci:NITF_PackingPlanPET" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This element defines data to be placed into the header of the resulting NITF product, commonly referred to at the NITF header "packing plan". This element should be omitted when the sibling ProductFormat doesn't indicate NITF, settings are left to the discretion of the Command recipient and/or default settings are acceptable.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CompressionRatio" type="xs:float" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Defined as the number of bytes in the input image divided by the number of bytes in the output image.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MISP_Settings" type="uci:MISP_PackingPlanType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates settings for imagery product defined in industry standard MISP.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProductRate" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the imagery product rate in frames/second on the service.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Interlaced" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates that an imagery product scan pattern is interlaced when true and non-interlaced or progressive when false.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProductSize" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the imagery product size in bytes.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProductResolution" type="uci:ProductResolutionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an imagery product dimensions in horizontal and vertical pixels and color depth.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="VideoOutput" type="uci:VideoOutputSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Settings for the video encoder for generating video streams.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_SettingsCommandMDT" uci:version="002.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CapabilitySettingsCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SubCapability" type="uci:PO_SubCapabilitySettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the subcapability settings to apply to this subsystem. All capabilities that are associated with the same SubcapabilityID will be impacted the same in accordance to this settings command message. Any PO_Commands received after this message has been processed will use these new settings unless directly overridden by settings specified in the PO_Command.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TrackSettings" type="uci:PO_TrackSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the settings that can be applied for track. All capabilities that are associated with the same TrackOptions ID in TrackSettings will be impacted the same in accordance to this settings command message. Any PO_Commands received after this message has been processed will use these new settings unless directly overridden by settings specified in the PO_Command.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ComponentSettings" type="uci:PO_ComponentSettingsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The component settings specified in this field are used to set the default component settings used by the sensor. All capabilities that are associated with the same ComponentID in ComponentSettings will be impacted the same in accordance to this settings command message. Any PO_Commands received after this message has been processed will use these new settings unless directly overridden by settings specified in the PO_Command.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionConstraintsSettings" type="uci:PO_CollectionConstraintsSettingsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The collection constraints settings specified in this field are used to set the default collection settings used by the sensor. Any PO_Commands received after this message has been processed will use these new settings unless directly overridden by settings specified in the PO_Command.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageOutput" type="uci:PO_MessageOutputsEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Specifies which messages are to be output by the Capability as the result of capability commands. Note: Only values advertised in the Capability message are allowed. Any non-supported values should result in rejection of the settings command. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FOR_Settings" type="uci:FOR_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>FOR limits to limit the optical view of the sensor to what it can see from its mounting position on the aircraft. These values override values defined in the Capability message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ThermalBlankingFOR_Settings" type="uci:FOR_Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>FOR limits to protect the sensor from being blinded by the sun or weapon effects(i.e. missile leaving jet). These values override values defined in the Capability message.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
