	<xs:complexType name="PO_SubCapabilitySettingsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an installed PO high-level SubCapability which adds an additional level of granularity to complete the mission using PO commands and tasks.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubCapabilityID" type="uci:SubCapabilityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A passive optical sensor will contain one or more subsystem subcapabilities. Each subsystem subcapability is identified by a unique ID. This ID is used in messages and capabilities to identify a particular subcapability. This field is the ID of the subcapability whose status is being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TechniqueSettings" type="uci:PO_TechniqueSettingType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="17">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the passive optical technique for tracking and search algorithm purposes. The technique setting is used to identify the technique type with the enumeration and any possible setting value associated with it with the optional fields.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_SubCapabilityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an installed PO high-level subCapability which adds an additional level of granularity to complete the mission using PO commands and tasks.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubCapabilityID" type="uci:SubCapabilityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A passive optical sensor will contain one or more subsystem subcapabilities. Each subcapability is identified by a unique ID. This ID is used in messages and capabilities to identify a particular subcapability. This field is the ID of the subcapability whose status is being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Spectrum" type="uci:SensorSpectrumEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency band or spectrum that is used to search, track, or generate products with the PO subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TechniqueSettings" type="uci:PO_TechniqueCapabilityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="17">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the passive optical technique for tracking and search algorithm purposes. Each technique setting requires the type with the enumeration and any possible minimum and maximum settings for that technique with the optional fields.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Environment" type="uci:PO_EnvironmentEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the passive optical target physical environment for tracking and search algorithm purposes.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_SweepSpeedConstraintControlsStatusType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Status" type="uci:ComponentControlsStatusType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates status of the commanded controls for the collection constraint.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Speed" type="uci:SpeedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This field is the current speed for this constraint.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_SweepSpeedConstraintControlsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Controls" type="uci:PO_ConstraintControlsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies commanded controls for the collection constraint.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Setting" type="uci:SpeedType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The rate at which the sensor look-point moves across the terrain.  This is only applicable to area or line targets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TargetType" uci:version="002.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the position or location to point the XX Subsystem to do a XX collection, track, or search as part of an XX Activity. If the XX Subsystem cannot point itself, then the TurretSlaved Type is used. If the system wants to allow the subsystem to control its own LOS then the ActivitySlavedID is used. FixedPointing is used to point to a predetermined location defined by its Enum values.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Geospatial" type="uci:TargetType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of or explicit values for geospatial characteristics of the target of the Command. When multiple points/targets are given, a best-fit, multi-track or similar behavior is expected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Pointed" type="uci:TurretCommandPositionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates body or inertially referenced pointing angles as the "target" of the Command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LOS_Option" type="uci:LOS_D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates body or inertially referenced line of sight pointing angles and/or rates as the "target" of the Command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Volume" type="uci:PO_AirTargetVolumeCommandType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the volume or specific Entity that defines the extents of the spatial region covered by the command. For non-cued Capabilities, one air volume instance of this element is expected. For cued Capabilities, two instances of this element are allowed: one with an Entity specified and a second with an air volume that define the extents of the cue volume around the Entity. For cued Capabilities, a single instance is allowed if it is an Entity in which case the Entity location uncertainty defines the extents of the cue volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TurretSlaved" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a PO_Command that has an accompanying TurretCommand that determines the "target" of the Command. The PO Capability is then pointed/targeted by the TurretCommand with other command details coming from the PO_Command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivitySlavedID" type="uci:ActivityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Pointing Command that has a secondary/coupled Activity, possibly of another Capability type such as AO or PO, that determines pointing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FixedPointing" type="uci:FixedPointingEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that a subsystem with point to a predetermined location defined by its Enum values.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TaskBaseType" uci:version="002.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Capability" type="uci:PO_CapabilityEnum">
