					<xs:documentation>Indicates details of the target of the Command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SensorSpectrum" type="uci:SensorSpectrumEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="14">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the spectrum that will be used for the PO Collection. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LookAtCoords" type="uci:LocatedEllipseType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an adjusted and/or more specific geospatial location for the collection. This element is used in cases where the sibling Target element isn't sufficiently specific and/or cannot be adjusted to suit the needs of the Task creator, but the relation to the original Target must be preserved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="MinimumNIIRS" type="uci:NIIRS_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The minimum NIIRS value required. See annotations of the underlying type for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DesiredNIIRS" type="uci:NIIRS_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The desired Imagery Interpretability Rating Scale value desired. See annotations of the underlying type for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CollectionConstraints" type="uci:OpticalCollectionConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the constraints for this collection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PairIdentifier" type="uci:PairIdentifierEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Task's role in a pair collection. See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Output" type="uci:PO_ProductOutputCommandImageryType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a desired output Product of the Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TaskType" uci:version="002.001.003.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PO_TaskBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Target" type="uci:PointingType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of or explicit values for geospatial characteristics of the target of the Command.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TechniqueCapabilityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Technique" type="uci:PO_TechniqueEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the SubCapability technique used for tracking and/or searching for targets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Intensity" type="uci:FloatMinMaxType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the intensity of a pixels to consider it a track object. Multiplier of value /10 to the auto threshold. A lower value means that less likely targets are detected, and a higher value filters out the less likely targets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Constellation" type="uci:FloatMinMaxType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of pixels around a detection to search when combining detections. A higher value means that an object with multiple detections is more likely to be combined into one track. If the value is too high, nearby objects may be treated as the same object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Stride" type="uci:FloatMinMaxType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates how many frames in which to use adaptive frame differencing. A stride of 1 is much like registration, but with additional processing applied to resolve misregistration errors. However, a stride above one will instead use a frame X frames ago. So stride 5 will mean that frame 105 will be registered with frame 100. This will detect slower moving targets, but may cause two detections on faster moving targets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PointIntensity" type="uci:FloatMinMaxType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This value controls the scale of the point to find.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EdgeIntensity" type="uci:FloatMinMaxType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This value controls the scale of the edge to find.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FalseAlarmLevelUpperLimit" type="xs:unsignedByte" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the FalseAlarmLevel capability is supported and also defines the upper limit allowed by the capability. Used to set the quantity of sensitivity levels. If omitted tracking range selection is the full range of the reference type. A common range is [0,15].</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TechniqueSettingType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Technique" type="uci:PO_TechniqueEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the SubCapability technique used for tracking and/or searching for targets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="IntensityValue" type="xs:float" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the intensity of a pixels to consider it a track object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConstellationValue" type="xs:float" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the number of pixels around a detection to search when combining detections.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StrideValue" type="xs:float" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates how many frames in which to use adaptive frame differencing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PointIntensityValue" type="xs:float" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This value controls the scale of the point to find.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EdgeIntensityValue" type="xs:float" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This value controls the scale of the edge to find.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FalseAlarmLevel" type="xs:unsignedByte" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the acceptable false alarm level for outputs from the Command.  This element can be used to adjust the sensitivity of the Capability in initiating tracks and reporting Entities.  Lower numbers indicate a more restrictive capability, i.e. fewer results. See FalseAlarmLevelUpperLimit for further details.  If omitted tracking range selection is left to the discretion of the command recipient. A common range is [0,15].</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TrackActivityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TrackMode" type="uci:PO_TrackModeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current status of target tracker on the primary target at the center line of sight.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TrackCapabilityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Allowable range of values for track parameters that can be used to customize target detections.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TrackOptionID" type="uci:TrackOptionsID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A passive optical sensor will contain one or more subsystem track options. Each subsystem track option is identified by a unique ID. This ID is used in messages and capabilities to identify a particular track option. This field is the ID of the track option whose status is being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TrackControlOptions" type="uci:PO_TrackCapabilityTypeEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="3">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>These are the additional features that the PO_Command can support and are not specifically settable (i.e., not available in PO_SettingsCommand). List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ATR_Filter" type="uci:IdentityBasicType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>These define the supported ATR Filter track capabilities provided by the corresponding PO sensor. This sets Automatic Target Recognition (ATR) filter parameters capabilities using one or more valid identity types based on MIL-STD-6016.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OffsetTrackSettings" type="uci:PO_OffsetTrackSettingsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allowable track offset setting parameters (Azimuth/Elevation/Roll and Azimuth/Elevation/Roll Rates) from the center of the LOS of the PO sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ObservedEntityThresholdSettings" type="uci:DurationRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The maximum and minimum range of thresholds allowed for the current capability that defines the number of seconds since the last update of an Observed Entity before the data is considered to be stale.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TrackingRange" type="uci:DoubleMinMaxType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The minimum and maximum tracking range allowed for the current capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CoastSettingOptions" type="uci:PO_CoastSettingOptionsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="6">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the allowed range of coast time settings associated with an environment setting for coasting a track before dropping it.  List size is based on allowing one per environment option available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BlankingVolumeSupported" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether current capability track option supports commanding a blanking volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TrackDetailsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Commanded values for track parameters that will be used to customize target detections.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TrackOptionID" type="uci:TrackOptionsID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This ID is used to command a specific track option available for a specific command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Mode" type="uci:PO_TrackCommandEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Command the target tracker to attempt to acquire a target, lock onto the target, or release the target and stop tracking.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TrackArea" type="uci:IncreaseDecreaseEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Adjust the size of the area in which the target tracker tries to acquire a target. The increase and decrease commands are dependent on the step sizes supported by the capability as defined in the associated program related documentation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LockPersistence" type="uci:PO_LockPersistenceEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>When enabled the tracker will assume last known heading and rate for a time period before breaking lock.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ATR_Filter" type="uci:IdentityBasicType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The set of commanded ATR Filter parameters based on one or more available identity types used to perform associated target track or search filtering.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="OffsetTrackSetting" type="uci:LOS_VariableB_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The offset track value commanded for the current capability as defined from the center of the LOS.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ObservedEntityThreshold" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Commanded value that defines the number of seconds since the last update of an Observed Entity before the data is considered to be stale.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TrackingRange" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The tracking range threshold commanded for the associated capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CoastSetting" type="uci:PO_CoastSettingValueType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="6">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Commanded value that defines the amount of time to coast a track before dropping it. The value should fall in the set of valid range values associated with the capability and associated environment setting. List size is based on allowing one per environment option available..</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BlankingVolume" type="uci:PO_AirTargetVolumeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The commanded blanking volume that constrains the LOS or track area from regions that the PO sensor would not be desirable for the current capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="PO_TrackSettingsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Commanded values for track parameters that will be used to customize target detections.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TrackOptionID" type="uci:TrackOptionsID_Type">
