	<xs:complexType name="QuerySpecificDataPET" abstract="true" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Base class to support polymorphic extensions that define application-specific queries not definable via QueryPETs. Available extension types include: IJMS_QuerySpecificDataType, Link11QuerySpecificDataType, Link16TN_QuerySpecificDataType, NATO_Link1QuerySpecificDataType, SelectionQuerySpecificDataType.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="QueryStepType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The mechanism by which queries navigate the data model of a UCI Message, which should be considered as a tree structure containing branch and leaf nodes.  Steps may either traverse up the tree (Ancestor and Parent), down the tree (Element, Descendant, and Child), or remain at the current context.  Steps are evaluated sequentially from the current context, with the default context of a query as the root of the tree, i.e. the top-level global element declaration.  The result of each Step forms a sequence of zero or more nodes that is then used as the input to the next Step, where each node of the input sequence is used as the current context with all sequences concatenated together, repeated until all Steps are evaluated.  Each node in this sequence is either a present optional field, a required field, or an item in a list.  For example, a Step that matches a list field with a length of two will result in a sequence of two nodes.  The resulting sequence is then evaluated by the query with a given operation.  Some operations, such as Equals, that operate on a single value are instead performed on each individual node in the sequence and the result is computed by the logical OR of all the results.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Element" type="uci:NamedElementType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Forms a sequence of zero or more nodes by navigating to the direct child of the current context with the specified local name and namespace URI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Root" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Forms a sequence of exactly one node that is the root of the current context.  This root is the Message that is the same context at which this query was initially evaluated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Ancestor" type="uci:WildcardElementType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Forms a sequence of zero or more nodes by navigating up the tree to any ancestor of the current context (regardless of depth) that matches the specified wildcard local name and namespace URI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Descendant" type="uci:WildcardElementType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Forms a sequence of zero or more nodes by navigating down the tree to any descendant of the current context (regardless of depth) that matches the specified wildcard local name and namespace URI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Parent" type="uci:WildcardElementType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Forms a sequence of one node (the parent of the current context) if the parent of the current context matches the specified wildcard local name and namespace URI, otherwise the empty sequence.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Child" type="uci:WildcardElementType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Forms a sequence of zero or more nodes by navigating down the tree to any direct child of the current context that matches the specified wildcard local name and namespace URI.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="QueryTopicPairType" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Binds a specific UCI message to a URI.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="MessageType" type="uci:MessageTypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Lists the type of message that is referenced.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ReceiverAddress" type="uci:VisibleString1024Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the address of the receiver to which the responding message should be sent. For example, this field could be a URI that identifies where and how to send the responding message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="QueryType" uci:version="001.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Defines the generic UCI Query Language (UQL) operations.  Each operation has a single input, a node that is the current context of the query, and will output either true or false.  When determining whether a Message should be sent in a corresponding status, it should be sent if the output of the query is true.  The data model of a UCI Message should be considered as a tree structure containing branch and leaf nodes.  The default context of a query is the Message, i.e. the top-level global element declaration.  Each UQL query is evaluated separately for each Message.  For more information on how the tree is evaluated, see the annotations in QueryStepType.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:QueryPET">
				<xs:choice>
					<xs:element name="Equals" type="uci:QueryEqualsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is equal to the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="LessThan" type="uci:QueryComparisonType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is less than the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="LessThanOrEqualTo" type="uci:QueryComparisonType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is less than or equal to the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="GreaterThan" type="uci:QueryComparisonType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is greater than the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="GreaterThanOrEqualTo" type="uci:QueryComparisonType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is greater than or equal to the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ContainsCaseSensitive" type="uci:QueryContainsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is a string value that has a substring (case-sensitive) equal to the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ContainsCaseInsensitive" type="uci:QueryContainsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is a string value that has a substring (case-insensitive) equal to the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="InstanceOf" type="uci:QueryInstanceOfType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is or derives from the given type name.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Count" type="uci:QueryCountType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if the length of the sequence formed by the Step sub-element matches the Value sub-element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Exists" type="uci:QueryExistsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if the sequence formed by the Step sub-element contains one or more nodes.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AnyMatch" type="uci:QueryMatchType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any node in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element is evaluated by the sub-query (i.e. the Test sub-element) to true.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AllMatch" type="uci:QueryMatchType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if all nodes in the sequence formed by the Step sub-element are evaluated by the sub-query (i.e. the Test sub-element) to true.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="And" type="uci:QueryPET" minOccurs="2" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if all of the sub-queries are evaluated to true.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Or" type="uci:QueryPET" minOccurs="2" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if any of the sub-queries are evaluated to true.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Not" type="uci:QueryPET">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Evaluates the query to true if the sub-query is evaluated to false.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:choice>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RaceTrackOrbitType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Duration" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The duration to maintain the racetrack orbit. If this is not provided, the intent is to maintain the orbit until commanded otherwise.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="StartLongitude" type="uci:AngleType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orbital line of longitude of the start of the racetrack measured in radians. Valid values range from -Pi to Pi.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EndLongitude" type="uci:AngleType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the orbital line of longitude of the end of the racetrack measured in radians. Valid values range from -Pi to Pi.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarActivityCommandType" uci:version="002.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ActivityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Attempt" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If specified, indicates the specific attempt of an activity to which this command applies.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionOptions" type="uci:RadarCollectionOptionsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates guidance regarding which aspect or aspects of collection to favor if the command cannot be optimally scheduled as requested.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityCommandType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureActivityCommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Attempt" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>If specified, indicates the specific attempt of an activity to which this command applies.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TemporalConstraints" type="uci:CapabilityCommandTemporalConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates temporal constraints for the command. If omitted, the command should be scheduled immediately while satisfying other applicable constraints.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="OverrideRejection" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates that the Command shall be performed even though it was previously rejected.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:CapabilityCommandFrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency to be used for the Command. If omitted, frequency selection is left to the command recipient within constraints of RF_Profiles imposed by RF_ControlCommand, MDF, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionOptions" type="uci:RadarAltimeterCollectionOptionsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates required optional aspects of the Capability to be included in the Command. Only those options supported by the Capability should be Commanded.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CollectionConstraints" type="uci:RadarAltimeterCollectionConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates constraints on the collection and/or processing.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AtmosphericPropagation" type="uci:AtmosphericPropagationLossType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Atmospheric propagation information to be used when determining SNR or range/power levels.  If multiple instances are given, each should be of a different band as indicated by the child element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SeaState" type="uci:WeatherSeaStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the sea state that should be assumed when performing the collection and processing. See enumerated type for further details; the enumeration corresponds to World Meteorological Organization definitions of sea state codes. These codes correspond to specific wave height values.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="TerrainType" type="uci:GroundTerrainTypeEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Descriptive text label or enumeration defining the type of ground (non-water) terrain that should be assumed when performing the RadarAltimeter collection and processing.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="BackScatterCoefficient" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the backscatter coefficient that should be assumed in performing the RadarAltimeter height measurement; in units of decibels.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Repetition" type="uci:RepetitionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the required repetition of the command. If omitted, the command should be performed once.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityEstimatedPerformanceType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SurfaceEnvironmentType" type="uci:EnvironmentEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Environment type of the targeted surface area being measured.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedProbabilityOfDetection" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Estimated probability of detection for the given targeted surface area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityMDT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Subsystem which hosts the RadarAltimeter Capabilities whose Activities are given in this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Activity" type="uci:RadarAltimeterActivityType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dynamic operational characteristics of an Activity of a RadarAltimeter Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityMetricsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specific performance metrics that provide the system insight regarding the progress of an activity, description of the results of an activity and related stats. This is a list to provide reporting for all revisits between activity messages.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Attempts" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>For the duration of this activity, this is the number of times the capability has attempted to generate an observation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualRevisitPeriod" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the average calculated amount of time between RadarAltimeter measurements since the capability was commanded to begin operation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualStartTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the first time at which this activity utilized front end resources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActualStopTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the last time at which this activity utilized front end resources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConcurrentActivity" type="uci:ConcurrentCollectionDetailsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the list of other activities that were executed concurrently with this activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PercentRadarTimeline" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the percentage of radar timeline which is taken up by this activity. The Revisit Rate and Time to Service both affect this metric. For instance an Activity might execute frequently and require a long Time To Service, meaning it would take up much radar timeline.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PercentageInFOV" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the percentage of the target collection area along the local normal/vertical that is currently in the radar FOV. The field of view is defined as the area where the radar can immediately see (typically some acceptable beamwidth portion of the main beam). The field of regard is defined as the area the radar can see after mechanical movement or rotation. Generally, the FOV is a subset of the FOR.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedERP" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum estimated Effective Radiated Power (ERP) at the face of the array used for this activity attempt. If this attempt requires multiple beam positions, then this is the maximum estimate across all positions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPerformance" type="uci:RadarAltimeterActivityEstimatedPerformanceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="5">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Estimated performance of the activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeToService" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the amount of time that is needed for a single visit/service of the Target area. This is different from Revisit Period, since other Activities are not taken into account when calculating this metric. This is the estimate of the time needed for the next service period.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LastTimeToService" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the amount of time that is needed for a single visit/service of the Target area. This is different from Revisit Period, since other Activities are not taken into account when calculating this metric. This is the actual completion time that was needed for the last successful service period.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AverageTimeToService" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the amount of time that is needed for a single visit/service of the Target area. This is the arithmetic mean of Service times over the last N visits, where N is an arbitrary number of visits greater than 1.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityMT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:RadarAltimeterActivityMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityPredictedActivityDetailType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ActivityState" type="uci:ActivityStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current state of the Activity state machine. See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivityReason" type="uci:CannotComplyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates details regarding the reason for and/or a contributing factor to the sibling ActivityState element. This element is only expected when the Activity is in a potentially undesirable state such as constrained, failed or completed with less than optimum results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedRevisitPeriod" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is an estimate of what observation revisit rate will likely be achieved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPercentageInFOV" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the percentage of the target collection area along the local normal/vertical that is currently in the radar FOV. The field of view is defined as the area where the radar can immediately see (typically some acceptable beamwidth portion of the main beam). The field of regard is defined as the area the radar can see after mechanical movement or rotation. Generally, the FOV is a subset of the FOR.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedStartTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the estimate of the time at which this revisit will first gain access to the front end timeline to perform the requested collection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedStopTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is the estimate of the time at which this revisit will complete the collection and no longer require access to the front end.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedERP" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Maximum estimated Effective Radiated Power (ERP) at the face of the array used for this activity attempt. If this attempt requires multiple spots, then this is the maximum estimate across all spots.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPerformance" type="uci:RadarAltimeterActivityEstimatedPerformanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Estimated performance of the activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ConcurrentExecutionAssumed" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Flag to communicate whether or not the model assumed that concurrent execution was assumed in the model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityPredictedCollectionsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="OwnshipLocation" type="uci:Point3D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This defines the ownship location at the start of the predicted collection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PredictedCollectionMetrics" type="uci:RadarAltimeterActivityPredictedActivityDetailType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines a set of fields which provide detailed information about the predicted activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterActivityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SharedRF_ApertureActivityBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SubCapability" type="uci:RadarAltimeterSubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="3">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific SubCapability associated with the Activity. If omitted, all SubCapabilities of the associated Capability are applicable for the Activity. This element is required whenever a subset of SubCapabilities of a Capability are used by the Activity. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Metrics" type="uci:RadarAltimeterActivityMetricsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Specific performance metrics that provide the system insight regarding the progress of an activity, description of the results of an activity and related stats.  This is a list to provide reporting for all revisits between activity messages.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Repetition" type="uci:RepetitionType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded repetition of the Activity. If omitted, the Activity is not repetitive.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PolicyApplied" type="xs:boolean" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>When TRUE, indicates the Activity could not be scheduled as requested but the radar was able to apply the command's CollectionPolicy and then successfully schedule or complete the activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AllMessagesProduced" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Flag indicating whether or not all messages (e.g., RadarAltimeterReport) expected to be produced by this activity have been output.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PredictedCollections" type="uci:RadarAltimeterActivityPredictedCollectionsType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Supports interaction with a capability assessment function. This allows a subsystem or a model of a subsystem to estimate future performance.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ElectronicProtectionOptionsEmployed" type="uci:ForeignKeyType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates which electronic protection IDs are in use for this activity.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="RadarAltimeterAngleConstraintsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Bounding allowable angular deviations from true vertical for the altimetry measurement.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ZX_AngularOffsetMax" type="uci:AngleHalfType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Contains the maximum limiting bound in the angle between the intended direction of peak directivity of the transmission beam and local level vertical along the z-x body plane (the x-axis is positive out the nose of the aircraft in the plane of symmetry of the aircraft, and the z-axis is perpendicular to the x-axis in the plane of symmetry of the aircraft and positive below the aircraft) measured in radians. Positive ZX Angular Offset is rotation from the positive z-axis towards the positive x-axis.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="YZ_AngularOffsetMax" type="uci:AngleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Contains the maximum limiting bound in the angle between the intended direction of peak directivity of the transmission beam and local level vertical along the y-z body plane (the y-axis is perpendicular to the x-z body plane and positive out the right, or starboard, wing) measured in radians. Positive YZ Angular Offset is rotation from the positive z-axis towards the negative y-axis.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
