					<xs:documentation>Indicates whether the Capability supports filtered, unfiltered, or both types of measurements. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ElectronicProtectionOptionsSupported" type="uci:ElectronicProtectionOptionsSupportedType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the list of EP capabilities that the current HW / SW allows an external actor to control for this capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FalseAlarmLevelUpperLimit" type="xs:unsignedByte" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the FalseAlarmLevel capability is supported and also defines the upper limit allowed by the capability. Used to set the quantity of sensitivity levels. If omitted tracking range selection is the full range of the reference type.</xs:documentation>
