	<xs:complexType name="ResponsePlanConstraintType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ResponsePlanID" type="uci:ResponsePlanID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the ResponsePlan being referenced.  When omitted, the current/active ResponsePlan for the System is implied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ChangeableAllocations" type="uci:PlanChangeableConstraintsEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates which kinds/categories of Responses in the ResponsePlan indicated by the sibling ResponsePlanID are considered changeable.  The exact definition of "changeable" is left to particular Services and/or Systems to develop according to their requirements.  A lenient interpretation would equate "changeable" with "removal allowed" thereby giving a System and/or planning Service freedom to remove any changeable Responses from the constraining plan in order to optimize a new *Plan for new and/or unchangeable Responses.  Those removed Responses would then be dealt with in subsequent planning steps/iterations.   With this definition, an "unchangeable" Response item is "System/vehicle constrained" and therefore the new *Plan being developed should avoid changes that would cause the item to be removed.  A stricter interpretation might additionally require that any temporal constraints of an unchangeable Response from the constraining ResponsePlan be unchanged as a result of the new *Plan being developed.  In a System of Systems with inter-*Plan temporal dependencies, this stricter interpretation could reduce automated replanning chain reactions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ResponseType" type="uci:ResponseTypeEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="4">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a type of Response in the ResponsePlan referenced by the sibling ResponsePlanID element that constrains the new *Plan.  If any are given, only Responses of the specified type or types are constraints.  If omitted, all Response types are constraints. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
