	<xs:complexType name="ResponsePlanInputsType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PlanInputsCoreType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="PlanningCandidate" type="uci:RequirementPlanningCandidateType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates specific Systems to consider and plan for along with System-specific planning constraints.  If omitted, all Tiers and all Systems at and below those that the planning process is applicable to shall be planned.  A System is a planning "candidate" because its plan may or may not change as a result of the command; zero to one Plans per *Plan type will potentially be created for each candidate.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProposedResponsePlan" type="uci:ResponsePlanConstraintType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an existing ResponsePlan of the System superior to the sibling PlanningCandidates that provides a proposed "response deck" to allocate amongst the candidates.  This element can be supplemented with additional Responses from the sibling ProposedResponse element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ProposedResponse" type="uci:ResponseAllocationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a proposed Response for the planning process.  A Response given here is added to any Responses provided in the sibling ProposedResponsePlan to create the full set of Responses to be considered by the planning process.  A Response given here overrides the same Response in the sibling ProposedResponsePlan.  An empty list here, combined with no sibling ProposedResponsePlan is considered a command to deallocate previously allocated Tasks.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="AssociationConstraint" type="uci:RequirementAssociationConstraintType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates an association between Requirements that is a constraint on how the Responses are allocated and planned.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="OutputPlanParts" type="uci:ResponsePlanPartsType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a Part that is required in the output ResponsePlan.  When populated, this element must match or be a subset of the Parts associated with the planning process (sibling PlanningProcessID) as advertised in PlanningFunction*messages.  This element is optional when all Parts of the process are required.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
