	<xs:complexType name="ServiceRegistrationRequestMDT" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Sent by a service requesting to be registered for specific mission purposes/functions/mission critical transitions.  Allows a service to announce what functions they provide (what its purposes are) that are not related to a Capability.  For example this could be used for mission processing service orchestration along with a system level orchestrator that understands the system needs in executing specific Mission behaviors.  Allows multiple services to be available (register) to perform functions that are not typical capabilities such as Mission Planning, Routing, Assessment Models, and Task Allocation.  Then the system level orchestrator can determine which of multiple services available for a specific function should be performing the function based on current and/or specific mission objectives.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:RequestBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ServiceID" type="uci:ServiceID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
