	<xs:complexType name="STANAG_4607_PackingPlanPET" abstract="true" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The base Polymorphic Extension Type (PET) used by STANAG 4607 packing plan types.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="STANAG_4607_PackingPlanRevA_Type" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Defines the fields required to be passed from the MTI tasking authority (ACTDF, ATO, target deck spreadsheet, email, chat, whatever) to the platform for inclusion in its STANAG 4607 product.  NOTE: This is an updated version of the original STANAG_4607_PackingPlanType that addresses the problems described for that version herein.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:STANAG_4607_PackingPlanPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Nationality" type="uci:CharOrSpacePairsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This is the nationality of the platform generating the STANAG 4607 product. STANAG 4607 Packet Header field P3 (Nationality), from ACTDF Country Code. A digraph, in accordance with FIPS Publication 10-4, which identifies the nationality of the platform providing the GMTI data. NATO platforms providing GMTI data shall use the digraph XN.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PacketSecurityClassification" type="uci:STANAG_4607_PacketSecurityClassificationType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>STANAG 4607 Packet Header field P4 (Packet Security Classification), from ACTDF Classification. Valid values are
1=Top Secret
2=Secret
3=Confidential
4=Restricted
5=Unclassified.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PacketSecurityClassificationSystem" type="uci:CharOrSpacePairsType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>STANAG 4607 Packet Header field P5 (Packet Security Class. System), from ACTDF File Security Classification System. This field must contain valid values indicating the national or multinational security system used to classify the file. Country Codes per FIPS PUB 10-4 must be used to indicate national security systems. The designator "XN" is for classified data generated by a component using NATO security system marking guidance. This code is outside the FIPS 10-4 document listing, and was selected to not duplicate that document's existing codes.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PacketSecurityCode" type="xs:unsignedShort">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>STANAG 4607 Packet Header field P6 (Packet Security Code), from ACTDF File Security Code. A two-byte flag field, defined in STANAG 4607 Table 2-1.3, that indicates additional control and/or handling instructions associated with the GMTI data. A value of 0 (hex 0x00) indicates there are no additional security codes that apply to the GMTI data. Each bit of the field, when set to a binary "1", indicates that the corresponding security code in Table 2-1.3 applies to the data. This field allows multiple security codes to be associated with the GMTI data. (NOTE: This table is representative, based on US security handling codes, and is not an exhaustive list of all allowable codes. Each nation shall be responsible for developing and publishing their own packet security handling codes as required.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ExerciseIndicator" type="xs:unsignedByte">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>STANAG 4607 Packet Header field P7 (Exercise Indicator) from ACTDF Exercise Indicator. An enumeration table indicating whether the data contained in this packet is from a real-world military operation or from an exercise, and whether the data is real (originates from live-fly or other non-simulated operational sources), simulated (originates from target simulator sources), or synthesized (a mix of real and simulated data). Allowable values are defined in STANAG 4607 Table 2-1.4, repeated below:.
0 = Operation, Real Data
1 = Operation, Simulated Data
2 = Operation, Synthesized Data
3-127 = Reserved
128 = Exercise, Real Data
129 = Exercise, Simulated Data
130 = Exercise, Synthesized Data
131-255 = Reserved.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PlatformIdentifier" type="uci:VisibleString10Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>STANAG 4607 Packet Header field P8 (Platform ID) from ACTDF Platform ID. Optional, will be supplied by platform if not supplied by ACTDF. An alphanumeric field that identifies the platform. For aircraft the platform ID shall be the tail number. For a space-based platform the platform ID shall be the satellite name with an appropriate numerical designator. For other systems, an appropriate unique designator shall be used. Unused bytes shall be filled with the BCS space character (hex 0x20). In all cases, the platform ID is determined by the nation owning the platform, whose responsibility it is to ensure that all its platforms are uniquely identified within the set of platforms it owns.  NOTE:  The BCS character set includes CR, LF, and FF but XML 1.0 does not support FF (0x0C) so it has been omitted from this restriction. When an update to a compatible version of XML is approved, the "0x0C" can be reintroduced and this NOTE removed.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MissionPlan" type="uci:STANAG_4607_PlanType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Surface Moving Target Indicator mission plan identification. For STANAG 4607 Mission Segment Mission Plan field M1, from the ATO or the ACTDF Mission Plan field. An alphanumeric field that identifies the mission, and which shall be unique for all the missions defined for that platform. For aircraft or land-based systems, the Mission Number from the Air Tasking Order (ATO) or an equivalent document shall be used. For space-based platforms, the mission identifier or a suitable designator such as "yymmhhnn", where yy (year), mm (month), and hh (hour) indicate the time the collection mission began and nn is the identifying number of the satellite, shall be used. If there is no Mission Plan to be sent, or if there are unused bytes in the field, the field shall be filled with the BCS space character (hex 0x20).  NOTE:  The BCS character set includes CR, LF, and FF but XML 1.0 does not support FF (0x0C) so it has been omitted from this restriction. When an update to a compatible version of XML is approved, the "0x0C" can be reintroduced and this NOTE removed.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FlightPlan" type="uci:STANAG_4607_PlanType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>For STANAG 4607 Mission Segment Flight Plan field M2, from the ATO or the ACTDF Flight Plan field. An alphanumeric field that identifies the flight plan. This field provides a unique identification of the flight plan. If the flight plan is not available from the ATO or an equivalent source, a suitable unique identifier may be inserted in this field. If there is no Flight Plan to be sent, or if there are unused bytes in the field, the field shall be filled with the BCS space character (hex 0x20).  NOTE:  The BCS character set includes CR, LF, and FF but XML 1.0 does not support FF (0x0C) so it has been omitted from this restriction. When an update to a compatible version of XML is approved, the "0x0C" can be reintroduced and this NOTE removed.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="STANAG_4607_PackingPlanType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>NOTE: This version of the STANAG_4607_PackingPlanType suffers from the following problems: Some elements are one space longer than allowed by STANAG_4607; some elements' lengths are off by more, short or long; some segments and elements are extraneous (set by platform, not needed in UCI Task message), while other required tasking authority fields are missing; and some required fields are marked optional. The RevisedSTANAG_4607_PackingPlanType resolves these problems.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:STANAG_4607_PackingPlanPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ExerciseIdentifier" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Surface Moving Target Indicator exercise identification.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ClassificationSystem" type="uci:FIPS_ClassificationSystemType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>This field shall contain valid values indicating the national or multinational security system used to classify the file. Country Codes per FIPS PUB 10-4 shall be used to indicate national security systems. The designator "XN" is for classified data generated by a component using NATO security system marking guidance. This code is outside the FIPS 10-4 document listing, and was selected to not duplicate that document's existing codes.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="OriginatorIdentifier" type="uci:AlphanumericDashSpaceUnderscoreString11Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Surface Moving Target Indicator originator identification.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MissionPlan" type="uci:AlphanumericDashSpaceUnderscoreString13Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Surface Moving Target Indicator mission plan identification.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Recipient" type="uci:AlphanumericDashSpaceUnderscoreString11Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Surface Moving Target Indicator data recipient identification.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FreeText" type="uci:VisibleString81Type" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Surface Moving Target Indicator description.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StandardIdentityConfidenceType" uci:version="002.001.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:StandardIdentityType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Confidence" type="uci:PercentType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the confidence of the StandardIdentity declaration.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ExerciseIdentityData" type="uci:ExerciseIdentityType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The entity's exercise identity and allegiance. The sibling StandardIdentity is expected to be FRIEND and the sibling Confidence element is expected to be 100% when this optional element is used. Derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUI 376/001 for additional details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SpecialIdentity" type="uci:SpecialIdentityEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates a type of special interest track like KILO, ZOMBIE, TRAVELER, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StandardIdentityType" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="StandardIdentity" type="uci:StandardIdentityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the "standard identity" of the Entity. Derived from MIL-STD-6016; see MIL-STD-6016 DFI/DUI 376/007 for additional details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Allegiance" type="uci:CountryCodeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>DOD standard country code designator to which an entity owes its allegiance.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StateCovarianceNED_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates position, velocity and acceleration covariance in the NED coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:PositionAndVelocityCovarianceType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="AccelerationAcceleration" type="uci:AccelerationAccelerationCovarianceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates acceleration-acceleration covariance in the NED coordinate system.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="PositionAcceleration" type="uci:PositionAccelerationCovarianceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates position-acceleration covariance in the NED coordinate system. Required when the sibling acceleration-acceleration covariance is populated.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="VelocityAcceleration" type="uci:VelocityAccelerationCovarianceType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates velocity-acceleration covariance in the NED coordinate system. Required when the sibling velocity-velocity and acceleration-acceleration covariances are populated.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SteeringUnitVectorType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Steering unit vector and its defined coordinate frame.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="LOS_ReferenceFrame" type="uci:LOS_ReferenceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the base reference frame for the LOS_UnitVector data. Four reference frame options are enumerated: Body, NED, Inertial, and Capability. The Body frame is defined relative to the host platform, the NED frame is a local North, East, Down frame, the Inertial frame is similar to the NED frame with the addition of a Wander Angle, the Capability frame is defined with respect to the subsystem providing the associated Capability. Additional details can be found in the annotations for each enumeration value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CapabilityID" type="uci:CapabilityID_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This indicates the Capability that defines the reference frame for the LOS unit vector when the Capability Enumeration is used in the LOS_ReferenceFrame element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LOS_UnitVector" type="uci:UnitVectorType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Line of sight vector from the system to the Entity. The meaning of the X,Y,Z components of the LOS vector depends upon the enumeration value of the sibling LOS_ReferenceFrame element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StorageDetailType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="StorageDeviceName" type="uci:VisibleString256Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The name of the storage device.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Size" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The size of the storage device in MB.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Used" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The number of MB used by this storage device.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Available" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The number of MB available for this storage device.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StoreCarriageCapabilityStatusBaseType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
