	<xs:complexType name="StrikeTaskMetricsTargetingType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="Quality" type="xs:float">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element represents the positional accuracy of the entity.  It is the area, in square data miles, within which it is assessed that there is a 95% probability that the track/point lies.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="UncertaintyEllipse" type="uci:EllipseType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element represents an ellipse describing the position uncertainty.  The ellipse is defined by the length of its semi-major and semi-minor axes.  The orientation of the ellipse defines the angle between the semi-major axis and true north.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StrikeTaskMetricsType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NumWeaponsReleased" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The number of weapons released for this task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Targeting" type="uci:StrikeTaskMetricsTargetingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a metric on the quality of targeting associated with the strike.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BDI_Collection" type="uci:BDI_CollectionType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Bomb Damage Indication (BDI) metrics include quality of the strike and the confidence of the metric.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StrikeTaskReleaseConstraintsType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="ReleasePoint" type="uci:Point3D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Release point within a Launch Acceptable Region (LAR).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ReleaseArea" type="uci:AreaConstraintsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines an area where release is acceptable.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StrikeTaskType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Target" type="uci:TargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates or references geospatial characteristics of the Strike target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TargetInformation" type="uci:TargetInformationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides additional information on the target of the strike task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="IngressConstraint" type="uci:AnglePairType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Min and Max Ingress Angle defines the acceptable range of bearing-from-target values that the strike vehicle must satisfy at weapon release.  Bearing from target is defined as the true heading from the target point to the weapon release point. Because of wrap-around Max value can be smaller than Min value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EgressConstraint" type="uci:AnglePairType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Min and Max Egress Angle defines the acceptable range of bearing-from-target values that the strike vehicle must satisfy after weapon release.  Bearing from target is defined as the true heading from the target point to the weapon release point. Because of wrap-around Max value can be smaller than Min value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="InitialPoint" type="uci:Point3D_Type" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the point from which to ingress.  This element can be provided in an ATO.  Otherwise, the IP can be left to the tasked system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ReleaseConstraints" type="uci:StrikeTaskReleaseConstraintsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies constraints on the release conditions of the weapon.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WeaponList" type="uci:StrikeTaskWeaponListType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates weapon or weapons for the Strike.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NoStrike" type="uci:EmptyType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If element is present, indicates this task should be planned as if it does not expend a weapon. It still requires that the needed store types still be available at time of execution. It is intended that this task will only be executed if the primary task was unable to be completed for any reason. In the off nominal case where this task is required to execute, the ability to execute tasks after this will have to be reevaluated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StrikeTaskWeaponListType" uci:version="002.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Weapon" type="uci:StrikeTaskWeaponType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a type and quantity of weapon to be used for the strike.  Multiple instances of this element with the child RequiredWeapon element indicating TRUE should be considered as being all required and could include a mixture of weapon/store types.  Multiple instances with RequiredWeapon set FALSE indicate that any one will be sufficient for the Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StrikeTaskWeaponType" uci:version="002.001.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:WeaponeeringType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="RequiredWeapon" type="xs:boolean">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates that the specified weapon is a required weapon for the strike (TRUE); if the required weapon isn't available then the strike Task should not be executed.  Otherwise (FALSE) indicates that the weapon is a sufficient choice.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StrikeWeaponCommandType" uci:version="001.001.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="SelectForKeyLoad" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If true, this store will be commanded into a state where it is ready to receive cryptographic keys.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssignTarget" type="uci:GeoLocatedObjectType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The identifier used to uniquely address the target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WeaponArm" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>When true, the weapon is commanded to the armed state.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SelectForJettison" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If true, this store will be selected for ejection from the host platform without being armed or otherwise prepared for launch.  The next time all release conditions are met and release consent is provided this store will be jettisoned.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GenerateDynamicLAR" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the weapon will calculate the LAR information.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SelectForRelease" type="xs:boolean">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If true, the next time all release conditions are met and release consent is provided this store will be released.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SelectAO_Code" type="uci:AO_CodeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a PRF and/or PIM code supported by this store.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StructureAssessmentCharacterizationType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Conduct collection to support assessment of spacecraft structure to provide baseline or foundational characterization or to enable change detection.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SizeEstimation" type="uci:SizeEstimationCharacterizationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Conduct collection to enable estimation of size of object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Resolved" type="uci:ResolvedCharacterizationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Conduct collection (and appropriate processing) to support assessment of length, width, height of a spacecraft as well as similar values and relative positions/orientations of spacecraft components (e.g., solar panels, telescopes, antennae).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="StructureAssessmentType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a task and requirements to enable characterization of or assessment of changes to the structure of a spacecraft.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="SizeEstimation" type="uci:SizeEstimationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Task for collections to enable the estimation of the size of the object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Resolved" type="uci:ResolvedCharacterizationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Conduct collection (and appropriate processing) to support assessment of length, width, height of a spacecraft as well as similar values and relative positions/orientations of spacecraft components (e.g., solar panels, telescopes, antennae).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubCapabilityDetailsType" uci:version="003.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SelectAntenna" type="uci:SelectAntennaType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a Shared Antenna and/or AntennaResources to be used for the EA activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FrequencyRestriction" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific frequency to be used for the Acquisition command.  If omitted, the command defers to the active MDF.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TargetEmitterData" type="uci:ESM_TargetType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of or explicit values for emitter characteristics of the target.  If omitted, the emitter characteristics should be determined from the active MDF.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ESM_Location" type="uci:ESM_LocationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of or explicit values for the kinematic location of the target or search volume.  When specified, the kinematic location overrides any given in the sibling TargetEmitterData element.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PulseDataCollection" type="uci:PulseDataCollectCommandType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the parameters used to collect pulses.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Geolocation" type="uci:ESM_SubcapabilityGeolocationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This indicates the commanded geolocation type/technique to use.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubCapabilityID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to resource capabilities.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubCapabilitySelectionType" uci:version="003.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubCapability" type="uci:ESM_SubCapabilityEnum" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="12">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a specific ESM SubCapability being invoked by the command.  If omitted, all SubCapabilities of the CapabilityID are to be invoked.  If specified, only those SubCapabilities specified are required in order to satisfy the command.  See enumeration annotations for further details. This element is required, in order to qualify the affected SubCapability for the ResourceAccessPriority (and other antenna/resource attributes) in the sibling SubCapabilityDetails. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubCapabilityDetails" type="uci:SubCapabilityDetailsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the details required for a subcapability. at least one of the data sets need to be populated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubjectType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates whether an UCI Entity subject or an UCI System subject is to be selected.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="SystemID" type="uci:SystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a UCI System subject.  See the SystemStatus message annotations for details of what it means to be a UCI System.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a UCI Entity subject.  See the Entity message annotations for details of what it means to be a UCI Entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubordinatePlanningProcessType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PlanningProcessID" type="uci:PlanningProcessID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique identifier of the subordinate planning process.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AppliesTo" type="uci:AppliesToType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates what System, Subsystem, and/or, Service the subordinate planning process applies to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubPlanActivationSettingType" uci:version="001.000.001.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubPlan" type="uci:SubPlanTypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the SubPlan type which the sibling ActivationCommand applies to.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActivationCommand" type="uci:PlanActivationCommandEnum" maxOccurs="7">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a step in the MissionPlan activation process. List size for this element is based on "Select All That Apply" condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubPlansModificationType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specifies details pertaining to the Sub Plans Modification.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubPlansAdditions" type="uci:PlansReferenceBaseType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an additional set of *Plans which are included as part of the MissionPlan. The included SubPlans share the same Applicability as the MissionPlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubPlansRetractions" type="uci:PlansReferenceBaseType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the removal of set of *Plans which are included as part of the MissionPlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemActiveBIT_Type" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="BIT_ID" type="uci:BIT_ID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the BIT.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedCompletionTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimated time at which the BIT will complete.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPercentComplete" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current estimated percent complete of the BIT.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemActiveCalibrationType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates estimates on completion time of the active calibration.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="CalibrationID" type="uci:CalibrationID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the calibration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedCompletionTime" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the estimated time at which the calibration will complete.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EstimatedPercentComplete" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current estimated percent complete of the calibration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_CommandMDT" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:CommandBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Subsystem being commanded to perform the sibling CommandType.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="CommandType" type="uci:SubsystemBIT_CommandType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of BIT related action or actions to perform.  As this message can be used to aggregate several actions in a single command, it is anticipated that the receiving Subsystem would accept or reject the command as a whole, and subsequently use the SubsystemBIT_Status message to report at the individual BIT/fault level.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:CapabilityCommandFrequencyType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the frequency to be used for the Command.  If omitted, frequency selection, if relevant to the Subsystem, is left to the command recipient within constraints of RF_Profiles imposed by RF_ControlCommand, MDF, etc.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_CommandMT" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:SubsystemBIT_CommandMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_CommandStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SubsystemCommandStatusBaseType" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_CommandStatusMT" uci:version="002.001.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:SubsystemBIT_CommandStatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_CommandType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Identifies specific BIT IDs or Fault codes relevant to this command.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="InitiateBIT_ID" type="uci:BIT_ID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID or IDs of the BIT or BITs to initiate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CancelBIT_ID" type="uci:BIT_ID_Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID or IDs of the BIT or BITs to cancel.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ClearFaultCode" type="uci:VisibleString256Type" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the "codes" or names of the faults to clear.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_ConfigurationID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to SubsystemBIT_Configurations.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_ConfigurationMDT" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemBIT_ConfigurationID" type="uci:SubsystemBIT_ConfigurationID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a unique ID assigned to the SubsystemBIT_Configuration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Subsystem corresponding to this message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BIT" type="uci:SubsystemBIT_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a BIT supported by the Subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_ConfigurationMT" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ObjectState" type="uci:ObjectStateEnum" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the internal software object that the data in the message is based upon.  The state of the software object is determined by the publisher.  The publisher could be the original/master publisher or an intermediary re-publisher such as a persistence/data manager.  This element is not a commanded CRUD operation.  It is not an indication of the state of an instance of a message.  It is not a mechanism for partial, incremental, or fragmentary publication of a message.  It is a signal from a publisher to subscribers.  For REMOVED state, in particular, some subscribers will mirror the publisher and treat the message as if the object no longer exists, but others, such as mission recorders, might not (in order to support retaining historical records of activity, for example).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:SubsystemBIT_ConfigurationMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_StatusMDT" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SubsystemID" type="uci:SubsystemID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the Subsystem whose BIT status is being reported.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ActiveBIT" type="uci:SubsystemActiveBIT_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a BIT that is currently running or enqueued to run.  This element can be used for BIT initiated via SubsystemStateCommand, SubsystemBIT_Command and/or by the Subsystem itself (periodic BIT (PBIT), background BIT (BBIT), start-up BIT (SBIT), etc.).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CompletedBIT" type="uci:SubsystemCompletedBIT_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates results of a previously completed BIT.  This element can be used for results from BIT initiated via SubsystemStateCommand, SubsystemBIT_Command and/or self-initiated by the Subsystem.  Subsystem self-initiated BIT examples include periodic BIT (PBIT),  background BIT (BBIT), startup BIT (SBIT), maintenance BIT (MBIT), etc.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Fault" type="uci:SubsystemFaultType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a current fault in the Subsystem.  When omitted, the Subsystem has no current faults.  Faults aren't necessarily related to or exclusively detected by BIT.  This element is independent of the sibling CompletedBIT so that faults can be reported regardless of how they were detected or triggered.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_StatusMT" uci:version="001.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:SubsystemBIT_StatusMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="SubsystemBIT_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="BIT_ID" type="uci:BIT_ID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the BIT along with its human readable name.  This ID is used to initiate the BIT via SubsystemBIT_Command and status the BIT via SubsystemBIT_Status.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
