				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreadConfigurationRF_Type" uci:version="001.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="BeamConfigurationIndex" type="xs:unsignedInt">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The allocation includes the actual BeamConfigurationIndices to be used for each AntennaID. The number maps to an actual beam buffer in the antenna (or is set to "1" for a simple antenna), so the BeamConfigurationIndex cannot exceed the number of BeamBufferSize identified in the Shared Aperture Information File.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SupportCapabilityID" type="uci:SupportCapabilityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique identifier for this particular antenna.  This can also be used to describe a towed decoy as the radiating source. AntennaID is the same as the Antenna SupportCapabilityID.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AntennaResourceInstanceID" type="uci:AntennaResourceID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of a specific resource (such a "Transmit, Quarter Sub-Array Number Three") on a Shared Antenna. Defined in Shared Aperture Information Files.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="RF_Mode" type="uci:RF_TypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates if the resource is for Rx or Tx.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BeamPowerMode" type="uci:BeamPowerModeEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Selects LINEAR or COMPRESSED power mode.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Frequency" type="uci:FrequencyRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Center Frequency of the Beam.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BeamPointingReference" type="uci:BeamPointingReferenceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Beam Pointing Information for a directed beam.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Polarization" type="uci:PolarizationControlType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Polarization description for the beam.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AntennaAttenuation" type="uci:DecibelType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Attenuate the Beam power by this amount.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AntennaPriority" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Used by Antennas for internal prioritization, such as using a FIFO Beam Command Concept to push higher in the Antenna Queue, or for managing saturation when more than one RFTI shares antenna resources.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BeamShaping" type="uci:BeamShapingType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Supports limited Beam Shaping Direction to the Antenna.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatAssessmentMetricsType" uci:version="002.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Acquisition" type="uci:ThreatAssessmentProbabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the detection chance. The probability of detection is conversion of the calculated signal to noise ratio via a Swerling model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Track" type="uci:ThreatAssessmentProbabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the track chance. The probability of track uses scan period, chance of detection, and required number of detections in a frame to determine if the radar tracker has initiated/maintained a track.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Launch" type="uci:ThreatAssessmentProbabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines missile launch opportunities, defined as a tracking radar exposure that occurs at a time when a valid kinematic missile firing solution exists.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Intercept" type="uci:ThreatAssessmentProbabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines missile intercept opportunities, defined as a launch opportunity followed by a sufficient time period of tracking/guidance radar detection to guide the missile all the way to intercept, with no detection dropouts longer than the missile's coast time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Kill" type="uci:ThreatAssessmentProbabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the probability the vehicle will not survive the intercept opportunity. The probability should be a function of intercept probability, and potentially predicted intercept geometry, depending on algorithm fidelity. The individual kill probabilities shall be able to be combined to determine the overall chance of the vehicle surviving the route.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DetectionEnvelope" type="uci:DetectionEnvelopeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the detection characteristics of the vehicle as a "BugSplat".</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ThreatZone" type="uci:ThreatZoneType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the threat zone around an entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatAssessmentProbabilityType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EffectiveProbability" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Probability of the metric.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ExposureTime" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides the time duration since the last position that the exposure has happened.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatAssessmentRequestType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The inputs used in generating and/or requesting a Route Threat Assessment.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ThreatCapability" type="uci:ThreatCapabilityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the threat capability to assess (i.e. - detection method or technology).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ThreatSuppression" type="uci:AssessmentSuppressionEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element specifies whether the assessment results should include suppression of the sibling ThreatCapability or not. The INCLUDE_BOTH option indicates that the results should include assessments with and without suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ThreatEntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element indicates a specific threat Entity to assess.  If omitted, all relevant threat Entities are assessed.  If any are given, only they are assessed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssessmentInterval" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element specifies the time interval at which assessment results should be rolled up in the assessment results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SystemToAssess" type="uci:SystemRoutePlanSpecificationType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a System or Systems to assess given their RoutePlan and available capabilities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SupportingSystem" type="uci:SystemRoutePlanSpecificationType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates additional systems to be considered for the assessment, but are not assessed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatAssessmentSystemType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>ID of threat which is detecting the vehicle.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WithoutSuppression" type="uci:ThreatAssessmentMetricsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element provides the predicted threat assessment of a mission plan without suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WithSuppression" type="uci:ThreatAssessmentMetricsType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element provides the predicted threat assessment of a mission plan with suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatExposureProbabilityType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TimeIndex" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the second that was used to calculate the probability of exposure.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProbabilityOfDetection" type="uci:PercentType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the probably of exposure for the given time segment (second) incurred due to the associated threat.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatExposureType" uci:version="001.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the unique Entity that is causing the exposure being described.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ExposureTime" type="uci:DurationType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides the time duration along the route or path segment that have exposure time for the specified threat.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ExposureEvent" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides a method for defining exposure events along a route path or segment into time segments against a particular threat. An exposure event is defined as a time ranges during which exposure to a particular threat occurs.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ExposureEventPosition" type="uci:Point2D_RangeType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the threat exposure event positions along a route path against a particular threat as a set of locations; sibling ExposureEvent provides exposure with respect to time. An exposure event position is defined as a start point to an end point during which exposure to a particular threat occurs.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ProbabilityMetrics" type="uci:ThreatExposureProbabilityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides a method for breaking the exposure probabilities along a route path or segment into time segments against a particular threat.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatNominationAssessmentDataType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The results of an assessment that determines which entity poses the highest threat to a system or systems.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="NominationWithoutSuppression" type="uci:ThreatNominationResultType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the threat nomination result without suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NominationWithSuppression" type="uci:ThreatNominationResultType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the threat nomination result with suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatNominationAssessmentRequestType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The inputs used in generating and/or requesting a Threat Nomination Assessment.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SystemToConsider" type="uci:SystemRoutePlanSpecificationType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Systems to be considered for the assessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AssessmentSuppression" type="uci:AssessmentSuppressionEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element specifies whether the assessment should generate results which include suppression or not. The INCLUDE_BOTH option indicates that the results should include assessments with and without suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A list of entities that can be utilized during nomination (zero entities assumes that all entities can be nominated).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatNominationAssessmentType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Base data structure containing both the inputs and outputs for a Threat Nomination Assessment.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Parameters" type="uci:ThreatNominationAssessmentRequestType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the parameters used in calculating the sibling results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Data" type="uci:ThreatNominationAssessmentDataType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the results of a threat nomination assessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatNominationResultType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The best entity to nominate based on the overall reduction in exposure and flight time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EntityNominationResults" type="uci:EntityNominationResultType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A list of threat nomination results for each individual system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GlobalExposureReduction" type="uci:PercentType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The percent reduction in the exposures for all systems if the nominated threat is removed from the mission.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="GlobalFlightTimeReduction" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The percent reduction in the flight time for all systems if the nominated threat is removed from the mission.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatVulnerabilityByCapabilityType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ThreatCapability" type="uci:ThreatCapabilityEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the category of threat for the sibling vulnerability threshold.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Threshold" type="uci:ThresholdVulnerabilityType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If the detection costs of a generated *Plan exceed these levels then approval is required in all cases. This data is optionally associated to the NEW_THREAT trigger.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThreatZoneType" uci:version="001.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="ThreatZoneArea" type="uci:AreaChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Geospatial zone where the associated Entity can threaten the vehicle.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="DetectionEnvelopeViolationSeverity" type="uci:RiskPrioritizationEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies how severe the associated Entity is violating the detection envelope.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EffectiveProbability" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The effective probability of detect for thiis TheatZoneArea.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThresholdOffOrbitTriggerDataType" uci:version="002.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>A trigger that refers to a spacecraft that has deviated from its planned orbit to such a degree that a replan is required.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="PositionErrorThreshold" type="uci:RTN_PositionDeltaType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threshold for position error of the spacecraft's orbit expressed in Radial-Transverse-Normal coordinates.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VelocityErrorThreshold" type="uci:RTN_VelocityDeltaType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threshold velocity error of the spacecraft's orbit expressed in Radial-Transverse-Normal coordinates.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeThreshold" type="uci:TimeErrorType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time difference threshold between the planned time and the current time which would demonstrate a spacecraft has deviated from the planned route to such a degree that a replan is required.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThresholdOffRouteTriggerDataType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TrackError" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Cross track error of flight path.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AltitudeError" type="uci:DistanceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Altitude error of flight path.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeError" type="uci:TimeErrorType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time difference threshold between the planned time and the current time which would demonstrate a vehicle has deviated from the planned route to such a degree that a replan is required.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThresholdVulnerabilityType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="VulnerabilityWithoutSuppression" type="uci:VulnerabilityLevelsCombinedType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the threshold levels of vulnerability for the *Plan without suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="VulnerabilityWithSuppression" type="uci:VulnerabilityLevelsCombinedType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies the threshold levels with suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ExposureEventProbabilityThreshold" type="uci:PercentType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Defines the probability of exposure that estimated exposure calculations must exceed to be counted as an actual exposure event. The length of time of exposure events are used to calculate Composite and Cumulative exposure times.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="ThumbnailType" uci:version="000.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Description" type="uci:ProductOutputType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the content and format of the Product thumbnail.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="FileName" type="uci:FileNameType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element defines the file name of the stored thumbnail.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimeAndPolarDataType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Information on offsets between time systems and on polar motion, both of which are available from the Naval Observatory International Earth Rotation Service.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TAI_UTC_Difference" type="xs:int">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>TAI - UTC.  Difference between International Atomic Time (TAI) and Coordinated Universal Time (UTC), number of leap seconds since the beginning of GPS time, always a whole number of seconds.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="UT1_UTC_Difference" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>UT1 - UTC offset, units of seconds. A common range is (-10,10).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="UT1_Rate" type="xs:double">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the linear drift of UT1-UTC, units of msec/day. A common range is (-10,10).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="PolarMotion" type="uci:PolarMotionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the x and y coordinates of polar motion.  Reference http://www.iers.org/IERS/EN/Science/EarthRotation/PolarMotion.html.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NutationModelTerms" type="xs:int">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the number of terms of the nutation model to be used.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="NextLeapSecond" type="uci:DateTimeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Time of the next scheduled leap second.  May be omitted if the information is unknown or unscheduled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimeAndPolarRecordType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Information on offsets between time systems and on polar motion, both of which are available from the Naval Observatory International Earth Rotation Service.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:TimeAndPolarDataType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Epoch" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the time range when the sibling EOP data is applicable.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimeCoverageType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="TimeSpan" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the range of time that this time coverage specification is good for.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CoverageArea" type="uci:ZoneType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the specific area that is covered by this time coverage specification.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimedZoneType" uci:version="002.000.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Extends ZoneType with a time schedule during which the zone applies.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ZoneType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Schedule" type="uci:ScheduleType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the time schedule (multiple time spans, periodic availability or both) when the zone is applicable.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimeErrorType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Early" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The difference between the planned time and the current time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Late" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The difference between the planned time and the current time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimeFunctionType" uci:version="000.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>A time and its associated function or purpose.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Function" type="uci:TimeFunctionEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The operational function of the Value.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Value" type="uci:DateTimeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The time when the associated object will perform the Function.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimeWindowType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Range" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the begin and end times for the time window.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Duration" type="uci:DurationType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the duration or active/execution time for the time window.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TimingConstraintsType" uci:version="003.000.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Provides a choice of timing constraints including repetitive timing and event based repetition.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="AsSoonAsPossible" type="uci:EmptyType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the timing should be As Soon As Possible.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TimeWindow" type="uci:TimeWindowType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the time window during which the Requirement should be initiated and, once initiated, the duration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="WeekdayInterval" type="uci:WeekdayIntervalType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a recurring time.  For example, a recurring time as a constraint on a Task may result in the need for a Task or other Requirement to be broken down into multiple discrete children corresponding to each interval.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Repetitive" type="uci:RepetitionConstraintsType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a repetition and defines the number and frequency of product collection and generation such as start/stop/frequency or min # of collections.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TLE_BaseType" uci:version="002.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the default or "catalog" orbital element set (also known as two line element or TLE) for the satellite.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:COE_OrbitBaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="Epoch" type="uci:DateTimeType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Time at which the orbital elements are valid. Formatted as UTC DateTime values.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ElementSetNumber" type="xs:unsignedShort" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The element set number is a carryover from the legacy Two Line Element set (TLE) format, and is provided to support processes that transform to/from that format. Element Set Number increments with each newly generated element set. A common range is [0,999].</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="FirstTimeDerivativeOfMeanMotion" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>First time derivative of the mean motion, in units of revolutions per day. This field is only used with the SGP orbital model (ephemeris type = 1).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="SecondTimeDerivativeOfMeanMotion" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Second time derivative of the mean motion, in units of revolutions per day. This field is only used with the SGP orbital model (ephemeris type = 1).</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="BSTAR_Drag" type="xs:double" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Ballistic drag coefficient.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Position" type="uci:COE_PositionType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Position of the spacecraft at the time indicated by the sibling Epoch element.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="MeanMotion" type="xs:double">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The number of revolutions per day.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="RevolutionNumber" type="xs:unsignedInt" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Represents the revolution number (Revs) at the Epoch.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TLE_Type" uci:version="003.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Two Line Element (TLE) is a standard format for conveying the orbital elements of an Earth orbiting object at a point in time. Prediction models may be used to determine past and future positions of the object based on the TLE content.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:TLE_BaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="SatelliteIdentity" type="uci:SatelliteIdentifierType">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the identity of the asset.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="Classification" type="uci:ClassificationEnum">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>The classification of the TLE.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="EphemerisType" type="xs:unsignedByte">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Represents the orbital model used to generate the data.  1=SGP, 2=SGP4, 3=SDP4, 4=SGP8, 5=SDP8, 0=SGP4/SDP4 as appropriate. Distributed element sets are typically marked 0.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TLE_WithParametersType" uci:version="002.001.001.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the default or "catalog" orbital element set (also known as two line element or TLE) for the satellite.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:TLE_BaseType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="ModelParameters" type="uci:OrbitalElementSetParametersType" minOccurs="0">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates the parameters for an orbital element set.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TraceabilityType" uci:version="002.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Tasking sources work at different levels of detail and abstraction, progressing from what to do to how specifically to do it.  Inputs from abstract tasking sources and Tasks can be decomposed into discrete, actionable Tasks.  This type provides traceability to the external tasking or Task from which this Task was derived.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Requirement" type="uci:RequirementInstanceID_ChoiceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Requirement (Effect, Action, Task, [Capability]Command or Response) which the subject traces/originates from.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="CollectionDeckTraceability" type="uci:CollectionDeckTraceabilityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a reference to an external (non-UCI) tasking source, the collection deck, which the subject traces/originates from.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ACTDF_Traceability" type="uci:ACTDF_TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a reference to an external (non-UCI) tasking source, Airborne Collection Tasking Message, the subject traces/originates from.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="EEI_ID" type="uci:EEI_ID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a reference to an external (non-UCI) tasking source, Essential Element of Information, the subject traces/originates from.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ATO_Traceability" type="uci:ATO_TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a reference to an external (non-UCI) tasking source, the Air Tasking Order, the subject traces/originates from.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="AOCO_Traceability" type="uci:AOCO_TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a reference to an external (non-UCI) tasking source, Airborne Overhead Cooperative Operations, the subject traces/originates from.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="STO_Traceability" type="uci:CS_STO_TraceabilityType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a reference to an external (non-UCI) tasking source: Space Tasking Order.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TrackingOpZoneFilterAreaType" uci:version="001.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element represents the content of a filtered area.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:OpZoneFilterAreaPET">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="InclusionData" type="uci:OpZoneTrackAreaDomainSourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates that data inside the zone should be included and used by tracker.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
					<xs:element name="ExclusionData" type="uci:OpZoneTrackAreaDomainSourceType" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>Indicates that data inside the zone should be excluded and not used by tracker.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TrackNumberOrEntityType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Choice between a Link 16 TN or UCI EntityID_Type value.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="EntityID" type="uci:EntityID_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>UUID of the referenced vehicle.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TrackNumber" type="uci:Link16TrackIdentifierType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Link 16 Track Number of the referenced vehicle. Used to reference TNs without a matching UCI object.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TrackOptionsID_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The ID type for UCI IDs that correspond to resource capabilities.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:ID_Type" />
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TransceiverType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="SkysearchMode" type="uci:SkysearchModeEnum" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the current mode for accessing a remote waveform transceiver/relay.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="SoftwareVersion" type="uci:VisibleString256Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides the version string for the Transceiver Software.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ComponentID" type="uci:ComponentID_Type" minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the unique ID of the component referenced in the SubsystemConfiguration message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TransitionStatusType" uci:version="002.000.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Transition" type="uci:ActivityTransitionEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of current/past Activity transition being statused.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TransitionTime" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The time or time window when the Activity transition occurred.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TransitionLocation" type="uci:KinematicsMultiStandardType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the location of the System when the sibling Transition occurred.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="ResultTime" type="uci:DateTimeRangeType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The time or time window when the result of the planned Activity transition occurred.  This element is intended for Activity transitions that aren't instantaneous such as Strike Tasks or OrbitChange Tasks.  For instantaneous Activities, only the sibling TransitionTime is necessary to indicate the time of the transition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TurnGeometryChoiceType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element is used to specify whether a turn is a bank angle or turn radius.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="TurnRadius" type="uci:DistanceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the radius of the turn.  When neither BankAngle nor TurnRadius are specified, indicates that the TurnPoint is in the end of a turn.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="BankAngle" type="uci:AngleHalfType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates bank angle of the turn.  When neither BankAngle nor TurnRadius are specified, indicates that the TurnPoint is in the end of a turn.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TurnPointType" uci:version="002.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This element is used to specify all cases of turns in a segment including fly-through and turn-short.  TurnPoints will generally come in groups of at least two in linked PathSegments.  All but the last in a group will include a TurnRadius.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Waypoint" type="uci:WayPointPointChoiceType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This element indicates the location and time of arrival of the end of the path segment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TurnPointType" type="uci:TurnPointTypeEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Represents the desired behavior at the associated way point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Course" type="uci:AngleType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the course at the Waypoint of this TurnPoint.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="TurnGeometry" type="uci:TurnGeometryChoiceType" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the bank angle or radius of the turn.  When Turn Geometry is not specified, indicates that the TurnPoint is in the end of a turn.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TurretCommandChoiceType" uci:version="002.001.002.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:choice>
			<xs:element name="FixedMode" type="uci:FixedPointingEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Enumeration defining the Gimbal Modes that must be explicitly commanded. Other modes can be reached by generating an appropriate command (e.g. sending a platform referenced Position command will put the turret in a body fixed mode, while sending a PointTarget will put it into a geo-referenced mode).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Position" type="uci:TurretCommandPositionType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Command to specify the look angle of the gimbal using Azimuth/Elevation and Reference Frame (INERTIAL/BODY) specifications.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="LOS_Position" type="uci:LOS_D_Type">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Command to specify the look angle of the gimbal. The option provides two choices: LOS which includes Reference Frame, Azimuth, Elevation, Roll and associated LOS Rates or LOS_Rates which allows for Azimuth, Elevation and Roll Rate settings.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Volume" type="uci:PO_AirTargetVolumeCommandType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the volume or specific Entity that defines the extents of the spatial region covered by the command. For non-cued Capabilities, one air volume instance of this element is expected. For cued Capabilities, two instances of this element are allowed: one with an Entity specified and a second with an air volume that define the extents of the cue volume around the Entity. For cued Capabilities, a single instance is allowed if it is an Entity in which case the Entity location uncertainty defines the extents of the cue volume.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Geospatial" type="uci:TargetType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the source of or explicit values for geospatial characteristics of the target of the Command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:choice>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TurretCommandMDT" uci:version="003.001.002.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Command" type="uci:TurretCommandType" maxOccurs="unbounded">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a command instance.  Multiple command instances allow a sequence of related commands to be described in a single coherent message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TurretCommandMT" uci:version="003.002.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:MessageType">
				<xs:sequence>
					<xs:element name="MessageData" type="uci:TurretCommandMDT">
						<xs:annotation>
							<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
						</xs:annotation>
					</xs:element>
				</xs:sequence>
			</xs:extension>
		</xs:complexContent>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TurretCommandPositionType" uci:version="001.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:sequence>
			<xs:element name="Azimuth" type="uci:AnglePositiveType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Heading of the turret relative to the coordinate frame specified by the Reference element.

BODY: 0=down the nose, + values are clockwise. i.e., 1.57 = looking down the right wing.

INERTIAL: 0=True North, + values are clockwise.i.e., 1.57 = looking East.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Elevation" type="uci:AngleType">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Pitch of the turret relative to the coordinate frame specified by the Reference element.

BODY: 0=straight ahead relative to vehicle waterline. Positive values are down and back. i.e., 1.57 = straight down.

INERTIAL: 0=straight ahead relative to local level in the global frame. Positive values are up.i.e., 1.57 = straight up.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
			<xs:element name="Reference" type="uci:LOS_ReferenceEnum">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Specifies if parameters are Inertial Referenced or Body Referenced.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:element>
		</xs:sequence>
	</xs:complexType>
	<xs:complexType name="TurretCommandStatusMDT" uci:version="002.000.003.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>See annotations in child elements and messages/elements that use this type for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:complexContent>
			<xs:extension base="uci:SupportCapabilityCommandStatusBaseType" />
