	<xs:simpleType name="AngleRateType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an angle rate in radians/sec (rad/s).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:double" />
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AngleType" uci:version="000.001.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates angles in radians with values with a range of [-Pi,Pi).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:double">
			<xs:minInclusive value="-3.141592653589793238462" />
			<xs:maxInclusive value="3.141592653589793238462" />
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AntennaTypeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of antenna, as in what direction it can communicate.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="OMNI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>An OMNI antenna communicates in all directions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DIRECTIONAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A DIRECTIONAL antenna must be pointed in a specific direction for the antenna to be utilized.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AO_CapabilityEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type establishes the first tier in the taxonomy of the Active Optical (AO) category of Capabilities.  For AO, the first tier is an indication of the operational purpose or supported use case.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ILLUMINATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability to illuminate a target to improve target visibility for optical sensors.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DESIGNATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability to designate a target in support of a laser guided weapon.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="TARGET_MARKING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability to mark a target with a laser spot visible to night vision goggles or other optical sensors in support of targeting coordination.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LADAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability to create LADAR images of a target.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RANGING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability to determine range to a target using a laser.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AO_MessageOutputsEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a message that is an output of the Capability.  See enumerated type annotations for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="AO_ACTIVITY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates dynamic status for the Capability will be reported via its associated Activity message.  For example, the ESM_Activity message for an ESM Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OBSERVATION_MEASUREMENT_REPORT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates results of the Capability will be reported via the ObservationMeasurementReport message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AO_PIM_CodeType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>4 digit Pulse Internal Modulation Code.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:length value="4" />
			<xs:pattern value="[0-9]{4}" />
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AO_PRF_CodeType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Joint Pub 3-09.1 defines the PRF Code to be: "...Depending on the laser equipment, either a three or four-digit code can be set. Three digit code equipment settings range from 111 to 788. Four-digit code equipment settings range from 1111 to 1788.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:minLength value="3" />
			<xs:maxLength value="4" />
			<xs:pattern value="1?[1-7][1-8]{2}" />
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ApproachConditionStatusEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Enumeration defining the condition of the flight deck.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="CV_CLASS_I">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Visual meteorological conditions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CV_CLASS_II">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Conditions varying between visual and instrument.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CV_CLASS_III">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Instrument meteorological conditions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ApproachLightingEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates which MIL-STD-6016 enumeration should be used to interpret the ApproachLighting (DFI 1873 DUI 005).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="NONE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates no approach lighting is available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LIMITED_EMERGENCY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates Limited Emergency approach lighting is available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BAR_3">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates 3-Bar approach lighting is available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FULL_NATO">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates full NATO approach lighting is available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ApprovalRequirementEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This enumerated type represents the types of approval.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="APPROVAL_REQUIRED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates approval is required by the operator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTO_APPROVE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates approval is automatically approved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTO_REJECT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates approval is automatically rejected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ApprovalResponseEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This enumerated type represents the approval response.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="APPROVED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the state is approved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REJECTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the state is rejected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ApprovalStateEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the approval state of the associated item.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="PENDING_APPROVAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated item has been created and is being assessed to determine whether or not approval is required.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="APPROVAL_REQUESTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a request to the approving authority or authorities for approval has been submitted for the associated item.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="APPROVED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated item has been approved by the approving authority or authorities or was approved automatically per ApprovalPolicy.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REJECTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated item has been rejected by the approving authority or authorities or was rejected automatically per ApprovalPolicy.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ApprovalStatusEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This enumerated type represents the status of the approval process.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="APPROVED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the request was approved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REJECTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the request was rejected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PENDING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the request is pending.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CANCELED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the request was canceled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ArcSecondsType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an angular measurement in units of arc seconds (arcsec).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:double" />
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AreaType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a non-negative area in square meters (m^2).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="uci:DoubleNonNegativeType" />
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ArresterWiresEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates which MIL-STD-6016 enumeration should be used to interpret the ArresterWires.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="NOT_AVAILABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates arrestwires are unavailable.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="TOUCHDOWN_WIRE_RIGGED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates touchdown wires are available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OVERRUN_WIRE_RIGGED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates overrun wires are available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BOTH_WIRES_RIGGED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates both touchdown and overrun wires are available.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AS_IntegratorModeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Contains the USSF Astrondynamic Standards integrator modes that are supported.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ASW">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>In the space domain ASW stands for Astrodynamics Support Workstation and is the normal mode used on CAVENet. ASW is a suite of software applications that provides the higher-accuracy satellite catalog needed for a conjunction assessment of spaceflight safety.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SPADOC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Space Defense Operations Center (SPADOC) mode is used by ASW when it is important to match a Special Perturbations (SP) propagation performed on the SPADOC system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AS_IntegratorStepModeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Represents the type of step used by the USSF Astrodynamic Standards integrator.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="TIME_INTEGRATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Integrator uses time for the integration step.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="S_INTEGRATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Integrator uses a time-regularized independent variable S in integration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTOMATIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Automatic Integration.  Integrator uses time or a time-regularized independent variable S for the integration step depending on orbit eccentricity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AS_PartialDerivativesEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>USSF Astrodynamic Standards Partial Derivatives Type.  Represents the different ways the propagator can calculate partial derivatives.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ANALYTIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Analytic values were used to calculate the partial derivatives.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAST_NUMERIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Fast numeric values were used to calculate the partial derivatives.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FULL_NUMERIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Full numeric values were used to calculate the partial derivatives.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AssessmentStatusEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This enumerated type represents the assessment state for an assessment item.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="NOT_ASSESSED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Assessment for this item has not be done.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ASSESSED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Assessment for this item was done.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ASSESSING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This assessment for this item is currently being assessed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SKIPPED_BY_OPERATOR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The assessment for this item is being skipped by operator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AssessmentSuppressionEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Specifies whether the assessment generates results including threat suppression.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="WITHOUT_SUPPRESSION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the assessment generates results without threat suppression included.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WITH_SUPPRESSION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the assessment generates results with threat suppression included.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INCLUDE_BOTH">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the assessment generates results with and without threat suppression.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AssociatedAccessAssessmentInfoEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>List of all message types that can be associated with a Kinetic Threat Warning.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ACCESS_ASSESSMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is an AccessAssessment. This would be an AccessAssessment from a different source that influenced this AccessAssessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ENTITY_NOTIFICATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is an EntityNotification. This would be an EntityNotification that is a result of or was produced with the AccessAssessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LAUNCH_OBSERVATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is a LaunchObservation. This would be a LaunchObservation associated with the object's launch.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPERATOR_NOTIFICATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is an OperatorNotification. This would be an OperatorNotification that is a result of or was produced with the AccessAssessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OP_POINT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is an OpPoint. This would be an OpPoint that was source data for the AccessAssessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ORBIT_CONJUNCTION_ASSESSMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is an OrbitConjunctionAssessment. This would be an OrbitConjunctionAssessment associated with the orbits of the object and the subject.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OBSERVATION_MEASUREMENT_REPORT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is an ObservationMeasurementReport. This would be an ObservationMeasurementReport that was source data for the AccessAssessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SIGNAL_REPORT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the associated message is an SignalReport. This would be an SignalReport that was source data for the AccessAssessment.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AtmosphereModelEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>An enumerated type to uniquely identify the types of atmospheric models that may be used in propagation.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="JACCHIA65_COESA62_ANALYTIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia 65 – COESA62 analytic atmospheric model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JACCHIA65_COESA62_TABULAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia 65 – COESA 62 tabular atmospheric model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JACCHIA70_COESA76">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia70 – COESA76 atmospheric model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JACCHIA70_DCA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia 70 DCA atmospheric model. Computes atmospheric density based on the composition of the atmosphere, which depends on the satellite's altitude as well as a divisional and seasonal variation. Valid range is 90km - 2500 km.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JACCHIA71">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia 71 atmospheric model. Computes atmospheric density based on the composition of the atmosphere, which depends on the satellite's altitude as well as a divisional and seasonal variation. Valid range is 100km - 2500 km.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JACCHIA_ROBERTS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia-Roberts atmospheric model. Similar to Jacchia71 but with some analytical methods to improve performance.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JACCHIA70_MSIS90">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia 70 – MSIS90 atmospheric model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JBH09">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Jacchia-Bowman-HASDM atmospheric model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MSIS90E">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>MSIS90E atmospheric model. Empirical density model developed by Hedin based on satellite data. Finds the total density by accounting for the contribution of N2, O, O2, He, Ar and H. 1990 version, valid range of 0-1000 km.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MSIS90E_AP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>MSIS90E AP atmospheric model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NRLMSISE_2000">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>NRL MSIS-E 2000 atmospheric model. Empirical density model developed by the US Naval Research Laboratory (NRL) based on satellite data. Finds the total density by accounting for the contribution of N2, O, O2, He, Ar and H. Includes anomalous oxygen above 500 km. 2000 version, valid range of 0-1000 km.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>An unspecified or otherwise agreed upon atmospheric model.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NONE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A value of NONE means no drag was modeled. This applies to RSOs in orbits above the effects of atmospheric drag.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AttributedURI_Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Provides the name of a resource or location.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:maxLength value="256" />
			<xs:minLength value="1" />
			<xs:pattern value="[ -~]{1,256}" />
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AutonomousActionStatusEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The state of the action for an autonomously triggered condition.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="DISALLOWED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the triggering condition for an autonomous action has occurred but the action won't be initiated because autonomy settings or other autonomy controls currently don't allow it.  Manual action by operators or changes to autonomy controls are required to resolve the triggering condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IN_PROGRESS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the triggering condition for an autonomous action has occurred and the action is in progress.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAILED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the autonomous action failed to resolve the triggering condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SUCCESSFUL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the autonomous action successfully resolved the triggering condition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DETECTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the triggering condition for an autonomous action has occurred, but no action has been taken.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="AutopilotModeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The autopilot mode and indicates the type of flight path the autopilot is following.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="HEADING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Autopilot mode where the flight path is determined by the heading, altitude and speed autopilot commands.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BANK">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Autopilot mode where the flight path is determined by the bank angle, altitude and speed autopilot commands.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CIRCLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Autopilot mode where the flight path will follow a circular maneuver centered on a designated latitude and longitude reference point.  The altitude, speed, climb rate and time are set by autopilot commands.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OVAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Autopilot mode where the flight path will follow an oval maneuver around two designated latitude and longitude reference points.  The altitude, speed, climb rate and time are set by autopilot commands.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FIGURE_EIGHT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Autopilot mode where the flight path will follow a Figure eight maneuver around two designated latitude and longitude reference points.  The altitude, speed, climb rate and time are set by autopilot commands.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BDS_AddressType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Surveillance Identifier (modern address type): lockout interactions</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:hexBinary">
			<xs:length value="2" />
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BeamPowerModeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the method or mode in which power will be applied to the beam.  See enumerated values for more details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="LINEAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the method in which power will be applied to the beam.  Linear is used for a control ERP response such as DRFM or AM techniques.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMPRESSED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the method in which power will be applied to the beam.  Compressed is used for a maximum ERP response such as Noise jamming techniques.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BeamWeightingEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the weighting function used to define the beam shape to the antenna.  See enumerated values for more details on each type of weighting function.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="UNIFORM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Uniform being more conventional. Weights are the same across all beams.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="TAYLOR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Representative of a function as an infinite sum of terms that are calculated from the values of the function's derivatives at a single point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BehavioralChangeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Behavioral changes of the threat or target pertinent to the Battle Damage Assessment (BDA).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="RF_EMISSIONS_CEASED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threat or target's RF emissions have stopped.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IR_EMISSIONS_REDUCED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threat or target's IR emissions are reduced.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MOVEMENT_CEASED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threat or target is no longer moving.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ABANDONED_BY_PERSONNEL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the threat or target was abandoned by the operating personnel.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BodyFaceEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the faces of a body.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="NORTH">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the North face of a body.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EAST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the East face of a body.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SOUTH">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the South face of a body.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the West face of a body.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ZENITH">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Zenith face of a body.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NADIR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Nadir face of a body.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BodyReferenceEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Identifier of the portion of the target for which characterization is desired.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ANY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Used for initial characterization and large change detection.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NADIR_DECK">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The part of the spacecraft that typically faces Earth.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ZENITH_SURFACE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The part of the spacecraft that typically faces directly away from Earth.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="VELOCITY_FORWARD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The part of the spacecraft that typically faces the positive velocity direction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="VELOCITY_BACKWARD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The part of the spacecraft that typically faces the negative velocity direction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CROSS_ORBIT_POSITIVE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The part of the spacecraft that typically faces normal to the orbital plane in the positive sense.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CROSS_ORBIT_NEGATIVE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The part of the spacecraft that typically faces normal to the orbital plane in the negative sense.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FEATURE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Allows specification of specific feature of the target (e.g., telescope) to be specified (via separate channels).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BrakingActionEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates which MIL-STD-6016 enumeration should be used to interpret the BrakingAction.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="POOR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates POOR breaking action in accordance with the ICAO system and STANAG 3634, for active runway (braking deceleration is significantly reduced for the wheel braking effort applied - potential for hydroplaning exists).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MEDIUM_POOR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates MEDIUM/POOR breaking action in accordance with the ICAO system and STANAG 3634, for active runway.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MEDIUM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates MEDIUM breaking action in accordance with the ICAO system and STANAG 3634, for active runway (braking deceleration is noticeably reduced for the wheel braking effort applied).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MEDIUM_GOOD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates MEDIUM/GOOD breaking action in accordance with the ICAO system and STANAG 3634, for active runway.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="GOOD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates GOOD breaking action in accordance with the ICAO system and STANAG 3634, for active runway (braking deceleration is normal for the wheel braking effort applied).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="BytePositiveType" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates 8-bit integer values greater than or equal to one with a range of [1,255].</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:unsignedByte">
			<xs:minInclusive value="1" />
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CannotComplyEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The reason why an action (Task, Command, Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated or failed.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_ATTEMPTS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the number of attempts specified in the command was reached before the action achieved the desired result.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_ENDURANCE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of insufficient endurance.  For example, fuel or battery limitations.  This is a generalization of the former INSUFFICIENT_FUEL_QUANTITY indication.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_CLASSIFICATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the classification of the action, actor, capability or associated elements is inconsistent.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_FOR_FOV_LIMIT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because it exceeds field of regard (FOR) or field of view (FOV) limitations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_GATING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of a gating constraint on the command.  For example, the target of the action didn't meet velocity, range, power, etc. gates/filters in the command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_MANEUVER_LIMIT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because maneuvering exceeds maneuver limits of the action.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_OP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of a constraint imposed by an "Op" message (OpZone, OpLine, OpRouting, etc.).  For example, a Strike Task in a NO_FIRE OpZone.  This is a generalization of the previous NO_FIRE or NO_IMAGE indications.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_OCCLUSION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of line of sight limitations due to terrain occlusion.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAPABILITY_RANGE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of a range related limitation of the associated Capability.  This is a generalization of the former INSUFFICIENT_SENSOR_RANGE indication.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAPABILITY_PERFORMANCE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that Resource Manager cannot allocate resources to the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) such that the PerformanceConstraints in PerformanceMetricSetType are met.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_RF">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of a conflict between the needed/commanded RF parameters and the RF spectrum available.  For example, the commanded RF band isn't supported by the loaded MDF of a Capability or there is an active RF_Profile that doesn't allow transmission in the commanded band.  This is a generalization of the former INVALID_RF_BAND, RF_SPECTRUM_LIMITED, RF_UNAVAILABLE and RF_PROFILE_RESTRICTION.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_ROUTE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because it isn't achievable given the currently planned route.  Alternatively, a route to achieve the action couldn't be generated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_SAFETY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of a safety related constraint.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_TARGET_ANGLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of command constraints on the angle between the actor and the target of the action.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_TIME">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because it has temporal requirements that can't be achieved or were reached before the action achieved the desired result.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSTRAINT_SYSTEM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because it was constrained for allocation to a specific System that cannot complete it.  This is a generalization of the previous INELIGIBLE_VEHICLE indication.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INFEASIBLE_ROUTE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because a route to achieve the action couldn't be generated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MISSION_EVENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily due to a general mission event (flight contingency, mission contingency, allocation change, etc.).  This is generalization of the previous MISSION_EVENT indication.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="STATE_OR_SETTINGS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of current/future state or settings of the corresponding Capability or Subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="STATE_OR_SETTINGS_CHANGE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because a change in the state or settings of the corresponding Capability or Subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SYSTEM_UNAVAILABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the associated System wasn't available at the needed time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SYSTEM_FAULT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the associated System is faulted.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SYSTEM_CONFLICT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the action results in conflict with another System's route, sensor, weapon or other plans/actions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SUBSYSTEM_UNAVAILABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the associated Subsystem wasn't available at the needed time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SUBSYSTEM_FAULT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the associated Subsystem is faulted.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAPABILITY_FAULT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the associated Capability is faulted.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAPABILITY_PRECEDENCE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the precedence of its associated Capability within the associated Subsystem wasn't high enough for the action to proceed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the associated Capability wasn't available at the needed time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of insufficient resources (e.g. signal processors, memory or other items generally subordinate to Subsystems and Capabilities).  In this condition, the associated Capability, Subsystem and System should be otherwise able to perform the action.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RANKING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because its ranking wasn't high enough to gain or maintain access to the required capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of weather effects.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INELIGIBLE_CONTROL_SOURCE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the source of the action isn't eligible and/or hasn't been granted permission to control (mission control, primary capability control, secondary capability control, automated capability management) the associated System or Capability.  This is a generalization of the former SYSTEM_NOT_IN_CONTROL and SERVICE_NOT_IN_CONTROL.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEPENDENCY_PREDECESSOR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because a required predecessor action wasn't allocated, unallocated, failed, etc.  This is a generalization of the former UNASSIGNABLE_DEPENDENT_TASK.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEPENDENCY_ALL_OR_NOTHING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because it has an "all or nothing" association with another action that wasn't allocated, unallocated, failed, etc.  This is a generalization of the former ALL_OR_NOTHING_TASK_CONSTRAINT.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEPENDENCY_EITHER_OR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because it has an "either or" association with another action that wasn't allocated, unallocated, failed, etc.  This is a generalization of the former EITHER_OR_TASK_CONSTRAINT.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INIT_CRITERIA_NOT_MET">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the initialization conditions were not met.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNKNOWN_ID">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the object corresponding to an ID in the command could not be found.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INVALID_INPUT_PARAMETER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because a parameter in the action or other associated input was invalid.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INPUT_OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of another unspecified input problem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MDF_ACTIVATION_ERROR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action to activate an MDF ([Capability]SettingsCommand was rejected because the commanded MDF_ID and/or SubCategory FileID is invalid or represents a file set that is not compliant with the Capability.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MULTIPLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of multiple sibling enumeration reasons but a specific single reason isn't known.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CANCELED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was canceled, generally by the originating source.  This is a generalization of the previous USER_CANCELED indication.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of another reason which hasn't yet been incorporated into the enumeration.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNKNOWN">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because of an unknown reason.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ABORTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was aborted due to constraints and/or priorities of the mission or system.  This is different from an action that was canceled, rejected, or failed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ALIGNMENT_MANEUVER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action (Task, [Capability]Command, [SupportingCapability]Command, [Capability]Activity, etc.) was rejected, interrupted, unallocated, failed or generally can't be completed satisfactorily because the store reports conditions which indicate that their inertial navigation system platform quality is poor and the platform should perform a maneuver to allow system to align itself.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CapabilityAvailabilityEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the availability state of the defined capability.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="AVAILABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability is available for use.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNAVAILABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability isn't available for use and future availability isn't known.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="TEMPORARILY_UNAVAILABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability isn't available for use but is expected to become available in the future.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EXPENDED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability isn't available for use because it was expended.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DISABLED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability isn't available for use because it is disabled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAULTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability isn't available for use because it has faults.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CapabilityCommandStateEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an accepted state command for the Capability.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="DISABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded capability state should be disabled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ENABLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded capability state should be enabled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RESET">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the commanded capability state should be reset.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CapabilityControlInterfacesEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates an accepted control interface for the Capability.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:annotation>
				<xs:documentation>Indicates UCI messages and other interfaces used to control a Capability.</xs:documentation>
			</xs:annotation>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTO_MDF">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability that uses non-UCI controls for initiation; a Capability automatically/self-initiates Activity according to its built-in design generally with optional tailoring from a MDF.  The Capability may use or depend on UCI data inputs to support and/or trigger initiation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CAPABILITY_COMMAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability that can be controlled by [Capability]Command messages that initiate new Activities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="TASK_COMMAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability that can be controlled by TaskCommand messages that initiate new Activities.  In the UCI standard, a subset of Capabilities map one-to-one with Task types.  For those Capabilities, a given System could choose to support a Task-based interface (TaskCommand(SAR), TaskCommand(EA), etc.) instead of or in addition to a [Capability]Command-base interface (SAR_Command, EA_Command, etc.) as indicated by the sibling CAPABILITY_COMMAND enumerate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVITY_COMMAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability that can be controlled by [Capability]Command messages that modify existing interactive Activities; indicates Activities associated with the Capability (reported in a [Capability]Activity message) can be interactively changed via a [Capability]Command message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLANNED_REQUIREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability that can be controlled by *[Requirement]Plan messages (EffectPlan, ActionPlan or TaskPlan) whose associated Requirements are directly interpreted to initiate [Requirement]Activities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLANNED_ACTIVITY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability that can be controlled by *ActivityPlan messages whose planned Activities are directly interpreted to initiate actual Activities.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONSENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability whose Activities may indicate consent is required via associated *ConsentRequest/Status messages.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CapabilityCoverageAreaBasisEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates whether this Capability Coverage Area is static or dynamic.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="STATIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DYNAMIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CapabilityCoverageAreaFactorEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates limiting factors used in computing the Capability Coverage Area.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="TERRAIN_OCCLUSION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that terrain occlusion should be considered when computing the Capability Coverage Area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OWNSHIP_ORIENTATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that ownship orientation should be considered when computing the Capability Coverage Area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OWNSHIP_MASKING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that ownship masking should be considered when computing the Capability Coverage Area. An example of this would be a jet engine which blocks a portion of the field of view.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SENSOR_DEFICIENCIES">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that sensor deficiencies should be considered when computing the Capability Coverage Area. This would include changes in field of regard due to unusable array elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RF_RESTRICTIONS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that radio frequency restrictions should be considered when computing the Capability Coverage Area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CapabilityInitiationEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the extent to which initiation of the Capability is automated, from a C2 perspective, by the Subsystem/Service which hosts it.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTO">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Capability (mode) that is initiated automatically by a Subsystem, as specified in its software/OFP and/or its Mission Data Files (MDF), without explicit commands from outside the Subsystem.  An auto Capability 1) cannot be initiated by a Capability Command message, 2) is subject to enabling, disabling and control of its settings by a [Capability]SettingsCommand message, 3) may be constrained by RF profiles, safety concerns, blanking and/or many other constraints.  Status and dynamic operation of an auto Capability is reported via a Capability Activity message.  Expected Product type and/or message type outputs of an auto Capability are specified in the Capability message.  Interactive Activity of a Capability can be modified via a Capability Command message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MANUAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Capability is initiated in response to discrete manual commands from outside the hosting Subsystem/Service (when conditions permit, based on the Subsystem/Capability design, the loaded MDF and other supporting inputs).          Indicates a Capability (mode) of a Subsystem that is initiated only when an explicit Capability Command message is received from outside the Subsystem.  A manual Capability 1) can only be initiated by a Capability Command message, 2) is subject to enabling, disabling and control of its settings by a [Capability]SettingsCommand message, 3) may be constrained by RF profiles, safety concerns, blanking and/or many other constraints.  Status and dynamic operation of a manual Capability is reported via a Capability Activity message.  Expected Product type and/or message type outputs of a manual Capability are specified in the Capability message.  Interactive Activity of a Capability can be modified via a Capability Command message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
