	<xs:simpleType name="CollectionPatternEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the pattern to be used for the collection.  It is generally applicable to non-CUED AMTI, especially when the search volume is large.  See enumerated type annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ZAMBONI_HORIZONTAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the scan follows a horizontal Zamboni pattern, where the beam sweeps horizontally across the field of view, reaches the far edge, and sweeps back the other direction below the prior sweep.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ZAMBONI_VERTICAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the scan follows a vertical Zamboni pattern, where the beam sweeps vertically across the field of view, reaches the far edge, and sweeps back the other direction below the prior sweep.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RASTER_HORIZONTAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the scan follows a horizontal raster pattern, where a narrow beam sweeps horizontally across the field of view, blanks upon reaching the far edge, returns to the other side, and commences another sweep.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RASTER_VERTICAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the scan follows a vertical raster pattern, where a narrow beam sweeps vertically across the field of view, blanks upon reaching the far edge, returns to the other side, and commences another sweep below the prior sweep.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BOXIN_HORIZONTAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a horizontal box-spiral shaped search pattern to be used for this collection.  The search box is filled from outside to inside.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BOXIN_VERTICAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a vertical box-spiral shaped search pattern to be used for this collection.  The search box is filled from outside to inside.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BOXOUT_HORIZONTAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a horizontal box-spiral shaped search pattern to be used for this collection.  The search box is filled from inside to outside.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BOXOUT_VERTICAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a vertical box-spiral shaped search pattern to be used for this collection.  The search box is filled from inside to outside.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CollectionPolicyEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type enumerates policies regarding which collection aspects should be favored for a collection Capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="COVERAGE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates coverage of the collection volume/area is more important than performance; coverage should be favored/maximized if the collection is constrained such that there is a trade-off between coverage and performance.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PERFORMANCE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates meeting performance expectations of the collection is more important than coverage of the collection volume/area; performance should be favored/maximized if the collection is constrained such that there is a trade-off between coverage and performance.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COVERAGE_AND_PERFORMANCE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates both coverage of the collection volume/area and meeting performance expectations is required in order for the collection to be useful.  If both cannot be met, the collection should not proceed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FLEXIBLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the choice of which collection aspect or aspects to favor is left to the Command recipient.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="COMINT_DwellStateEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of this specific dwell.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ENABLED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell is enabled.  An enabled dwell may transition between periods of "active" and "inactive" subject to scheduling, resource availability, priority and other constraints.  An enabled dwell won't necessarily detect a signal and/or produce data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DISABLED_CALIBRATION_FAILURE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell is disabled because it could not be properly calibrated.  Disabling due to calibration failure isn't necessarily an end state; a subsequent successful calibration can result in the dwell becoming enabled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DISABLED_ADAPTATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell is disabled because interference was detected and the dwell has been temporarily replaced by a similar dwell that adapts to the interference.  Disabling due to adaptation isn't necessarily an end state; the original dwell can be re-enabled after the interference is no longer detected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DISABLED_BY_COMMAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell was disabled by a Command.  Disabling due to command isn't necessarily an end state; the dwell can be re-enabled by a subsequent Command.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DISABLED_OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell was disabled for a reason not described by the sibling enumerates.  Disabling due to for an "other" reason isn't necessarily an end state; the dwell can be re-enabled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMPLETED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell has completed as expected; all collection functions associated with the dwell have stopped.  A dwell can complete independent of whether a signal was detected and/or data was produced.  This is an end state for a dwell.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAILED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell has failed unexpectedly.  A fault code may be reported separately.  This is an end state for a dwell.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DELETED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the dwell was deleted, for example by a Command.  This is an end state for a dwell.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="COMINT_DwellTypeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the type/purpose of a dwell.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="MDF_ACQUISITION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Original dwell provided in the MDF for acquisition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MDF_ADAPTATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>An original MDF acquisition dwell was modified/adapted due to detected interference.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MDF_SUBCATEGORY_FILE_ACQUISITION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Original dwell provided in an MDF Subcategory File for acquisition.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MDF_SUBCATEGORY_FILE_ADAPTATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>An original MDF Subcategory File acquisition dwell was modified/adapted due to detected interference.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MODULATION_MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Added dwell to accomplish a specific frequency or phase Modulation analysis to potentially resolve an emitter identification ambiguity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SCAN_MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Added dwell to accomplish a specific scan measurement to potentially resolve an emitter identification ambiguity or as requested by an operator/resource manager.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="GEOLOCATION_MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Added dwell to accomplish a specific geolocation measurement per the mission or as requested by an operator/resource manager.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SPECIFIC_EMITTER_IDENTIFICATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Added dwell to accomplish a specific emitter identification measurement to potentially resolve an emitter identification ambiguity or as requested by an operator/resource manager.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER_MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Added dwell to accomplish another measurement to potentially resolve an emitter identification ambiguity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PULSE_DATA_COLLECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Added dwell to accomplish a specific pulse data collection as requested by an operator/resource manager.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Added dwell to accomplish another task that does not fit into one of the above categories.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="COMINT_SubCapabilityEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>This type establishes the second tier in the taxonomy of the COMINT category of Capabilities.  The second tier is a list of general collection types and/or processing.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ACQUISITION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that searches for, acquires and then monitor signals from emitters.  Acquisition can be done based on basic characteristics of a signal such as frequency or the known signal characteristics of specific emitter types whose signal characteristics are described in a MDF.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DIRECTION_FINDING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that determines the direction (line of bearing) from which a signal arrives at the receiver.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EMITTER_TYPE_IDENTIFICATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that identifies the type of system emitting a signal by comparing the signal's characteristics to the signal characteristics of known emitter types described in a MDF.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SPECIFIC_EMITTER_IDENTIFICATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that identifies a specific instance of a type of system emitting a signal by comparing the signal's characteristics to the signal characteristics of known emitter type instances described in a MDF.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SINGLE_SUBSYSTEM_GEOLOCATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that determines the location of the emitter of a signal using a single Subsystem.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MULTI_SUBSYSTEM_GEOLOCATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that determines the location of the emitter of a signal using multiple Subsystems working cooperatively.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FINE_FREQUENCY_MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that measures the frequency characteristics of a signal in fine detail.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MODULATION_MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that measures the modulation of a signal in fine detail.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SCAN_MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that measures the scanning characteristics of the emitter of a signal in fine detail.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DATA_COLLECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that collects signal data at a specific, pre-coordinated time.  The resulting signal data can then be processed with signal data from other Subsystems which collected simultaneously.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NETWORK_IDENTIFICATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Identifies the communications network of a transmission.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEMODULATION_AUDIO">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that Provides demodulation of audio signals.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEMODULATION_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that provides demodulation of digital data signals.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IQ_FORWARDING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that provides I/Q data extracted from radio signals.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SPECTRAL_DENSITY_REPORTING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that provides spectral density reports/pan display data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability that provides specialized signal processing that is not described by the other enums.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CommAcquisitionModeTypeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Used to indicate whether the acquisition mode is scintillation or normal.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="NORMAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates normal acquisition mode.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SCINT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A mode used by the Comm type BLOS where acquisition flows a more robust protocol than for normal processing.  This mode changes timing and messaging for the acquisition process.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CommAllocationTransitionEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the possible values with which to transition the communication allocation.  States available for the action include ACTIVATE or DEACTIVATE.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVATE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEACTIVATE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CommandProcessingStateEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the associated command.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="RECEIVED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a [NEW] Command has been received and the Subsystem or Service is determining if it can perform the Command.  An [UPDATE] Command can be received in this state which will modify the command parameters.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ACCEPTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Subsystem or Service has accepted the Command and will subsequently status it through [Capability]Activity or other another status message.  This is a terminal state and the Subsystem or Service will ignore all subsequent updates to the Command, including CANCEL.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REJECTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Subsystem or Service has determined that it will not perform the Command.  This is a terminal state and the Subsystem or Service will ignore all subsequent updates to the Command, including CANCEL.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CANCELED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a [CANCEL] Command was been received while the Subsystem or Service could honor it and the Command was removed from consideration with no resulting Activity and/or functionality starting.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CommandStateEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates whether an instance of a message is new, an update to an existing message/object or a request/command to remove the message/object from the network.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="NEW">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the command message is new to the network.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UPDATE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that this command message is an update to a command message previously placed on the network.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CANCEL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the command should be canceled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CommAssetCategoryEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Categorizes a communication asset as able to move on its own while in use or not.  See enumerated values for more details on each category.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="STATIONARY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>STATIONARY assets do not move on their own.  It is possible for a stationary asset to relocate but doing so may change its identification.  The expectation is that the asset will not move while it is in use.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MOBILE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>MOBILE assets may move or change their location while it is in use and must be accounted for when scheduling and/or evaluating communications coverage.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CommAssetEstimationMessageEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of messages to produce in response to the communication asset's requested position estimation.  The requested estimation could be specifying a response in a PositionReport message (COMM_ASSET_POSITION_REPORT) or an Assessment message (COMM_ASSET).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="COMM_ASSET_POSITION_REPORT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMM_ASSET">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="CommCapabilityEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the first tier in the taxonomy of the Waveform Capability.  See enumeration annotation for additional details.  The enumerates aren't necessarily orthogonal.  Some enumerates indicate a band while others indicate specific communications systems operating within an enumerated band.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="FALCON">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="5G">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Fifth Generation (5G) of mobile technologies; supports high band (also called millimeter wave, or MMW), which operates between around 24 and 300 gigahertz (GHz); mid band, which operates between 1 GHz and 6 GHz; and low band, which operates below 1 GHz.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MBITR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AEHF">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Advanced Extremely High Frequency (AEHF) system operated by the United States Space Force, used to relay secure communications.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JTRS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="BOWMAN">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Bowman tactical communications system that operates in the HF/VHF/UHF frequency ranges.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="C_BAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communication in the 4-8 GHz frequency range i.e. used for satellite communications, for full-time satellite TV networks or raw satellite feeds.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CDL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Common Data Link (CDL), a secure U.S. military communications protocol that operates in the KU Band and is the primary link/protocol for imagery and signals intelligence.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CMF">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DSCS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Defense Satellite Communication System, a US Space Force satellite constellation.  DSCS is being replaced by the Wideband Global SATCOM system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EHF_SATCOM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates extremely high-frequency (EHF) bands (30-300 GHz) for broadband transmission over satellite links.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EPLRS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Enhanced Position Locating Reporting System (EPLRS) which provides secure, jam-resistant, near real-time data communications support for the five Battlefield Functional Areas of the Army Tactical Command and Control System (ATCCS).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="HAVE_QUICK">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the HAVE QUICK radio system which is a ECM resistant, frequency-hopping system used to protect military aeronautical mobile (OR) radio traffic.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="HF">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates High Frequency (HF) communications in the 3 to 30 MHz frequency range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="HNW">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communication with the Highband Networking Waveform (HNW) radio.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IFDL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Intra-Flight Data Link (IFDL).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INMARSAT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communication with the International Maritime Satellite (INMARSAT) system which provides marine vessels with reliable communications, primarily for enhancement of shipping safety.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Internet Protocol (IP) which is the set of rules governing the format of data sent via the internet or local network i.e. IPv4 or IPv6.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IRIDIUM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communication using the Iridium constellation of 66 crosslinked Low Earth Orbiting (LEO) satellites.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="KA_SATCOM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates satellite communications links operating in the 26-40 GHz frequency range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="KU_SATCOM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates satellite communications links operating in the 12-18 GHz frequency range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="L_BAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications in the 1-2 Ghz frequency range.  Global Positioning System (GPS) carriers and also satellite mobile phones operate in this range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LINK4">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Link 4 system.  Link 4 a non-secure military data link for providing vector commands to fighter aircraft.  Link4A provides digital surface-to-air, air-to-surface, and air-to-air tactical communications.  Link 4C is a fighter-to-fighter data link.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LINK11">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Link 11 system.  Link 11 is a secure military tactical data link to exchange digital data among airborne, land-based, and shipboard tactical data systems.  Link 11 is also know as TADIL-A and is compliant with MIL-STD-6011.  It will be replaced by Link 22.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LINK16">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Link 16 system including via the Joint Range Extension Application Protocol (JREAP).  Link 16 is a secure military tactical data link network.  Operates in the frequency band 960–1,215 MHz.  Link 16 is also known as TADIL-J and is compliant with MIL-STD 6016 and STANAG 5516.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LINK22">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Link 22 system.  Link 22 Is a secure digital Tactical Data Link (TDL) that operates in the HF and UHF frequency bands. It was developed to securely exchange data between all allied forces (air, ground, and sea) and replace Link 11.  Link 22 supports both LOS and BLOS (Beyond Line of sight) communication links in the HF band.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MADL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communication with the Multifunction Advanced Data Link (MADL).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MF">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates Medium Frequency (MF) communications in the 300 kilohertz (kHz) to 3 megahertz (MHz) frequency range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MILSTAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communication with the Military Strategic and Tactical Relay (MILSTAR); a constellation of military communications satellites in geosynchronous orbit.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MUOS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates communications with the Mobile User Objective System (MUOS) constellation of satellites.  Provides global narrowband connectivity to terminals, platforms, tactical operators and operations centers.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="S_BAND">
				<xs:annotation>
