		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="WHOLE_REPLACEMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Plan provided as a constraint will be wholly included in the Plan (of the same type) being created, except for added, modified or deleted Parts.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FORWARD_REPLACEMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Plan provided as a constraint will be included in the Plan (of the same type) being created from the start of the new Plan forward except for added, modified or deleted Parts.  For example, during live operations an active Plan could be half complete.  If a new Plan constrained by the active Plan is created, the new Plan would include future content of the active Plan and any additions, modifications or deletions of the new Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NO_REPLACEMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates content from a Plan provided as a constraint will not be included in the new Plan (of the same type) being created.  The constraining Plan will be left unchanged while additions will be included in the new Plan.  The two Plans can then be activated and executed concurrently.  For example, during live operations an active Plan could be half complete.  If a new Plan constrained by the active Plan is created, the new Plan would include new additions that don't conflict with the active Plan.  The active Plan would continue to be executed while the new Plan is activated and executed in parallel.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ControlInterfaceEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates categories of message sets used for System control.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="PLAN">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates *Plan messages as an interface.  A System that supports *Plan messages as an interface can take an externally created *Plan as input.  In other words, the System can potentially activate and execute a *Plan that it didn't create itself.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLAN_ACTIVATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates *PlanActivation messages as an interface.  A System that supports *PlanActivation messages can be invoked to activate an existing *Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="APPROVAL_MANAGEMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates Approval* messages as an interface.  A System that supports Approval* messages as an interface can take ApprovalPolicy, ApprovalAuthority and ApprovalRequest messages as input and perform self *Plan approval management based on them.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REQUIREMENT_CANCEL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ControlRequestEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates whether to acquire or release control.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ACQUIRE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates control is to be acquired.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
