	<xs:simpleType name="DMPI_StateEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the state of the DMPI.  This can be a rollup of the DMPI_StoreStateEnum in the sense that the store state will influence the state of the DMPI but it is not exclusively a rollup.   For example, the DMPI states of PROPOSED, UNALLOCATED, ALLOCATED, DROPPED, and CANCELED are used as part of mission management but are not related to weapon state.  A DMPI can be in the ALLOCATED state even if no weapons have been assigned to the DMPI (no weapons available on the platform).  If a single weapon fails to release or the DMPI fails for some other reason (door failed to open) the DMPI state will be FAILED.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="PROPOSED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI has been proposed to an allocation service or to be assigned to a task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNALLOCATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI is not currently allocated to a task or has been unallocated from the Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ALLOCATED_PENDING_APPROVAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI is ALLOCATED and approval is pending.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ALLOCATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI is currently allocated to a Task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CANCELED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI has been canceled.  If TaskID is given then canceled from that task only.  This is a terminal state.  A DMPI could be canceled because the mission changed to remove the DMPI or the associated task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EXECUTING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>If multiple weapons are being released, the DMPI state will be EXECUTING while the weapon states are a mix of RELEASED and ALLOCATED.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RELEASED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Weapon associated with the DMPI has been released and is in flight to DMPI location.  If multiple weapons are associated with the DMPI, then this indicates all weapons have been released.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMPLETED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the weapon associated with the DMPI has reached the DMPI location.  If multiple weapons are associated with the DMPI, then this indicates all weapons have reached the DMPI location.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DROPPED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the DMPI has been dropped by the task.  For example, dropped occurs when a mission is deactivated. The DMPI transitions to the dropped state upon deactivation of the mission plan if it was never completed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAILED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the attack/strike of the DMPI has failed.  For example, if a single weapon fails to release or the DMPI fails for some other reason (door failed to open) the DMPI state will be FAILED.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
