	<xs:simpleType name="ImageRemapEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Defines the available algorithms used to turn complex pixels into image pixels.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="GDM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>No annotation will be provided.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LINLOG">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a lin-log magnitude algorithm is used to calculate the magnitude of each image pixel. The lin-log magnitude algorithm applies linear scaling to the magnitude of the complex vector associated with that complex pixel below a chosen transition point, and applies logarithmic scaling to the magnitude of the complex vector above the transition point. This maximizes use of the pixel type's dynamic range, and minimizes pixel over- and under-saturation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
