				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PULSE_STAGGER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the pulse repetition interval of a pulse modulated signal changes at each occurrence of the main-bang or sync pulse in discrete steps.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PULSE_DOPPLER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a pulse Doppler modulation. Pulse modulated signals with a high PRF are used in precision radar applications. The radar target's velocity is determined by measuring changes in the center frequency of the echo pulse with relation to the transmitted pulse center frequency. The pulses are used to determine target range.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NOISE_JAM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an AM or FM signal modulated with noise that is used to reduce the effectiveness of signals operating in the same frequency range as the noise signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CODE_MODULATION_PULSE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates sequences of pulses used to convey information either in the form of pulse amplitude, pulse width, pulse group, or pulse position relationships. Modulation on top of the pulses using FM, AM, or phase modulation techniques may add to the information content of pulse modulation signals.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="TIME_DIVISION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates allocation of signal function in the relationship to the start time of the signal information cycle provides a division of the information transmission time that allows different information sources to share a single RF carrier.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="VENDORSPECIFIC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a vendor specific modulation not covered by existing enumerations.  In this case, the VendorSpecificModulation element of the message should be populated with a string which describes the modulation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NONE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates modulation was not detected.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNDETERMINED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates modulation was detected but could not be determined by the sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
