				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ANY_AFFECTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a desire for the new plan to match the constraining plan while indicating that any items in the constraining plan, including locked items, which are affected by changes/events in the planning baseline or battlespace can be changed in the new plan.  This enumerate overrides locks for affected items.  The exact definition of "affected" and "change" is left to particular Services and/or Systems to establish according to their requirements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ANY_UNLOCKED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a desire for the new plan to match the constraining plan while indicating that unlocked items in the constraining plan, including those unaffected by changes/events in the planning baseline and/or battlespace, can be changed in the new plan.  The exact definition of "change" is left to particular Services and/or Systems to establish according to their requirements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NONE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a desire for the new plan to match the constraining plan with minimal change even for items in the constraining plan that are affected by changes/events in the planning baseline and/or battlespace.  The exact definition of "change" is left to particular Services and/or Systems to establish according to their requirements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanConfigurationActivationCommandEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the action associated with the *PlanActivationCommand.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVATE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action to activate the associated *Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEACTIVATE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the action to deactivate the associated *Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanConfigurationStateEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the configuration state of the *PlanActivationCommand.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan has received an activation command and all triggers have been enabled but the *Plan is not yet Active.  This state is a transitional state and can be bypassed if the transition to Active is immediate.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEACTIVATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the initial state or the associated *Plan has been deactivated and is no longer active.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ACTIVE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan successfully activated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanConstraintUsageEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the relationship between the System associated with a constraining *Plan and the System whose *Plan is being or was created.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="SUPPORTED_SYSTEM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an existing *Plan of another System supported by the subject *Plan or *PlanCommand.  For example, the existing RoutePlan of another System (the supported System) can constraint Electronic Attack actions in a subject RouteActivityPlan of the supporting System.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SUPERIOR_SYSTEM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an existing *Plan of a superior System that is a constraint to the subject *Plan or *PlanCommand.  For example, a weapon can be a System that is carried and deployed by another System.  The weapon's RoutePlan can be constrained by the RoutePlan of the superior/carrying System.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SUBORDINATE_SYSTEM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an existing *Plan of a subordinate System that is a constraint to the subject *Plan or *PlanCommand.  For example, a weapon can be a subordinate System that is carried and deployed by a superior System.  The superior/carrying System's RoutePlan can be constrained by the RoutePlan of the subordinate/weapon System in use cases where the weapon release point is predetermined.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONTEXT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an existing *Plan of another System that is a constraint to the subject *Plan or *PlanCommand.  The specific relationship between the two Systems and their *Plans is determined by context.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanExecutionStateEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the command-independent states of *Plan execution.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="PENDING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan is currently pending.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EXECUTING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan is currently executing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMPLETE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan is currently complete.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SUPERCEDED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan is currently superseded.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CANCELED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan is currently canceled.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAILED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the associated *Plan is currently failed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanInitiationSourceEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of source that initiated and created a *Plan.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="PLANNER_SERVICE_AUTONOMOUS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the *Plan was created by a planning service invoked by an autonomous/automated replanning function/service.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLANNER_SERVICE_OPERATOR_INITIATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the *Plan was created by a planning service invoked by an operator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPERATOR_CREATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the *Plan was created manually by an operator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPERATOR_EDITED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the *Plan was initially created by a planning service then edited by an operator.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EXTERNAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the *Plan was created by a source considered external to the System or System of Systems.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanningDataSourceEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates category/type of source for data to use for planning.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="LIVE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates live position and status data should be used as the basis of planning for a given System.  Live position and status data is given in the "station-keeping" set of UCI messages including PositionReport/SystemOrbitalPositionReport, SystemStatus, NavigationReport, [Capability]Status and [Capability]Activity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NON_LIVE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates non-live position and status data should be used as the basis of planning for a given System.  Non-live position and status data is given in the SystemReadiness message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CONTEXT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the choice between live vs. non-live position and status data should be made based on context.  When a *PlanCommand initiates planning for a particular Mission, the planning Service should use live data (as described in the sibling LIVE enumerate) if the associated MissionDefinition message indicates the Mission is active, the given System has activated and reached the initial conditions of the existing Plan for that Mission and the given System is reporting live "station-keeping" messages.  Otherwise, non-live data (as described in the sibling NON_LIVE enumerate should be used.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanningInterfaceEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates categories of messages sets used for planning.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="PLAN_COMMAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates *PlanCommand messages as an interface.  A System that supports *PlanCommand messages as an interface can be invoked to create *Plans.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLAN_VALIDATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates *PlanValidation messages as an interface.  A System that supports *PlanValidation messages can be invoked to validate an existing *Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTOMATED_PLANNING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates various messages as a triggering interface for autonomous/automated planning.  This enumerate is a self-invoked version of the sibling PLAN_COMMAND enumerate.  There are many enumerated triggers (and associated messages) as indicated in the PlanningFunction* messages.   A System that supports automated planning as an interface supports configuration (enable/disable) of its automated planning triggers via the PlanningFunction* messages.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REQUIREMENT_MANAGEMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an interface for assignment of Requirement planning responsibility using the RequirementSet message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLAN_SCORES">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Plan Score interface.  A System that supports a Plan Score interface can be invoked to score an existing *Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLAN_METRICS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Plan Metrics interface.  A System that supports a Plan Metrics interface can be invoked to calculate metrics for an existing *Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLAN_ASSESSMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a Plan Assessment interface.  A System that supports a Plan Assessment interface can be invoked to assess an existing *Plan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanningResultEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the results of allocation planning for a Requirement.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ALLOCATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Requirement was in the list of Requirements in a *PlanCommand and was successfully allocated to a System.  For example, a Task in TaskPlanCommand (listed by TaskID and/or through a reference to a superior TaskPlan) that was successfully allocated to a candidate System.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REALLOCATED_SAME_SYSTEM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Requirement was allocated in an existing *Plan that constrained a *PlanCommand and remains allocated to the same candidate  in the new *Plans produced by the *PlanCommand.  For example, a Task that was previously allocated in a candidate's constraining plan remains in the same candidate's new TaskPlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="REALLOCATED_NEW_SYSTEM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Requirement was allocated in an existing *Plan that constrained a *PlanCommand but is allocated to a different System in the new *Plans produced by the *PlanCommand.  For example, a Task that was previously allocated in a candidate's constraining plan could be out prioritized by new Tasks and shifted to a different candidate's  TaskPlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNALLOCATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Requirement was in the list of Requirements in a *PlanCommand and was not successfully allocated to a System.  For example, a Task in TaskPlanCommand (listed by TaskID and/or through a reference to a superior TaskPlan) that was not successfully allocated.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEALLOCATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Requirement was allocated in an existing *Plan that constrained a *PlanCommand but was is no longer allocated in the new *Plans produced by the *PlanCommand.  For example, a Task that was previously allocated in a candidate's constraining plan could be out prioritized by new Tasks and no longer allocated in any candidate's  TaskPlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PLANNED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Requirement was planned in a *ActivityPlan.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PlanningStateEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
