			<xs:enumeration value="AUTOMATIC_NO_PATTERN">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Switching between groups of fixed PRIs without a clearly discernible pattern of switches.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DWELL_SWITCH">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Switching between groups of fixed PRIs with a repeatable pattern of switches.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PRI_TypeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the different top level types of Pulse Repetition Interval (PRI).</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="CW">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a continuous wave (CW) signal with no PRI characterization.  This enumeration is included in PRI_TypeEnum to avoid the potential conflict of a separate CW boolean indication independent of this type.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FIXED_PRI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a signal with fixed PRI with undetectable or small seemingly unintentional PRI deviation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JITTER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a signal with fixed PRI with detectable deviation that is seemingly random.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SWITCHING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a signal that is switching between fixed PRIs, possibly groups of fixed PRIs.  Characteristics of the switching are given by other data elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="STAGGER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a signal with a fixed sequence of different PRIs that is referred to as a "pattern" that repeats. Individual PRIs in the pattern are referred to as "levels".  Characteristics of the pattern and levels are given by other data elements.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AGILE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a signal with a sequence of different PRIs that is referred to as a "pattern" that repeats based up on a second, usually periodic function instead of a fixed sequence.   Individual PRIs in the pattern are referred to as "levels".  Characteristics of the pattern and levels are given elsewhere.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="UNKNOWN">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a signal whose PRI type is unknown or not yet determined.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PrioritizationListEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the different top-level lists this message supports.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="THREAT_TARGET_PRIORITIZATION_LIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A prioritized list of battlespace objects or areas that are prioritized by an operational or tactical planner.  For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could include, for example, an entity, a signal, a point or region.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CRITICAL_ASSET_LIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A prioritized list of battlespace objects or areas that are prioritized by the joint force commander to be defended with the resources available. Critical assets are generally specific assets of such extraordinary importance that their loss or degradation would have a significant and debilitating effect on operations or the mission. For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could typically be, for example, an entity, a system or a point.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JIPTL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Joint Integrated Prioritization Target List (JPITL) is a prioritized list of targets and associated data approved by the Joint Forces Commander or designated representative.  An approved JIPTL is the central product of the target development cycle. For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could typically be, for example, an entity or a system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JIPTL_NOMINATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A product of the target development phase is the JPITL nomination list. Targeteers determine this list during the objectives, effects, and guidance phase and analyze which targets should be struck (or otherwise affected) to accomplish them. For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could typically be, for example, an entity or a system.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="JOINT_TARGET_LIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A consolidated list of selected targets considered to have military significance in the combatant commander's area of responsibility. For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could typically be, for example, an entity, a system, a point, or area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MISSION_TARGET_LIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The list of battlespace targets that are considered to have military significance and are required for the successful completion of the mission. For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could typically be, for example, an entity, a system, a point, or area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NO_STRIKE_LIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A list of battlespace objects characterized as protected from the effects of military operations under international law or Rules of Engagement (ROE).  Attacking these may violate Law of Armed Conflict (LOAC) or ROE or interfere with friendly relations with indigenous personnel or governments.  For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could typically be, for example, an entity, a system, a point, or area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RESTRICTED_TARGET_LIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>A list of targets that have specific restrictions imposed upon them.  Actions on restricted targets are prohibited until coordinated and approved by the establishing authority.  Targets are restricted because certain types of actions against them may have negative political, cultural, or propaganda implications, or may interfere with projected friendly operations. The Restricted Target List (RTL) is nominated by elements of the joint force and approved by the JFC. Targets on this list may only be struck with JFC or higher approval. Actions taken by an opponent may remove a target from the RTL.  For planning purposes, the ListItem associated with this enumeration could typically be, for example, an entity, a system, a point, or area.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEFENDED_ASSET_LIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>The Defended Asset List (DAL) is a listing of those assets from the critical asset list prioritized by the joint force commander to be defended with the resources available. Critical assets that are reinforced with additional protection capabilities or capabilities from other combat power elements become part of the DAL. It represents what can be protected, by priority. The DAL allows commanders to apply finite protection capabilities to the most valuable assets.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ProcessingStatusEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the processing status of a request or command.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="QUEUED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates processing has been scheduled/queued.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PROCESSING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates processing is currently being performed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMPLETED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates processing has completed successfully and results have been reported.  This is a terminal state of the processing status state machine.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAILED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates processing has failed prior to completion.  This is a terminal state of the processing status state machine.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ProcessingTypeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The actual type of processing that will occur on products to produce another product.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="WCMD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Wideband Complex MASINT Data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WCID">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Wideband Complex Image Data  (Not human viewable, used as input to CCD and 2CMV).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WBID">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>(Wideband Imagery Data) is a SAR collection product that has passed through all processing steps to become a viewable image.  This would be a jpg, tif, or other viewable image file.  The product may be wrapped in a NITF file depending on the sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INVERSE_SAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Inverse synthetic aperture radar.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COHERENT_CHANGE_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a coherent change detection algorithm is applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="TWO_COLOR_MULTI_VIEW">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates processing which requires two parent products as input.  These products should be as close to spatially identical as possible.  They do need to be different temporally, such as from yesterday and today.  The usefulness of this product is to show change over time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DYNAMIC_IMAGE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a dynamic imaging algorithm is applied. Dynamic imaging automates the creation of images by zooming, panning, colorizing, and performing other image processing and color management operations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTOMATIC_TARGET_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an automatic target detection algorithm is applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUTOMATIC_TARGET_RECOGNITION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an automatic target recognition algorithm is applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="VISIBLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This enumerated item is used to identify the region of the electromagnetic spectrum that is visible to the human eye. The visible spectrum is generally assumed to fall in the range of 390 nm (770 THz) to 700 nm (430 THz).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="INFRARED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This enumerated item is used to identify the region of the electromagnetic spectrum corresponding to invisible radiant energy. The infrared spectrum is generally assumed to fall in the range from 0.8 um (short wave or near IR) up to 1000 um (long wave or far infrared).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MULTISPECTRAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This enumerated item is used to specify the region of the electromagnetic spectrum that includes both the visible and the infrared spectrum (see the VISIBLE_SPECTRUM and INFRARED_SPECTRUM enumerated items).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="HYPERSPECTRAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This enumerated item is used to specify the region of the electromagnetic spectrum that includes both the visible and the infrared spectrum that is captured as a hyperspectral image (see the VISIBLE_HYPERSPECTRAL _SPECTRUM and INFRARED_HYPERSPECTRAL _SPECTRUM enumerated items).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CLIP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a clip is taken from a longer stream.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="STILL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a still is taken from a video stream or larger still image.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IMAGE_GEOREGISTRATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an image georegistration algorithm is applied. Georegistration is the process of adjusting one drawing or image to the geographic location of a reference drawing, image, surface, or map.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IMAGE_PIXEL_GEOLOCATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an image pixel geolocation algorithm is applied. The algorithm identifies the geographic location of the chosen pixel in the reference image.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MAN_MADE_OBJECT_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Automatic Man Made Object Detection (AMMOD); processing of multiple SAR images, using image amplitude to create a new image with annotations or coloring that highlights man made objects.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MAN_MADE_OBJECT_DETECTION_3">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Provides visual indication of areas having size and edge characteristics associated with man-made objects.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AMPLITUDE_CHANGE_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Change detection using only the magnitude of the RF return.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ENHANCED_CHANGE_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Image generation that combines amplitude and phase change detection results.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MTI_ON_SAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Processing of a SAR image to create a new image with MTI related indicators/tracks/Entities overlaid.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_ON_SAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Processing to combine multiple SAR images of the same location into a new more detailed image.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MTI_TRACKS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Processing of MTI detections or an MTI stream to generate tracks/Entities over time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ROAD_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a road detection algorithm is applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OCEAN_SHIP_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an ocean ship detection algorithm is applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="THERMAL_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a thermal detection algorithm is applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CLOUD_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a cloud detection algorithm is applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ANNOTATED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates processing of an imagery Product to add human readable annotations.  This enumerate can be combined with others to indicate an automated type of processing that created the annotations.  Annotations could also be human created.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUGMENTATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an augmentation or manipulation of the product has been performed.  The manipulation can occur to the metadata or to the product itself and can represent addition, modification, enhancements, or redaction.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_AUGMENTATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an augmentation or manipulation of a Weather product to be performed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a form of processing is applied that does not appear in this list.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ProductClassificationRequestEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the desired behavior in response to the associated product classification request.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="APPLY_CLASS_LABEL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is a request for a product to be updated with a specific classification label.  In this case, the product will be labeled with the classification provided in the request or can be classified per the Product Classification Plan (if omitted from the request).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RETURN_CLASS_LABEL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This is a request to determine classification label based on the Product Classification Plan and return the classification label in the ProductClassificationRequestStatus.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ProductManagementTaskStateEnum" uci:version="000.001.000.001">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Identifies the state of a product management task.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="PROPOSED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the task has been proposed but not yet approved.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="QUEUED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the task is in the execution queue.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="EXECUTING">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the task is currently executing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="COMPLETED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the task has been completed successfully.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FAILED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the task failed to execute.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="CANCELED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the task has been canceled and will not be executed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ProductProcessingFunctionMessageOutputsEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The enumeration of all message output types of Product Processing and Product Processing Function.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="ENTITY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates results of the Product Processing Function will be reported via the Entity message.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRODUCT_METADATA_LOCATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates results of the Product Processing Function will be reported via products described by ProductMetadata and ProductLocation messages.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="ProductTypeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.002">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the product type.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="AMTI_AUXILIARY_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Auxiliary data file for an AMTI activity for use in data analysis and reprocessing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AMTI_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is  the result of an AMTI activity and contains raw target detections in a standardized format.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AMTI_WBRD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WBRD - (Wideband Raw Data) This product is created on the platform as the result of an AMTI collection task.  This is the unprocessed, raw phase history data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUDIO">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a product containing audio data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUDIO_CLIP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an audio output that is an audio file clip.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="AUDIO_STREAM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an audio output that is streamed.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DEMODULATED_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Demodulated digital data extracted from an RF Signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ESM_IQ_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the ESM data product is in the form of In-phase and Quadrature (I/Q) components decomposed from the original signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="GEOPRODUCT_ELEVATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an elevation geoproduct distinct from imagery.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="GEOPRODUCT_FEATURE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a geoproduct, typically vector or multi-dimensional.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="GEOPRODUCT_FEATURE_BORDER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a geoproduct, typically vector or multi-dimensional, with borders.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="GEOPRODUCT_FEATURE_ROADS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a geoproduct, typically vector or multi-dimensional, with roads.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="GEOPRODUCT_FEATURE_SHORELINE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a geoproduct, typically vector or multi-dimensional, with shoreline.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IMAGE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a file that is an image without specifying the collection method, wavelength, or sensor type.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IQ_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the  data product is in the form of In-phase and Quadrature (I/Q) components decomposed from the original signal.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="IQ_DATA_TIME_CORRECTED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates an I/Q data output, using corrected time.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ISAR_WBRD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WBRD (Wideband Raw Data). This product is created on the platform as the result of an ISAR collection task.  This is the unprocessed, raw phase history data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ISAR_AUXILIARY_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Auxiliary data file for an ISAR activity for use in data analysis and reprocessing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ISAR_MCPHD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Motion-Compensated Phase History Data MCPHD) - This product is created on the platform as the result of a collection task from WBRD with motion-compensation applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ISAR_WCMD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WCMD (Wideband Complex MASINT Data) - This product contains complex data generated as a result of a collection task.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ISAR_MOVIE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is created as a result of a collection task from ISAR_WBRD or ISAR_WCMD data and contains multiple image frames combined into a movie.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_IMAGE_VISIBLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical image in the visible spectrum.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_IMAGE_INFRARED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical image in the infrared spectrum.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_IMAGE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical image.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_IMAGE_HYPERSPECTRAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a hyperspectral optical image. Hyperspectral imaging involves imaging a scene in many different spectral bands, covering a wide range of wavelengths and with fine wavelength resolution.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_CLIP_VISIBLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical video clip in the visible spectrum.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_CLIP_INFRARED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical video clip in the infrared spectrum.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_CLIP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical video clip.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_CLIP_HYPERSPECTRAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a hyperspectral optical video clip. See annotation on hyperspectral imaging for details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_STREAM_VISIBLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical video stream in the visible spectrum.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_STREAM_INFRARED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical video stream in the infrared spectrum.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_STREAM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical video stream.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_VIDEO_STREAM_HYPERSPECTRAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a hyperspectral optical video stream. See annotation on hyperspectral imaging for details.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_IMAGE_GOOGLE_MAPPED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical image mapped to Google.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_IMAGE_DTD_MAPPED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical image mapped to Digital Terrain Data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_IMAGE_FOCUS_SWEEP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is an optical image taken with focus sweep techniques. Focus sweep takes multiple pictures of the same scene at different focal lengths, allowing the focus of the scene being viewed to be chosen after the image or images of the scene is taken.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OPTICAL_REPORT_CALIBRATION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a report on the optical calibration of the sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_WCMD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WCMD (Wideband Complex MASINT Data) - This is an intermediate compressed product that is derived from the WBRD product and has not had autofocus applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_WCMD_TOC">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WCMD (Wideband Complex MASINT Data) Table of Contents - This product provides a mapping of a SAR_WBID product back to SAR_WCMD products for use in chipping operations.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_WCID">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WCID (Wideband Complex Imagery Data) - This is an intermediate compressed product that is derived from the WBRD product that has potentially had autofocus applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_WBID">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WBID (Wideband Imagery Data) -This is a compressed product that is derived from the WBRD product. The result is a final viewable image.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_WBRD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WBRD - (Wideband Raw Data) This product is created on the platform as the result of a collection task.  This is the unprocessed, raw phase history data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_AUXILIARY_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Auxiliary data file for a SAR activity for use in data analysis and reprocessing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAR_MCPHD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Motion-Compensated Phase History Data (MCPHD) - This product is  created on the platform as the result of a collection task from WBRD with motion-compensation applied.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SHAPEFILE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is a product with vector data that describes points, lines and polygons that represent geospatial features such as roads, rivers or lakes.  The shapefile product type infers the Esri developed shapefile product format.  A shapefile could be static reference data or a dynamically generated output of Product processing with roads or other features identified.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_AUXILIARY_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Auxiliary data file for an SMTI activity for use in data analysis and reprocessing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_1D_HRR_PROFILE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is HRR products are designed to align with the definitions in STANAG 4607 Ed. 3. A chip representing a single Doppler bin / multiple range samples of a single entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_2D_HRR_CHIP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is chip representing multiple Doppler samples / multiple range samples of a single entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_SPARSE_HRR_CHIP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is chip with non-contiguous range / Doppler samples of a single entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_OVERSIZED_HRR_CHIP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is chip with range / Doppler that extends beyond extent of a single entity.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_HRR_FULL_RDM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is full detection space of the radar system (both range and Doppler).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_HRR_PARTIAL_RDM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is partial detection space of the radar system (both range and Doppler).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_HRR_RANGE_PULSE_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is block of pulse-range space data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_HRR_THRESHOLD_SCATTER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is scatters above a threshold for a 2-D HRR Chip.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_DETECTION">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is the result of an SMTI activity and contains raw target detections in a standardized format (e.g. STANAG 4607).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMTI_WBRD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WBRD - (Wideband Raw Data) This product is created on the platform as the result of a collection task.  This is the unprocessed, raw phase history data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="VIDEO">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates a file that contains either a video or video stream/clip without specifying the collection method, wavelength, or sensor type.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_STREAM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is streamed output of weather for overlay onto a display (e.g. ARINC 708).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_RADAR_WBRD">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is WBRD - (Wideband Raw Data) This product is created on the platform as the result of a collection task.  This is the unprocessed, raw phase history data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_RADAR_AUXILIARY_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is auxiliary data file for a weather activity for use in data analysis and reprocessing.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_RADAR_IMAGERY_BASE_REFLECTIVITY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Ground Weather Radar Imagery - Base Reflectivity (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_RADAR_IMAGERY_COMP_REFLECTIVITY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Ground Weather Radar Imagery - Composite Reflectivity (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_METAR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Aviation Routine Weather Reports (Text String).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_TAF">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Aerodrome Forecast, Weather (Text String).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_PIREP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Pilot Reports, Weather (Text String).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_AIREP">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Aircraft Reports, Weather (Text String).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_WINDS_ALOFT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Wind and Temperature Aloft Forecast Data (Text String).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_SATELLITE_IMAGERY_VISIBLE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Visible Satellite Imagery for Weather (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_SATELLITE_IMAGERY_INFRARED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Infrared Satellite Imagery for Weather (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_SATELLITE_IMAGERY_MSI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Multi-spectral Satellite Imagery for Weather (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_SATELLITE_IMAGERY_MICROWAVE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Microwave Satellite Imagery for Weather (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_SATELLITE_IMAGERY_WATERVAPOR">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Water Vapor Satellite Imagery for Weather (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_GRIB">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Gridded Binary Wind and Temperature Aloft Forecast Data (binary file).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_TABULAR_DATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Gridded Textual Wind and Temperature Aloft (UCI Format). The format of this file is the UCI weather data set message and is used when the size of a weather message is too large to be sending as a message. This file can represent current, forecast or historical weather data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_PROGNOSTIC_CHARTS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Weather Forecast Map (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_SURFACE_CHARTS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is Surface Weather depicting temps, high and low pressure areas (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_FORECAST_WIND_VELOCITY_CHART">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is graphic charts indicating Wind velocity at various altitudes (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_FORECAST_AIR_TEMPERATURE_CHART">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is graphic chart indicating air temperature at various altitudes (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_FORECAST_EAST_WIND_CHART">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is graphic chart indicating east wind speed at various altitudes (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WEATHER_FORECAST_NORTH_WIND_CHART">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is graphic chart indicating north wind speed at various altitudes (graphic image).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="OTHER">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the product is not represented by any of the existing enumerated options. Recommended for restricted use for pending change package proposals or debug purposes.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="PushContentsEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates what type of data will be pushed as a result of the dissemination plan.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="URI">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Uniform Resource Identifier (URI), or 'link' to the data product will be pushed to the planned recipients.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRODUCT_METADATA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the product metadata will be pushed to the planned recipients.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PRODUCT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates that the data product itself will be pushed to the planned recipients.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="QualityOfObsEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the quality of observations.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="HI_QUAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Used to designated position/velocity data suitable for inclusion in processes (along with other comparable data) to estimate orbits with low uncertainty.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="LO_QUAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Used to designate position/velocity for general confirmation of target presence (in a non-crowded environment) or near-term hand-off for tracking acquisition, but would not be desirable for use in processes to estimate orbits with low uncertainty.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ANY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indication that either HI_QUAL or LO_QUAL position/velocity data is acceptable for the desired purpose.  One use is when collection opportunities are sparse and, while high-quality data is preferred, any data can be put to use.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="QueryString4096Type" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>String type of 4096 characters in length. All characters are allowed for maximum compatibility with other string restrictions.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:minLength value="0" />
			<xs:maxLength value="4096" />
			<xs:pattern value="(.|&#10;|&#13;){0,4096}" />
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="R_BarApproachEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>The R-bar approach consists of the chaser approaching the target vehicle from the positive or negative radial direction of the target spacecraft. This occurs along the radial vector of the target vehicle.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="NEGATIVE_RADIAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the chaser is approaching from the negative radial direction of the target spacecraft.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="POSITIVE_RADIAL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the chaser is approaching from the positive radial direction of the target spacecraft.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="RadarAltimeterCapabilityEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the first tier in the taxonomy of the Radar Altimeter Capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="MEASUREMENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Altitude measurement.  May be Filtered or Unfiltered per the Collection Options.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RFI_CHECK">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Receive only measurement to detect RF interference.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="RadarAltimeterMessageOutputsEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates messages that are an output by the Capability as the result of capability commands. See enumerated type annotations for details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="RADAR_ALTIMETER_ACTIVITY">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This message indicates the combined in-work and to-do list of the RadarAltimeter capability of a system; it is generally a complete, coherent snapshot of all activities of the system for the entire RadarAltimeter capability category (i.e. multiple activities can reside within this message, possibly even originating from a single command or triggering event).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="RADAR_ALTIMETER_REPORT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>This message contains height AGL and vertical velocity data as observed by a system at a given location and time; it is the primary output product of the RadarAltimeter skill. It contains geographically-referenced location and characteristics of the measurement data.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="RadarAltimeterSubCapabilityEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates a SubCapability of the Radar Altimeter Capability.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="LAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the SubCapability of the Radar Altimeter subsystem will be optimized for operation over land.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SEA">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the SubCapability of the Radar Altimeter subsystem will be optimized for operation over sea.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MIXED">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the SubCapability of the Radar Altimeter subsystem will be optimized for operation over mixed land and sea.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="RadarBeamPersistenceEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the radar beam persistence.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="UNKNOWN">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the radar beam persistence is unknown.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="PERSISTENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the radar beam is persistently looking at sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="NOT_PERSISTENT">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates the radar beam is not persistently looking at sensor.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="RadarBeamTypeEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the type of region (beam) of radiation from an emitting radar.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
		<xs:restriction base="xs:string">
			<xs:enumeration value="UNKNOWN">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Indicates in beam type is unknown.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SIDE_LOBE_BEAM">
				<xs:annotation>
