					<xs:documentation>Indicates the Subsystem supports initiated/manual Calibration via the SubsystemStateCommand message.  Support of initiated Calibration via this message implies the Subsystem will change the overall Subsystem state to CALIBRATION while Calibration is in progress.  For example, if the Subsystem was in an OPERATE state then commanded to perform Calibration via the SubsystemStateCommand message, it will interrupt operational functions and capability while Calibration is in progress.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
	</xs:simpleType>
	<xs:simpleType name="SubsystemCalibrationResultEnum" uci:version="000.000.000.000">
		<xs:annotation>
			<xs:documentation>Indicates the overall status of the calibration results for the subsystem.  See enumeration annotations for further details.</xs:documentation>
		</xs:annotation>
