					<xs:documentation>Snow grains are characterized by small (less than 1mm) grains of ice.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DIAMOND_DUST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Diamond dust is characterized by a ground-level cloud composed of tiny ice crystals.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="ICE_PELLETS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Ice pellets are a form of precipitation consisting of small, translucent balls of ice, also known as sleet.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="HAIL">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Hail is characterized as solid precipitation.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMALL_HAIL_SNOW_PELLETS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Hail snow pellets are characterized as supercooled water droplets, also known as "soft hail" or "graupel".</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="MIST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Mist is characterized as tiny water droplets suspended in the atmosphere near the earths surface.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FOG">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Fog is characterized as visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals suspended in the air near the earths surface.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SMOKE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Smoke is characterized as visible suspension of carbon or other particles in the air.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="VOLCANIC_ASH">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Volcanic is characterized as fragments of rock, minerals, and volcanic glass, created during volcanic eruptions.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="WIDESPREAD_DUST">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Widespread dust is characterized as loose dirt/sand suspended in the atmosphere.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SAND">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Sand is characterized as visible suspension of sand in the atmosphere.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="HAZE">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Haze is characterized as dust, smoke, or other dry particles obscure the clarity of the sky.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DUST_SAND_WHIRLS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Sand/dust swirls are characterized as an ensemble of particles of dust or sand, sometimes accompanied by small litter, raised from the ground in the form of a whirling column of varying height with a small diameter and approximately vertical axis.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SQUALLS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Squalls are characterized as a sudden, sharp increase in wind speed lasting minutes, contrary to a wind gust lasting seconds.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="FUNNEL_CLOUDS">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Funnel-shaped cloud of condensed water droplets, associated with a rotating column of wind and extending from the base of a cloud but not reaching the surface.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="SANDSTORM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Sandstorms are characterized by strong wind blowing clouds of loose sand and dirt.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
			<xs:enumeration value="DUSTSTORM">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:documentation>Duststorms are characterized by strong wind blowing fine particles long distances.</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
			</xs:enumeration>
		</xs:restriction>
